PVD("thailand_ndp_2017-2021",{"docs":["","TH 12th Plan 2017 21 THAI"],"s":{"1":[[1,"30","1","Development Target Framework and Plan-Linkage Mechanism","Therefore, this plan has more detail on development targets and key indicators than previous plans in order to guide and link to development target-setting in secondary plans and action plans.",""],[1,"30","1","Budget and Action Plan Alignment Mechanism","Budget allocation and action plans must be closely linked to achievement of the main goals and the outputs of the work plans/projects, as well as government's key performance indicators.",""],[1,"77","4","National Committee for Sustainable Development","Thailand established the National Committee for Sustainable Development on June 9, 2015, chaired by the Prime Minister and led by the Secretary-General of the National Economic and Social Development Board as secretariat and committee.",""],[1,"77","4","SDGs Mobilization Sub-Committee","The National Committee agreed to the establishment of three sub-committees: (1) Sub-Committee for SDGs Mobilization, (2) Sub-Committee for Promotion of Understanding and Evaluation on the Implementations of Sufficiency Economy, and (3) Sub-Committee for the Database.",""],[1,"77","4","Sufficiency Economy Implementation Evaluation Sub-Committee","The National Committee agreed to the establishment of three sub-committees: (1) Sub-Committee for SDGs Mobilization, (2) Sub-Committee for Promotion of Understanding and Evaluation on the Implementations of Sufficiency Economy, and (3) Sub-Committee for the Database.",""],[1,"77","4","SDG Database Sub-Committee","The National Committee agreed to the establishment of three sub-committees: (1) Sub-Committee for SDGs Mobilization, (2) Sub-Committee for Promotion of Understanding and Evaluation on the Implementations of Sufficiency Economy, and (3) Sub-Committee for the Database.",""],[1,"77","4","National SDG Roadmap Publication","The three sub-committees are assigned to publish a roadmap on Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) that is in alignment with government policies, the 20-Year National Strategy, the Twelfth National Economic and Social Development Plan, the structural reform agenda, and the Thai Government Roadmap Phase II-III.",""]],"2":[[1,"2","3","Twelfth National Economic and Social Development Plan Implementation Framework","The National Strategy is to be translated into action through the five-year National Economic and Social Development Plans, commencing with the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"2","3","Twelfth Plan Flagship Projects","Each strategy within the Twelfth Plan lays out development agendas as well as flagship projects which need to be accomplished in order to prepare human capital, society and the economy for future challenges.",""],[1,"2","3","Twelfth Plan Implementation and M&E Procedures","Clear implementation mechanisms as well as monitoring and evaluation procedures are also identified to bring about genuine development that is effective, beneficial, and sustainable for all.",""],[1,"8","1","National Development Implementation Framework","The long-term development master plan will constitute a framework that regulates any and all aspects of development implementation, as well as linking overall and specific development plans at all levels to be properly integrated under the National Strategy.",""],[1,"8","1","Strengthened Monitoring and Evaluation System","Additionally, monitoring and evaluation processes need to be adjusted in order to regulate the linkages between strategies, budget allocation, and implementation that conforms to targeted outputs, outcomes, and impacts.",""],[1,"10","3","Twelfth Plan Implementation Mechanism","The National Economic and Social Development Plan is the mechanism that connects, oversees, and takes the development directions and goals of the 20-year National Strategy through to implementation at all levels and involving all aspects, harmoniously.",""],[1,"10","3","Pra-Cha-Rat Public-Private-Citizen Partnership Platform","Consequently, the Twelfth Plan emphasizes the \"Pra-Cha-Rat\" mechanism, which is the platform for combining the power of the public sector, private sector, and citizens.",""],[1,"11","2","Twelfth Plan Development Implementation Mechanism","the Twelfth Plan provides the development implementation mechanism by setting the development goals and directions that must be implemented in the first five years of the National Strategy",""],[1,"11","2","Flagship Program and Project Implementation Framework","they identify the flagship programs/projects which will be undertaken in the first five years of the 20-year National Strategy's implementation through sectoral plans, ministries' strategies, regional development plans, provinces' and provincial clusters' plans, and annual implementation plans of public organizations in driving forward the strategies of the Twelfth Plan",""],[1,"11","2","Sectoral Plan Implementation Continuity","the responsible organizations have indicated in their sectoral plans, or are in the process of implementation.",""],[1,"20","3","Development Strategy Monitoring and Assessment System","It is therefore important to consider the following: the seamless linkages of development strategies at all levels; an integrated and results-based budget system; continuous area-based development; investment in R&D and human development; and sets of indicators for regular monitoring and assessment of development strategies.",""],[1,"261","7","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation System for the Twelfth Plan","Participatory monitoring and evaluation of the Twelfth Plan is managed both at the ministerial level or equivalent and the provincial or area level, particularly in fields where there is an evaluation linkage between the Twelfth Plan and the National Strategy.",""],[1,"262","1","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation System","A participatory monitoring and evaluation system is one that opens up the opportunity for stakeholders to participate in the monitoring and evaluation processes.",""],[1,"262","2","Integrated Plan Evaluation System","It is an integrated evaluation system that aims to present outputs, outcomes and impacts.",""],[1,"262","3","Self-Evaluation and Independent Evaluation System","It involves self-evaluation assessment that creates a learning and monitoring process, and concurrently allows independent organizations to undertake evaluations.",""],[1,"263","3","Cross-Ministry Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establish a monitoring and evaluation system for ministryies' plans/projects and for works that are relevant to more than one ministry.",""],[1,"263","5","Monitoring and Evaluation of Sufficiency Economy-Based Plans and Projects","Monitoring and evaluating progress resulting from using the principles of the Sufficiency Economy to drive on-going plans/projects.",""],[1,"264","1","Provincial and Area-Level Monitoring and Evaluation System","Establish a monitoring and evaluation system for plans/projects at the provincial and area levels:",""],[1,"264","3","Monitoring and Evaluation of Sufficiency Economy-Based Plans and Projects","Monitor and evaluate progress resulting from using the principles of the Sufficiency Economy to drive on-going plans/projects.",""],[1,"264","5","Monitoring and Evaluation System Modernization Initiative","Create a research center, training course, and standard-checking system for monitoring and evaluation.",""],[1,"264","6","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation System","Enhance collaboration between the NESDB, the Office of the Public Sector Development Commission (OPDC), the Bureau of the Budget, and other relevant public institutions, both in central and local government.","NESDB | Office of the Public Sector Development Commission (OPDC) | Bureau of the Budget"],[1,"264","7","Central Evaluation Organization Establishment","Set up a central organization that is efficient, expert and well- accepted and able to undertake neutral evaluations.",""],[1,"265","3","Public Sector Indicator Criteria Development","Establish indicator criteria.",""],[1,"266","2","Joint KPI Management and Indicator Harmonization","Outcome Joint-KPI management by: (1) identifying development agendas of the Twelfth Plan that connect with goals and indicators under the National Strategy.",""],[1,"266","3","Ministerial-Level Output Joint KPI Framework","Activities and work stages will be identified to grasp linkages throughout the work process.",""],[1,"268","2","Monitoring and Evaluation Results Dissemination","Present monitoring and evaluation results to all involved parties, which include concerned members of the public, policy-makers, implementation agencies, funding agencies, and the general public.",""]],"3":[[1,"27","4","Good Governance and Public Administration Reform","This emphasizes the promotion of good governance aimed at tackling public administration and personnel challenges in a concrete manner.",""],[1,"27","4","Transparent and Accountable Public Administration","Transparent, effective and accountable public administration is encouraged.",""],[1,"27","4","Decentralization and Public Participation Reform","The decentralization of power, coupled with public participation and the fair distribution of responsibilities among national, regional and local actors, should also be promoted.",""],[1,"28","1","Administrative and Monitoring System Improvement","There is also a need to improve administrative and monitoring systems to become more in line with international standard, to ensure fair access to public services, and to guarantee consumer protection.",""],[1,"31","1","Public Management System Modernization and Decentralization","The public management system is efficient, up-to-date, transparent, and accountable, and also decentralized and involving popular participation.",""],[1,"31","1","Strengthened Decentralization for Local Administration","Decentralization should be pursued more effectively in order to strengthen local administration.",""],[1,"83","6","Public Administration Modernization and Integration","To improve public administration by enabling it to become more efficient, transparent, modern, and able to work in an integrated manner with various development partners.",""],[1,"85","3","Public Administration Modernization and Efficiency Reform","Public administration should be efficient, modern, transparent, accountable, decentralized, and welcome public participation.",""],[1,"85","3","Local Administrative Organization Flexibility Reform","The Local Administrative Organizations should be more flexible.",""],[1,"114","1","Transfer of Health and Education Service Delivery Functions to Local Administrative Organizations","In addition, it is important for authorities to expedite the transfer of public services provision functions, specifically health and education services, as well as strengthening the capacity of Local Administrative Organizations to be suitably prepared to carry out the transferred responsibilities effectively.",""],[1,"114","2","State-Owned Enterprise Management Restructuring","Restructuring the management of the state-owned enterprises (SOEs), including overall administration, and restoring some SOEs which are facing financial difficulties, developing operational efficiency that is in line with international standards in order to provide quality and fair public services.",""],[1,"167","1","Public Management Reform","The next five years will be a significant period for the acceleration of public management reforms in order to support the successful implementation of the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"167","1","Decentralization of Public Management Functions","Public management tasks should be decentralized, as appropriate, among central, provincial and local administrations.",""],[1,"168","10","Public Administration Restructuring and Downsizing","3.1 Restructure public organizations' and employees' roles, responsibilities and quality of human resources to become more efficient, transparent, modern, flexible, responsible, diverse and better qualified.",""],[1,"168","11","Clarification of Administrative Roles and Responsibilities","Clearly define missions and areas of authority between central, regional and local public administrations to reduce task redundancy.",""],[1,"169","2","Dissolution and Downsizing of Central Public Organizations","Establishing concepts and guidelines for the dissolution or downsizing of central public organizations, located in regional areas, leaving only those fulfilling special functions that cannot be substituted by or transferred to area-based organizations such as: regional public sector organizations, LAOs, the private sector, Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs), Social Enterprises (SEs), civil society, communities, and citizens.",""],[1,"172","2","Public Service Provider Competition and Regulation Framework","Encouraging competitiveness among public-public, public-private, civil society and community organizations in providing public services, for which rules, regulations and incentives are clearly stated.",""],[1,"179","2","Clarification of Public Administration Roles and Responsibilities","Defining clear roles and responsibilities for public administration at all levels, from central to provincial to local government.",""],[1,"179","3","Public Sector Agency Restructuring and Downsizing Reform","Revising the roles and responsibilities of each government agency, and adjusting the roles, responsibilities and organizational structure accordingly to reflect the core mission of the public sector.",""],[1,"179","4","Public Administration Legal and Regulatory Amendment","Amending laws in areas pertaining to public administration, categorizing related laws, and ensuring that ministerial regulations and other by-laws of the government agencies are in line with their changing roles and missions.",""],[1,"179","11","Public Agency Service Efficiency Improvement","Supporting public agencies to improve their service efficiency, so that they can enhance their competency needed for increasing national competitiveness and leading to excellence.",""]],"4":[[1,"167","5","Legal Process and Justice System Improvement","To improve legal processes and the justice system to be able to respond promptly and fairly to citizens' needs and demands.",""],[1,"176","6","Legal and Justice Process Reform","Reforming laws and justice processes to be up-to-date, fair and in line with international standards and agreements, in order equally to protect people's rights and liberties.",""],[1,"176","6","Rule of Law Compliance and Stakeholder Trust Building","The reforms should aim to build stakeholders' trust, recognition, and compliance with the rule of law, facilitate the implementation of government policy, promote private investment and business operations in general.",""],[1,"176","6","Efficient and Fair Law Enforcement and Judicial Proceedings","Furthermore, law enforcement should be strictly and efficiently pursued.",""],[1,"177","4","Justice Sector Institutional Reform","Reforming court organization, public prosecutors, attorneys and police agencies in an attempt to uphold justice in an efficient and transparent manner, by the following means:",""],[1,"177","6","Court Organization Restructuring and Judicial Process Improvement","Restructuring court organization, improving judicial proceedings and courts' quorum.",""],[1,"177","6","Court Expert Capacity Strengthening","Moreover, the shortage of experts in court organizations should be solved and court organizations should be strengthened.",""],[1,"177","7","Public Prosecution Constitutional Recognition and Independence Reform","Designating the public prosecution organization as one of the recognized organizations under the Constitution of the Kingdom of Thailand to act as public attorney, with full powers to conduct investigations together with the investigating officer.",""],[1,"178","1","Police Autonomy and Oversight Reform","Promoting the autonomy of organizations to be free from political interventions.",""],[1,"178","3","Judicial Arbitration Acceleration and Medium-Term Penalty Measures","Accelerating the judicial arbitration process, and introducing medium-term penalty measures.",""],[1,"181","14","Judicial and Legal System Reform Study","Conducting research in the proper reform measures to restructure the legal organizations and judicial proceedings and move toward and efficient, accurate, timely and fast system.",""],[1,"182","2","Legal Literacy and Justice System Improvement","Promoting citizens' knowledge and understanding of laws and judicial proceedings, and improving the law enforcement system to be efficient and fair.",""],[1,"182","3","National Forensic Systems Development","Developing national forensic systems to enhance standards of forensic science, to facilitate lawsuit proceedings and to protect public rights and freedoms through laws and judicial processes.",""]],"5":[[1,"7","2","Public Administration Reform","reforming public administration to be efficient, transparent, and accountable, in particular revising public administration laws and regulations.",""],[1,"7","3","Public Administration Good Governance and Anti-Corruption Reform","the Twelfth Plan highlights the need for the public administration system at every level to pursue good governance, be free from corruption, and adjust laws and regulations accordingly.",""],[1,"12","2","Strengthening Development Mechanisms","the Twelfth Plan continues to strengthen the development mechanisms to be more efficient and consistent with the current situation.",""],[1,"20","3","Economic and Social Structural Adjustment and Transformation","Critical issues are therefore economic and social structural adjustment, infrastructural investment, human development, and the transformation of values and living culture in work, learning, discipline and responsibility.",""],[1,"24","5","Equitable Public Services and Fair Competition Reform","Enhance the more equal distribution of quality public services including education, public health, infrastructure and social welfare.",""],[1,"24","5","Fair Resource Distribution and Competition Law Improvement","Also, the fair distribution of resources needs to be emphasized along with the creation of a complementary business environment, particularly by improving laws and regulations to support fair competition.",""],[1,"176","7","Legal Revision and Deregulation Initiative","Expediting ministries, departments and related agencies to revise and abrogate laws that are obsolete, unfair, unnecessary, inappropriate to the situation, not practical and sabotage people's daily life, as well as not complying with international commitments and hindering the criteria of Thailand's advancement to higher-income country, as stated in the Decree of the Appropriateness of the Law B.E. 2558.","ministries | departments and related agencies"],[1,"176","8","Regulatory Impact Assessment for Law Revision and Enactment","Applying Regulatory Impact Assessment (RIA) to analyze the necessity of law revision and law enactment before making proposals to the cabinet for consideration.",""],[1,"177","2","Public Legal Advisory Capacity Enhancement","Moreover, the capacity of the government's legal body should be enhanced in areas relating to public law, administrative prosecution, law formulation, and law interpretation.",""],[1,"177","3","RIA Support and Regulatory Quality Institutions","Developing and establishing organizations that are responsible for undertaking in-depth research and studies, so that rules, regulations and law categories are improved, developed or revised before enacting.",""],[1,"177","3","Regulatory Impact Assessment Advisory and Quality Review System","Also, the organizations should provide counseling on the RIA process to related public offices, analyze the quality of RIA reports, and set standard guidelines for the public hearing process for the proposition of any new draft act for every public office to follow, as well as provide supporting information to the public or those who are affected by the law's enactment.",""],[1,"183","5","Policy, Law, and Regulation Assessment Manuals","Developing manuals for the assessment of policy, law and regulations, as well as manuals for the development of a public participatory approach during the processes of policy, law and regulation formulation.",""],[1,"183","6","Policy and Law Reform Capacity Enhancement","Enhancing the potential of organizations in every sector to assess policy, law, rules and regulations, as well as supporting the establishment of in-house units for policy and law reform in all ministries.",""],[1,"183","8","Training on Policy, Law, and Regulation Assessment Manuals","Arranging training on the use of the manuals for policy, law and regulation assessment, and the manuals for building up participatory processes in order to promote the quality and efficiency of participation in policy and law formulation processes from all sectors.",""]],"6":[[1,"31","1","Anti-Corruption Reduction Measures","Corruption should be decreased.",""],[1,"74","4","Market Competition and Consumer Protection Regulatory Reform","Thailand prioritizes: (2) regulatory reform to support market competition, consumer protection, and ease of doing business;",""],[1,"74","4","Regulatory Impact Assessment Development","Thailand prioritizes: (3) development of Regulatory Impact Assessment (RIA);",""],[1,"85","3","Anti-Corruption and Tax Base Expansion Reform","The level of corruption should be reduced.",""],[1,"104","5","Business Environment and Competition Reform","Rules and regulations should also be improved to create fair business competition.",""],[1,"105","3","Business Environment and Competition Reform","Improve the business environment including rules and regulations toward a fair competitive environment.",""],[1,"167","1","Public Service Transparency and Accountability Improvement","The public management system should become transparent, efficient, and accountable, and the monitoring of its effectiveness should involve popular participation.",""],[1,"172","3","Public Communication and Feedback Channels","Providing various communication processes and channels to raise public awareness and understanding of the government's future activities and current performance, as well as listening to public opinions and recommendations from all sectors.",""],[1,"172","4","Public Behavior Promotion Publications","Additionally, publications to promote desirable behavior should be widely disseminated to increase acceptance of government initiatives and actions.",""],[1,"174","2","Anti-Corruption Values Promotion Movement","A movement promoting anti-corruption values should also be organized.",""],[1,"174","3","Public Integrity and Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaign","The dangerous impact of corruption, and cognizance of corruption in Thai society, should be publicized through social mechanisms, as well as the penalties for corruption and misconduct.",""],[1,"174","4","Code of Conduct Compliance and Enforcement Mechanism","Developing mechanisms and systems that support public officials and politicians to study and strictly abide by codes of conduct.",""],[1,"174","6","Corporate Governance and Integrity Promotion","Promoting good corporate governance and a culture of integrity awareness to fight against corruption, and supporting corporate social responsibility and consumer protection.",""],[1,"174","6","Integrity Pact Procurement Guidelines","Also, the private sector should systematically apply guidelines, as stated in integrity pacts, in the procurement process.",""],[1,"174","6","Inter-Agency Oversight Promotion","Furthermore, supervision by other agencies should be promoted.",""],[1,"174","8","Anti-Corruption Coordination and Civil Society Participation","Encouraging coordination among independent agencies, as stated in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Thailand, which are responsible for fighting against corruption.",""],[1,"175","2","Anti-Corruption Watchdog Networking and Whistleblower Protection","Advocating networking among anti-corruption watchdogs, and encouraging whistleblower protection systems for people from every walk of life.",""],[1,"175","3","Public Procurement and Inventory Management Reform","Reforming laws concerning government procurement and inventory management to become more transparent and efficient.",""],[1,"175","4","Anti-Corruption Fund","Establishing an anti-corruption fund",""],[1,"175","4","Corruption Witness Protection Program","and corruption witness protection program.",""],[1,"175","4","Corruption Knowledge, Monitoring, and Civil Society Prevention Support","Moreover, knowledge and understanding of corruption types and mechanisms, as well as corruption monitoring systems, should be promoted.",""],[1,"175","4","Cost-Effective Anti-Corruption Budget Allocation","Also, budget allocation for policy to fight against corruption should be cost-effective and in line with the country's fiscal position.",""],[1,"175","5","Anti-Corruption Measures and Continuous Monitoring System","Putting pressure on all government agencies to come up with measures to fight against corruption, with a continuous monitoring system.",""],[1,"175","6","Strengthening Anti-Corruption Operation Centers","Strengthening the efficiency and potential of anti-corruption operation centers in every public organization to act as the main watchdog and take mutual strategic responsibility in corruption prevention and repression.",""],[1,"175","7","Restructuring Independent Agencies and Anti-Corruption Organizations","Restructuring independent agencies and anti-corruption-related organizations by:",""],[1,"175","8","Reform of Independent Agency Commission Composition and Governance","Adjusting the composition of independent agency commissions, such as the Office of the National Anti-Corruption Commission (NACC), State Audit Commission (SAC), Office of the Public Sector Anti-Corruption Commission (PACC) and Office of the Election Commission of Thailand (OECT), to comprise representatives from various sectors.",""],[1,"176","1","Anti-Corruption Agency Merger","Promoting unity in working mechanisms among anti- corruption agencies by merging organizations that are responsible for monitoring public anti- corruption efforts, for instance, merging the Office of Public Sector Anti-Corruption Commission with the National Anti-Corruption Commission (NACC).",""],[1,"176","2","Anti-Corruption Information Integration Mechanism","Establishing mechanisms to integrate anti-corruption information and activities for systematic connectivity among public, private and international organizations.",""],[1,"176","3","Reform of Independent Agency Roles in Corruption Dispute Arbitration","Reforming the roles and responsibilities of independent agencies, as stated in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Thailand, particularly ones with public sector auditing roles - including the Office of the Election Commission of Thailand, the Office of the National Counter-Corruption Commission, and the Office of the Auditor General of Thailand - to be responsible for the arbitration of corruption disputes.",""],[1,"176","3","Assignment of Investigation Authorities to the Investigation Committee","Meanwhile, the investigation authorities should be under the purview of the Office of the Investigation Committee.",""],[1,"176","4","Increase Corruption-Related Penalties","Increasing corruption-related penalties among bribe-takers and - givers, especially government officials who are culprits in taking bribes or having conflicts of interests from their positions.",""],[1,"176","5","Social Sanctions and Media-Based Anti-Corruption Campaign","Intensifying social sanction measures that are severe enough to discourage corruption, and making use of all types of media to engage all stakeholders in fighting against corruption.",""],[1,"181","3","Customer Feedback-Based Complaint Management Improvement","Taking feedback from customers into account to improve complaint management and move toward a proactive service in line with customers' demands.",""],[1,"182","8","Corruption Risk Management and Public Procurement Integrity Reform","Checking, monitoring and setting up a risk management system to prevent risks from corruption through all processes, from analysis, assessment, monitoring and supervision, in order to reduce the risks from corruption as much as possible.",""],[1,"182","9","Public Education on Conflict of Interest and Anti-Corruption Compliance","Publicizing knowledge and educating the public on conflicts of interest between the private and public sectors, and educating the public on how to comply with the additional measures as stated in the national guidelines to fight against corruption.",""],[1,"182","10","Volunteering Networks for Corruption Surveillance","Developing volunteering networks for corruption surveillance through civil society networks and volunteers in the public and private sectors to encourage the duty of non-governmental organizations and their partners to be corruption watchdogs.",""],[1,"182","12","Public Anti-Corruption Awareness Campaigns","Advertising proactive and collaborative campaigns to raise and implant public anti-corruption awareness, and to help people to see corruption threats",""],[1,"258","4","Public Participation Channels for Development Planning","Introduce channels for public participation in the development process at both the policy and area-based levels.",""],[1,"258","4","Public Forums and Civil Society Dialogue Platform","Public forums will be provided and thereby development partners can organize activities such as civil society forums and dialogue.",""],[1,"258","4","Online Development Information Sharing Network","Online networks will be used as a platform for information sharing and activities for development.",""],[1,"260","4","Community-Led Local Planning and Implementation","Local citizens should drive plan implementation.",""],[1,"261","4","NGO Participation in Development Activities","The public sector will encourage NGOs to participate extensively in development activities.",""],[1,"268","1","Public Stakeholder Forum for Implementation Dialogue","Establish a public forum in which stakeholders are able to discuss openly and freely debate issues concerning implementation.",""]],"7":[[1,"11","1","Integrated Development Issue Implementation Framework","The Plan also determines the high-priority development issues that require integrated implementation, sets programs/projects that will effectively correspond to the development targets, and sets the targets and indicators that cover a wider range than was the case with the previous National Economic and Social Development Plans.",""],[1,"11","1","Public Sector Monitoring and Evaluation Alignment","Target-setting brings many factors into consideration, which are: congruence with the targets of the long-term 20-year National Strategy, which provides the structure for setting the minor targets and indicators which are to be exercised within the budgeting framework; and the monitoring and evaluation of the public sector in terms of its spending, performance and development which are to be consistent with and reinforce one another.",""],[1,"11","1","Spatial Development Prioritization for Manufacturing and Services","Hence, the Twelfth Plan sets the integrated development issues which provide the directions for the budget allocation, compiles and sets the key programs/projects at the implementation level, and sets the focal points for spatial development in the manufacturing and service sectors, as well as identifying the main provinces facing each development issue.",""],[1,"11","2","Integrated Budget Allocation and Public Financial Management Reform","The budget should be allocated by integrating development issues and spatial development, and setting indicators to monitor and evaluate systematically development outcomes and achievements.",""],[1,"11","2","Budget Allocation and Public Administration Reform","In the next five years, the budget allocation system, public budget management, the public administration plans, rules and regulations on financial and fiscal discipline, the monitoring and evaluation system of development strategy, and the monitoring and evaluation system of public performance will be changed radically to meet the challenge of driving towards effective implementation.",""],[1,"20","3","Infrastructure Investment Programme","Critical issues are therefore economic and social structural adjustment, infrastructural investment, human development, and the transformation of values and living culture in work, learning, discipline and responsibility.",""],[1,"20","3","Integrated Results-Based Budget System","It is therefore important to consider the following: the seamless linkages of development strategies at all levels; an integrated and results-based budget system; continuous area-based development; investment in R&D and human development; and sets of indicators for regular monitoring and assessment of development strategies.",""],[1,"20","3","Area-Based Development Approach","It is therefore important to consider the following: the seamless linkages of development strategies at all levels; an integrated and results-based budget system; continuous area-based development; investment in R&D and human development; and sets of indicators for regular monitoring and assessment of development strategies.",""],[1,"24","4","Area-Based and Integrated Budgeting Reform","Meanwhile, area-based budgeting and integrated budgets need to be promoted.",""],[1,"170","6","Public Fiscal and Monetary Monitoring and Evaluation Systems","Improve the budget process and establish public fiscal and monetary monitoring and evaluation systems to enhance the efficiency of budget allocation and spending, in order to strengthen its timeliness, equitability and contribution to the reduction of inequality.",""],[1,"170","6","Public and Private Sector Information Access Enhancement","Furthermore, information access for the public and private sectors should be enhanced, and there should be more transparency in the monitoring of operations budgets and fiscal procedures.",""],[1,"170","7","Budget Act Revision for Integrated and Area-Based Budgeting","Revising the Budget Act. B.E. 2502 (1959) to promote integrated budget allocation and area-based budgeting.",""],[1,"171","4","Annual Budget Program Prioritization and Disclosure Framework","Setting up structures and prioritizing programs, stated in an annual spending budgets, that are consistent with the 20-year National Strategy (2017-2036), the Twelfth National Economic and Social Development Plan 2017-2021, the National Security Policy 2015-2021, and government policy.",""],[1,"171","4","Annual Budget Spending Act Disclosure Requirements","Moreover, in proposing an Annual Budget Spending Act, sources of income, estimated revenues, expected outcomes and benefits from the annual budget, and consistency with the National Strategy and other development plans should all be openly stated.",""],[1,"171","5","Strengthening Monitoring and Evaluation Systems","Improving monitoring and evaluation systems in order to measure accurately development outcomes, efficiency, effectiveness, and the impact of public organizations operations and budget spending.",""],[1,"180","4","Integrated Area-Based Budget Allocation Reform","Amending the Budget Procedures Act (B.E. 2502) for the purpose of promoting integrated and area-based budget allocations and allowing provinces, provincial clusters and local administrations to act as budget allocation units, as well as encouraging public participation in budget decision making throughout the process, starting from project proposals according to community development plans, which link to provincial and local development plans.",""],[1,"180","4","Area-Based Budget Monitoring and Follow-Up","Also, area-based budget spending should be monitored and followed up.",""],[1,"229","10","Multi-Stakeholder Participation in Development Process","Encourage participation from civil society, the private sector, and local and central government in the development process.",""],[1,"250","13","Market Competition and Business Facilitation Regulatory Reform","regulatory reform to promote market competition, consumer protection, and business facilitation",""],[1,"250","13","Regulatory Impact Assessment System Development","system and process development for Regulatory Impact Assessment (RIA)",""],[1,"250","13","Services Sector Reform and Target Market Development","target market in the services sector to improve and reform the services sector",""],[1,"253","1","Integrated Planning and Budget Linkage Mechanism","the mechanisms that drive the Plan into action should be connected at different levels, linking the National Strategy, the Twelfth Plan, specific plans, operational plans, and the budget allocation system all together.",""],[1,"253","2","Integrated Budget Allocation System Improvement","The Twelfth Plan also aims to deliver an improved integrated budget allocation system.",""],[1,"253","2","Public-Private-People Cooperation Framework","The Plan also focuses on fostering cooperation between the public sector, private sector and the general population.",""],[1,"253","2","Participatory Monitoring and Evaluation System Improvement","The participatory monitoring and evaluation system will be improved to achieve an enhanced level of efficiency, and will also reflect the translation of the National Strategy and the Twelfth Plan into ministerial and provincial operational plans.",""],[1,"253","2","Harmonization of Targets and Indicators","Targets as well as output, outcome and impact indicators within those plans should be harmonized.",""],[1,"253","2","Public Agency Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening","Additionally, public agencies' capacity for monitoring and evaluation in order to fulfill the Plan's targets should be consistent, as should their overall performance levels.",""],[1,"253","2","Common Goals and Indicators Framework","This can be achieved by establishing common goals and indicators, and also coherence between targets and indicators.",""],[1,"253","2","Common Indicators for Cross-Cutting Issues","Common indicators regarding the execution of cross-cutting issues will also be identified.",""],[1,"253","3","Twelfth Plan Implementation Framework","Propelling national development by using the Twelfth Plan as the main framework for translating development objectives into action at all levels, as they relate to socio-geographic conditions.",""],[1,"254","1","Area-Function-Participation Development Planning Approach","Distributing development efforts to different areas and levels by using the Area-Function-Participation (AFP) approach.",""],[1,"254","3","Stakeholder Network and Cluster Development","Networks and clusters should be created to respond to local needs and each area's development potential.",""],[1,"254","4","Integrated Plan Implementation and Budget Alignment System","At the strategic level, the Twelfth Plan will connect national economic and social development objectives with specific action plans, and the budget allocation system will comply with integrated development, area development, and continuous development.",""],[1,"254","4","Development Monitoring and Evaluation System","The monitoring and evaluation systems will function in line with the key development issues, development objectives, and intended development outcomes.",""],[1,"254","5","Plan Communication and Stakeholder Engagement Campaign","The Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB) will create mutual understanding of the Plan's goals with all development partners through appropriate communication.","Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB)"],[1,"255","2","Strategic Issue Designation and Public Presentation","Designating significant strategic issues and presenting these to the public.",""],[1,"255","3","Strategic Investment Plan Formulation","Integrating development issues to formulate specific strategic investment plans.",""],[1,"255","3","Operational Planning and Implementation Framework","Operational plans should be precise and should cover programs, projects, budgets, partners, processes, timing and key personnel who will be responsible for implementing the Plan in an effective manner.",""],[1,"255","3","Project Management Staffing Priority","Priority should be given to the recruitment of personnel for project management.",""],[1,"255","3","Science and Technology Integration in Planning","Moreover, science and technology utilization should be applied to these plans/projects.",""],[1,"255","4","Development Investment Planning and Integrated Budget Allocation","Formulate investment plans for development by prioritizing key issues as reflected in the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"255","5","Public-Private Partnership Promotion for Mega Projects","Encourage Public-Private Partnerships (PPP) in mega- projects such as infrastructure development and logistics systems.",""],[1,"255","6","Ministerial Plan Integration of Targeted Tasks","Translate development issues into action through Ministerial Plans by integrating the main tasks that have concrete targets and indicators into the Plans.",""],[1,"255","6","Joint Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","The NESDB and involved agencies will jointly monitor and evaluate outputs and outcomes.",""],[1,"255","6","Cross-Ministerial Program and Project Integration","The integration of programs and projects both within and outside ministries should be encouraged.",""],[1,"255","7","Plan Alignment and Multi-Level Implementation Coordination","Link concepts, strategies, development issues and specific proposals under the Twelfth Plan with the National Strategy, the Reform Plan, government policies, and other plans.",""],[1,"255","7","Multi-Level Plan Implementation Framework","To execute the Plan, actions will be carried out at different levels ranging from government policies, the Government Administrative Plan, and the plans of central and local agencies, LAOs, communities and stakeholders.",""],[1,"256","2","Integration of the Twelfth Plan into Government Policies and Budgeting","Integrate high-priority development issues and specific plans under the Twelfth Plan with government policies, and present them to Parliament.",""],[1,"256","3","Regional, Urban, and Economic Area Development Strategy Formulation","The NESBD will formulate strategies concerning the development of regional, urban and economic areas by adhering to the Twelfth Plan.",""],[1,"256","3","Integrated Area-Based Development Planning Framework","These development strategies are designed to create the direction for regional and area development so that the development partners involved are able to use them as the framework for establishing their own development plans, including strategic plans and action plans, both of which should support each other.",""],[1,"256","3","Four-Year and Annual Action Plan Alignment","Ministries, departments, provinces and provincial groups will use their own development plans as the framework for formulating 4- year strategic plans and annual action plans.",""],[1,"256","3","Local Agency Mission Alignment for Development Guidelines","The development guidelines must be linked to the missions of the local agencies.",""],[1,"256","3","Integrated Project Linkage Mechanism","There is also a need to create linkages between projects in an integrated manner based on the area-function-participation principle.",""],[1,"256","4","Ministry and Department Strategy and Annual Action Planning","Ministries and departments will formulate strategies and annual action plans.",""],[1,"256","5","Provincial and Provincial Cluster Development Planning Framework","Provinces and provincial clusters will formulate a 4-year development plan and annual action plans.",""],[1,"256","6","Local Administrative Organization Development Planning","Local Administrative Organizations (LAOs) will formulate a 3- year development plan as well as annual projects.",""],[1,"257","1","Alignment of Development Plans and Annual Projects with the Twelfth Plan","development plans and annual projects that will conform to every strategy under the Twelfth Plan, especially regional, urban and economic area development strategies.",""]],"8":[[1,"170","9","Community Planning and Project Proposal Development","Formulating community plans that apply data and public participatory approaches, acquired from community brainstorming meetings.",""],[1,"170","9","Community-Responsive Project Proposal Drafting","Also, drafting project proposals that respond to community needs.",""],[1,"171","1","Tambon Community Consultation and Planning Mechanism","Arranging community brainstorming at the Tambon level, facilitated by village community committees and Tambon community organization councils, as a consulting mechanism for all levels from the village level to the Tambon level, so Tambon development plans can be formulated and proposals for budget allocations from local councils can be prepared at the Tambon level.",""],[1,"171","2","Integration of Tambon Development Plans into Planning and Budgeting","Integrating Tambon development plans cumulatively in order to comply with the principle of the participatory formulation of plans and budgets.",""],[1,"171","3","Provincial Development Plan Preparation and Integration","Developing provincial development plans that accurately and honestly declare situations and problems, and respond to people's needs.",""],[1,"173","3","Standardized Local Administrative Organization Recruitment and Appointment Reform","Standardizing recruitment and appointment processes for LAO officers, having a verification system for candidates, and developing the potential and knowledge of local executives, members of local councils and local staff in regard to understanding and realizing their roles and responsibilities as executives, politicians and practitioners of good governance.",""],[1,"173","3","Transparent Monitoring of Local Administrative Organizations","Additionally, LAOs should be openly and transparently monitored.",""],[1,"173","3","Participatory Local Development and Plan Formulation","Processes of local development and plan formulation that allow popular participation should also be emphasized.",""],[1,"173","4","Civil Society and Community Monitoring of Local Administrative Organizations","Also, civil society and communities should actively take part in monitoring the work of LAOs.",""],[1,"173","7","LAO Budget Spending Monitoring and Public Disclosure System","Effective LAO monitoring systems in budget spending should be designed, and information disclosure channels for the public's easy access should be promoted.",""],[1,"174","1","Participatory Local Budget Transparency and Public Monitoring Initiative","Promoting transparency in local budget formulation and management through participatory processes involving the people, tertiary education and local academic agencies by encouraging the public to monitor budget and procurement information, as well as project details and reference prices.",""],[1,"180","5","Amend State Administration and Provincial Cluster Laws","Amending related laws, namely the State Administration Act, B.E. 2534 (1991) and Royal Decree Integrated Province and Provincial Cluster Management, B.E. 2551 (2008).",""],[1,"257","1","Context-Sensitive Urban Development Planning","urban development should match the existing conditions and people's needs in that area, and should also be linked to the province's and district's development plans.",""],[1,"257","2","Participatory Budget Allocation Strategy","Create a budget allocation strategy that utilizes participation.",""],[1,"257","4","Budget Allocation Guidelines for Local and Provincial Development Plans","The Bureau of the Budget, NESDB and all involved agencies should work closely on the guidelines for budget allocation to support local, provincial and cluster development plans.","The Bureau of the Budget | NESDB | all involved agencies"],[1,"259","3","Provincial Development Plan Alignment and Implementation System","Use the provinces as a focal point to translate the Twelfth Plan into action, and evaluate its impact.",""],[1,"264","2","Provincial Development Agenda Coordination Platform","Create a platform to communicate with the involved agencies and to identify provinces' development agendas that link to the Twelfth Plan's development agendas and goals, and then integrate these linked issues to the National Strategy's goals.",""]],"9":[[1,"78","3","Public Sector Recruitment and Development Reform","public recruitment and development systems, as well as public administration itself, will have to adjust accordingly.",""],[1,"78","3","Public Employment Opportunity and Fairness Initiative","Opportunity and fairness in public employment, coupled with capacity development of public human resources towards leadership and the digital economy, should also be encouraged and delivered.",""],[1,"78","3","Public Human Resource Capacity Development for Leadership and Digital Economy","capacity development of public human resources towards leadership and the digital economy, should also be encouraged and delivered.",""],[1,"169","4","External Appointment of Heads for High-Priority Organizations","Allowing individuals from outside the government sector to be appointed as heads of organizations, exclusively for high-priority organizations that are significant for the country's development.",""],[1,"169","5","Merit-Based Public Sector Recruitment","Recruiting into the public sector, equally and fairly, people from the new generations with high potential and competencies.",""],[1,"169","6","Public Sector Workforce Rationalization through Information Technology","Introducing information technology to replace public manpower, together with studying the possibility of systematically employing retired employees, as appropriate to prevailing fiscal situations.",""],[1,"169","7","Civil Service Remuneration and Benefits Adjustment","Adjusting the remuneration systems and benefits for civil servants and public officers from governmental organizations, state-owned organizations, and independent public organizations, according to their job descriptions, expertise, competencies, job complexities and available market mechanisms.",""],[1,"169","8","Public Official Promotion and Transfer Reform","Establishing measures and methods for public official promotion and transfer, and considerations of remunerations and penalties, whilst ensuring that the system is fair, transparent and accountable, politically neutral, and in compliance with competency and merit systems.",""],[1,"169","9","Public Official Training for Digital Economy Operations","Training public officials at all levels to gain knowledge and abilities in compliance with the operations of a digital economy, particularly in the field of leadership building.",""],[1,"169","9","Public Executive Curriculum Improvement","Moreover, the development curricula for public executives should be improved to ensure value for money, efficiency and the highest public benefit.",""],[1,"169","9","Officer Capability Assessment and Evaluation System","Also, officers' capabilities in all aspects should be assessed and evaluated.",""],[1,"170","1","Performance Evaluation System for Senior Government Officers","Seriously establishing performance evaluation systems for government officers who hold high positions in order to assure acceptable outcomes for the public.",""],[1,"179","8","Public Executive Professional Development System Reform","Improving the overall professional development system for executives in the government agencies by assessing the programs' value for money and efficiency in developing the required skillset for the trainees in different fields.",""],[1,"179","8","Restrictions on Elite and Fundraising Networks in Public Sector Governance","Also, restricting the elements that may lead to the formulation of elite/privileged networks and networks for fund raising, which would degrade governance in the public sector.",""]],"10":[[1,"30","1","Active Citizenship and Sufficiency Economy Promotion","A good citizen is a person who is disciplined and has decent attitudes and behavior.",""],[1,"91","2","Improved Dissemination of Religious Teachings and Practices","Adjusting the way of disseminating information on religious teachings and practices, making it more comprehensive and practical, so that it can be used as one of the tools for instilling good values in Thai people.",""],[1,"91","3","Local Community Engagement in Public Interest and Social Organization","Strengthening local communities to have a greater role and engagement in organizing activities concerning the public interest and social organization, as well as determining appropriate social sanctions for those not behaving in accordance with certain social norms.",""],[1,"91","4","Creative Media and Social Networking Civic Education Initiative","Allocating air time and venues for creative media aimed at helping to promote morally ethical behavior, especially during peak airtime, as well as promoting the use of social networking services as a platform to educate Thai people about good citizenship.",""],[1,"96","7","Religious Leadership Role Model and Trust Restoration Initiative","Promoting those who disseminate religious teachings to behave as great role models by strictly following their own religious teachings and principles, as well as urgently regaining the people's trust of religious organizations.",""],[1,"96","8","Media Ethics and Conflict-Reducing News Promotion","Promoting media producers of all types to present truthful news and information which is based on media ethics, as well as emphasizing positive phenomena and trends aimed at reducing conflicts in society.",""],[1,"98","1","Community Sports, Cultural Learning, and Green Space Development","sports, (ii) cultural learning centers, and (iii) green areas or playgrounds in safe environments, as well as organizing the necessary public utilities for local communities in order to facilitate and encourage families and their children to take part in activities held within their communities;",""],[1,"159","2","Civil Awareness and Core Institutions Protection Measures","Cultivate civil awareness of nationhood and uphold the importance of nation, religion and monarchy.",""],[1,"159","3","Political Sector Checks and Balances Mechanisms","Strengthen national unity by creating checks and balance mechanisms for the political sector, promoting and enhancing the values and understanding of a society of peaceful coexistence of different opinions and political ideologies under the rights and duties of a democratic system, and truly recognizing the national interests and national security.",""],[1,"162","3","National Security Monitoring and Early Warning System","Improve the system for monitoring, surveillance, studying, analyzing and assessing the security situation and environment and changes therein; for identifying and predicting threats; and for proposing damage control measures and giving warning of any threats that may occur.",""],[1,"163","7","National Institution Protection and Public Awareness Campaign","The aim is to uphold the core institutions by creating awareness among the people of the need to cherish and retain the institutions of the nation, religion and monarchy to contribute to strengthening the unity of the people by reducing conflict",""]],"11":[[1,"127","3","Intellectual Property System Development","Developing the intellectual property (IP) system to meet international standards, with an emphasis on enhancing the efficiency of monitoring and registration systems for intellectual property, encouraging registration, and the utilization of innovations and intellectual property in order to create added value in commodities and services, along with supporting the establishment of IP central markets.",""],[1,"127","3","National Intellectual Property Database System","an IP database system should be developed so that researchers and entrepreneurs can be able to utilize expired intellectual property to further development and advance commercialization.",""],[1,"127","3","Intellectual Property Infringement Prevention and Enforcement","the prevention and elimination of IP infringements should be executed by integration and collaboration among relevant agencies in parallel with strengthening consumer awareness about purchasing and using copyrighted products.",""]],"12":[[1,"31","1","Expansion of Digital Public Services","Digital services should be widely utilized.",""],[1,"74","4","Public Sector Digital Services and Data Linkage Reform","Thailand prioritizes: (1) public sector reform to utilize systemized digital services and enhance data linkages;",""],[1,"85","3","Expansion of Digital Public Services","The use of digital services should be increased.",""],[1,"85","3","Public Sector Digital Skills Development","Public sector officers should become proficient in and highly adaptable to the technologies of the digital age.",""],[1,"104","4","Linked Public Service Management Databases","It is important that relevant databases be linked with public service management such that all agencies can benefit from the shared information.",""],[1,"113","8","Public Authority Database Sharing through E-Government System","It is important to expedite the use of database sharing among public authorities through the e-government system in order to access data on registered taxpayers",""],[1,"172","4","Online IT Management System for Public Administration","Improving organizational management by establishing an online IT management system that tracks operations and progress, provides information crucial for administration, and enables stakeholders to access and participate immediately in public activities when needed.",""],[1,"172","5","Digital Public Service Delivery Reform","Systematically modifying typical forms of public services to accommodate digital services systems.",""],[1,"172","6","Government Information Network Digital Platform Development","Developing a digital platform to support the Government Information Network (GIN).",""],[1,"172","7","Digital Disclosure of Statistical and Situation Assessment Data","Disclosing useful information such as statistical data and situation assessment data in a digital format, which can be easily accessed by both private and public stakeholders for further economic and social usage and innovation development.",""],[1,"180","9","Shared Government ICT Platform Upgrade","improving the government's shared ICT platform to be comprehensive and efficient to support digital government, such as the Government Information Network (GIN), Government Cloud (G-Cloud), and Government Common Services (G-SaaS).",""],[1,"180","12","Shared Central Data Networking Integration System","Using the shared central data networking system to integrate data from different agencies.",""],[1,"181","1","Smart Card and Registered User Account Identity Verification System","Verifying the identification and rights of each individual using the Smart Card or a registered user account through a central electronic system.",""],[1,"181","2","One-Stop Service Information Centers for Customer-Oriented Data Provision","(3) Providing data through one-stop service information centers that are customer-oriented.",""],[1,"181","4","Basic Infrastructure for Electronic Services","Providing basic infrastructure for electronic services",""],[1,"181","4","Collaborative and Proactive Public Service Delivery Plan","developing a plan to improve the quality of life for people in two aspects, including collaborative and proactive public service provision",""],[1,"181","4","Integrated Virtual Labor Market Platform","the enhancement of a labor productivity integrated virtual labor market",""],[1,"210","2","Government ICT Capacity Utilization and Service Platform Development","Accelerate the utilization of the full capacity of government ICT: including public access to government and public data, and developing the Government Service Platform and applications which will allow government agencies to access and share information.",""],[1,"224","3","Information Systems for Management Efficiency","Utilizing information systems to enhance management efficiency.",""],[1,"250","13","Public Sector Digital Services and Data Linkage Reform","public sector reform to utilize digital services and expand data linkages",""]],"13":[[1,"178","6","Judicial Efficiency and Digital Access Reform","Encouraging law enforcement systems to be efficient, fair, non- discriminatory and easily accessible by the public in a timely manner and at reasonable cost by improving investigation, inquiry and judicial proceedings against culprits.",""],[1,"178","6","Judicial Technology Platform Development","Judicial technological systems should be developed as platforms for timely and convenient access by the people.",""],[1,"178","6","Central Judicial Information Database System","Also, central information technology database systems for judicial processes, concerning both civil and criminal cases, should be developed.",""],[1,"258","3","Public Development Database Development and Maintenance","Economic, social, natural resource and environmental databases will be developed and kept up to date.",""],[1,"263","4","Cross-Agency Communication Platform for Plan Coordination","Creating a platform to communicate with the involved agencies, especially in areas where the National Strategy's development goals are linked to the Twelfth Plan's development agendas and goals.",""],[1,"268","3","Evaluation Information Management Systems Development","Develop databases and technology applications in order to optimize the evaluation process by establishing information management systems, supporting the analysis and accessibility of information, and enhancing the effectiveness of the evaluation process.",""]],"14":[[1,"37","1","Creation of New Industries and Services Using Multidisciplinary Technologies","Creation of new industries and services using multidisciplinary technologies in response to changes in demand in manufacturing, services, and in consumer behavior.",""],[1,"37","5","High-Technology Capability Development in Priority Industries","Thailand has to increase its capability in high technology, focusing on five fields: (1) food, agriculture and biotechnology industries; (2) health and medical industries;",""],[1,"38","1","Smart Devices, Robotics, and Electronic Mechanical Systems Industry Development","(3) smart devices, robotics and electronic mechanical systems industries;",""],[1,"38","1","Digital, IoT, AI, and Embedded Systems Industry Development","(4) digital, Internet of Things (IoT), Artificial Intelligence (AI), and embedded systems industries;",""],[1,"38","1","Creative, Cultural, and High-Value-Added Industry Development","(5) creative, cultural, and high-value-added industries.",""],[1,"110","11","Future-Technology Industrial Capacity Upgrade","Increasing the capacity of existing industries with regard to the technologies of the future, and laying the foundation for the development of new industries based on environmentally-friendly production.",""],[1,"119","3","High-Technology Industry Upgrading and Innovation Promotion","developing and strengthening existing competitive industries towards more high-technology-based industries by promoting the application of technology and creativity and the development of innovation, based on environmentally- friendly production.",""],[1,"121","2","Future Industries Development Initiative","Thailand should consider the establishment of new industries, or so-called \"future industries\", to meet novel and diverse global demand.",""],[1,"121","2","Manufacturing Automation Promotion","To promote this sector, the initial focus should be on encouraging automation utilization within the manufacturing sector, which will increase local demand and, at the same time, create design capability for robotics and automation systems as a further stage of development;",""],[1,"121","2","Medical Device and Equipment Industry Development","In parallel, R&D capabilities for advanced medical devices and equipment should be strengthened;",""],[1,"121","2","Bio-energy Industry Development","and (4) the bio-energy industry, to underpin national energy security and utilization efficiency, and to add value in agriculture and the production of bio-based raw materials.",""],[1,"122","2","Physical Technological Infrastructure Investment","placing a high priority on investments in physical technological infrastructure and mananagment",""],[1,"122","2","Incubation System Establishment","the establishment of an incubation system",""],[1,"122","2","Technology Transfer to Local Firms","technology transfer systems to local firms",""],[1,"122","2","Testing Centres for Targeted Industries","the setting up of important testing centres for the targeted industries",""],[1,"122","3","Strategic Studies for Future Industry Technology Policy","At the beginning, it will be necessary to have comprehensive studies to support policy makers in deciding a proper strategy to \"make or buy\" technology for the country's future industries, especially for industries that have low technological competence.",""],[1,"122","3","Technology Capability Upgrading Support for Local SMEs","Simulteneously, the policy should encourage technology-owning firms to help upgrade local Thai SMEs' technological capabilities through various strategic incentive measures, e.g. promoting co-investment on R&D and human resource development between technology-owning firms and local SMEs, facilitating the process of bringing in foreign experts in targeted technologies, etc.",""],[1,"133","4","Manufacturing Automation Support Project","This project aims to increase productivity of the manufacturing sector by encouraging and supporting the application of automation systems, such as machinery for the automotive and auto-parts industry and the electronics & electrical industry.",""],[1,"133","6","Food Processing Innovation Hub Project","This project aims to promote Thailand to become the Asian hub of food processing innovation.",""],[1,"133","8","Food InnoPolis Innovation Area Development Project","The project will establish an innovation area that is well- equipped with sound infrastructure and human resources in fields related to food science, technology and innovation through a collaborative effort among academic institutions, research institutions, and the private sector.",""],[1,"133","8","Food InnoPolis Investment Incentive Package","Nonetheless, innovation-based businesses will also be able to enjoy benefits from attractive investment privilege and incentive packages for their operation in Food InnoPolis areas.",""],[1,"134","2","Support for Service Sector Sub-Industries","Endorsing and supporting those sub-services, therefore, is essential for all related businesses and entrepreneurs to develop competitiveness skills in dynamic scenarios which will enhance their potential to expand into new markets and partnerships.",""],[1,"227","12","Industrial Production Process Improvement and High-Technology Industry Development","Encourage the industrial sector to improve the production process while supporting high-technology industry development to minimize",""],[1,"228","3","Cluster Development Incentive and Facilitation Programme","Encourage cluster development of related industries to minimize waste by providing investment incentives, efficient facilitation from government agencies, proper urban planning and implementation.",""]],"16":[[1,"6","1","Production and Service Sector Upgrading","with the targeted improvements in the production and service sectors, and with technological changes.",""],[1,"7","2","Environmentally Friendly and Inclusive Development","This development will be environmental-friendly, comply with SDGs, create and expand new and more inclusive income bases, as well as extend the existing income bases.",""],[1,"21","1","Innovation-Led Value Addition and Productivity Enhancement","The focus will be on using creativity and innovation development to create economic value-added in the production process, in product design and in services.",""],[1,"21","1","High-Tech and Innovative Product Prioritization","In order to achieve this, high-tech products, and/or innovative products and services - both local and high-end - which affect the quality of life and people's well-being should be prioritized.",""],[1,"21","1","Workforce Reallocation to Higher Value-Added Activities","For example: relocating personnel from the production line to other positions which yield higher value-added contributions to the value chain, such as in the process of product development and product design, R&D, creativity and innovation, and other activities including marketing, logistics, and branding.",""],[1,"26","1","Entrepreneurship Society Promotion","an entrepreneurship society where start-ups and social enterprises can flourish shall be promoted",""],[1,"26","2","Sports Industry Value-Added Development Strategy","The strategy will also prioritize the creation of economic added value in all dimensions of the sports industry.",""],[1,"126","2","Entrepreneurship and Smart SME Development Support","Promoting SMEs by: (1) encouraging new entrepreneurs with the requisite entrepreneurial spirit and business skills to adopt technology and innovation into production, management and trade, or to be smart SMEs and strengthen communities to move toward self-sufficiency by supporting the establishment of community enterprise based on the readiness and potential of each area for development.",""],[1,"126","2","Entrepreneurial Skills Curriculum Development","In addition, a curriculum related to entrepreneurial skills should be created and improved both at university level and vocational level so entrepreneurs are able to understand how to start or run a business, and are also aware of green business trends, with an emphasis on an educational environment that enables the learning process and stimulates entrepreneurial spirit;",""],[1,"126","2","SME Business Environment and Support Mechanism","With regard to SMEs, supporting business registration and developing support mechanisms should be established in parallel with creating potentiality by focusing on the participation of all segments of the private and public sectors in order to enhance growth and competitiveness;",""],[1,"126","2","SME Cluster Development and Supply Chain Linkages","promoting SMEs aggregation to form SME clusters, and linking SMEs with large enterprises or companies throughout the supply chain.",""],[1,"136","15","Commodity Processing, Branding, and Packaging Development","Extending the potential of commodity processing services, developing brands and packaging to gain recognition in international markets,",""],[1,"137","5","Entrepreneur Technology and Innovation Upgrading","Encouraging entrepreneurs to make use of technology and innovation in order to enhance production and management efficiency.",""]],"17":[[1,"24","6","Community Entrepreneurship Promotion","This will be done by promoting community-level entrepreneurship, supporting community skill-training centers to upgrade the skills of members,",""],[1,"27","1","Grassroots Economic Development Expansion","It is hoped to expand grassroots economic development to cover a larger number of communities across the country.",""],[1,"27","1","Entrepreneurship Enabling Environment Promotion","It is essential to create economic opportunities for various groups in society together with promoting an environment within which entrepreneurs can succeed.",""],[1,"29","2","SME Business Skills and Cross-Border Cooperation Support","enhancing Thai entrepreneurs' business skills, especially within SMEs, to increase business cooperation with neighboring countries",""],[1,"29","2","Business Environment Improvement and Business Council Support","improving the business environment and supporting the work of business councils under various cooperation frameworks",""],[1,"29","2","Entrepreneur Financing and Foreign Production Base Knowledge Support","providing Thai entrepreneurs with financial capital and in-depth knowledge regarding foreign production bases",""],[1,"30","1","SME Innovation and Digital Technology Support","The Thai economy should have strong SMEs that utilize innovation and digital technology in order to create quality goods and services.",""],[1,"75","2","MSME and Vulnerable Group Empowerment Programs","programs that strengthen MSMEs and the vulnerable populations, especially competitiveness and opportunity enhancement for MSMEs, and women's and the elderly's empowerment",""],[1,"84","6","Entrepreneurship and Social Entrepreneurship Promotion","Thailand should foster a new generation of entrepreneurs and social entrepreneurship.",""],[1,"84","6","SME Innovation and Technology Upgrading Support","Small and medium enterprises (SMEs) with high potential should improve their products and services through innovation and technology.",""],[1,"102","1","SME and Social Enterprise Support","Examples of assistance include support for SMEs, community- and social enterprises, development of microfinance and of financial access for job-creation, and promotion of access to high-quality inputs at fair prices",""],[1,"105","7","Community-Level Entrepreneurship Promotion","Strengthen community economies by promoting community-level entrepreneurship, supporting community training centers and connecting industrial clusters with community economies.",""],[1,"108","7","Private Sector and Social Enterprise Cooperation Promotion","The plan intends to promote cooperation between the private sector and social enterprises (community enterprises) and between social enterprises (community enterprises) across areas and across types.",""],[1,"108","7","Community Economy Promotion and Scaling of Community Business Models","The plan also includes promotion of community economies and coordinating with provincial and local administration in scaling-up successful community business models to other communities.",""],[1,"109","2","SME Competitiveness Enhancement Programme","Moreover, the strategy focuses on the use of biological resources; the support of value chain linkages; the development of new economic zones and corridors; the integration of the service sector and the trade sector, coupled with preparing the service sector to underpin freer competition; the enhancement of SME competitiveness; and the establishment of a culture for entrepreneurs to produce and sell by responding to rapid",""]],"18":[[1,"28","1","Downstream Industry Development Initiative","Additional strategy guidelines include development in downstream industries to bring about new economic opportunities, and promotion of entrepreneurs in the logistics sector to invest abroad.",""],[1,"84","6","Value-Added Upgrading of Existing Production and Service Bases","Existing production and service bases should generate higher value-added.",""],[1,"84","6","Logistics, Energy, and Research and Development Investment Support","The driving factors for this growth should include logistics, energy and investment in research and development programs which support the expansion of the manufacturing and service sectors.",""],[1,"109","1","Real Economy Sector Strengthening","In addition, the strategy also focuses on strengthening the sectors of the real economy, including agriculture, manufacturing and services as both conventional income sources and the means of diversifying to new production and service activities in the future.",""],[1,"109","2","Value Chain Linkage Support Programme","Moreover, the strategy focuses on the use of biological resources; the support of value chain linkages; the development of new economic zones and corridors; the integration of the service sector and the trade sector, coupled with preparing the service sector to underpin freer competition; the enhancement of SME competitiveness; and the establishment of a culture for entrepreneurs to produce and sell by responding to rapid",""],[1,"109","2","Service and Trade Sector Integration Reform","Moreover, the strategy focuses on the use of biological resources; the support of value chain linkages; the development of new economic zones and corridors; the integration of the service sector and the trade sector, coupled with preparing the service sector to underpin freer competition; the enhancement of SME competitiveness; and the establishment of a culture for entrepreneurs to produce and sell by responding to rapid",""],[1,"110","12","Services Sector Capacity Expansion","Increasing the capacity of existing services, and creating new services, in order to drive towards a more prominent services-based economy, as well as promoting a balanced and sustainable growth of tourism.",""],[1,"120","2","Industrial Technology Upgrading and Workforce Skills Development","Upgrading the capability of the important existing income-generating industries of Thailand to be able to shift towards more advanced technology production, which meets the diverse needs of consumers.",""],[1,"120","2","Automation, R&D, and Value-Added Manufacturing Promotion","the promotion of the application of automation in the production process, and a boost of R&D, creativity, and local wisdom utilization are key to increasing productivity and creating higher value-added products within the manufacturing sector.",""],[1,"120","2","Academic-Industrial Cooperation Platform for Industrial Innovation","one major development focus is on building up an environment conducive to knowledge-focused and innovation-driven production by establishing an efficient platform for cooperation linakges between the academic and industrial sectors in order to develop high quality human resources for industry, and support R&D for advanced industrial technology upgrading.",""]],"19":[[1,"84","6","Investment in Knowledge-Based Localized and Environmentally Friendly Production","There should also be investment in knowledge-based production and services, which is both localized and environmentally friendly.",""]],"20":[[1,"120","4","Regional Investment Distribution and Investment Facilitation Reform","Promoting the distribution of investments to every region in the country, and in other ASEAN countries, in order to build a platform for strong regional value chain linkages within ASEAN, and to increase opportunities for Thai entrepreneurs, especially in SMEs, to insert into global value chains.",""],[1,"120","4","Investment Rules and Regulations Renewal","Rules and regulations need to be renewed to facilitate Thai enterprises to invest in targeted economic areas and utilize investment privileges for acquiring labor and raw materials, and for accessing potential markets.",""],[1,"120","4","Targeted Area Infrastructure and Utilities Development","Moreover, the development of infrastructure and other utilities in the targeted areas must support business investments.",""],[1,"137","17","Inward and Outward Investment Promotion Measures","Setting measures for promoting inward investment in accordance with the potential of areas, and promoting outward direct investment of Thai investors by reducing obstacles to the mobility of skilled and unskilled labor.",""],[1,"213","1","Border Economic Zone Development","In addition, Thailand also has the opportunity to develop new economic zones within the border areas to enhance cross-border trade, investment, and connectivity as a member of the ASEAN Economic Community.",""],[1,"223","5","Pilot Special Economic Area Development","Developing three pilot districts, namely Betong, Nong chik, and Sungai Kolok, as specific economic area and then expanding to the surrounding areas by offering privileges on tariff and non-tariff incentives at a higher level than in other areas.",""],[1,"223","6","Approval Process Efficiency Improvement","Improving the efficiency of the approval process to be in line with international standards.",""],[1,"228","14","Border Special Economic Zone Development","ten high-potential border areas (Tak, Sakaeo, Songkhla, Nongkhai, Nakorn Phanom, Mukdahan, Trat, Kanchanaburi, Chiang Rai, and Narathiwat) will be developed to be new economic gateways connecting Thailand with neighboring countries and which aim for sustainable and tangible development.",""],[1,"229","1","Tax and Non-Tax Investment Incentive Scheme","Create appropriate tax and non-tax incentives for both domestic and international investors.",""],[1,"229","2","One-Stop Service Center Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capacity of the One-Stop-Service-Center to be able to carry out authorizing activities in licensing, approval-granting, and decision-making regarding usage of land and target activities in each area.",""],[1,"230","8","Border Special Economic Zone Integrated Budget Plan","Special Economic Zone Integrated Budget Plan",""],[1,"230","8","Border Special Economic Zone Infrastructure and Customs Checkpoint Development Plan","Infrastructure and Customs Checkpoint Development Plan",""],[1,"230","8","Border Special Economic Zone Industrial Estate Development Plan","Industrial Estate Development Plan",""],[1,"230","8","Border Special Economic Zone Labor Management Plan","Labor Management Plan",""],[1,"236","5","Special Economic Zone Industrial Estate Development Projects","Special Economic Zone Industrial Estate Development Projects in Sakaeo, Tak, Songkhla, and Nong Khai.",""],[1,"240","1","Strategic Economic Area Investment Promotion","government will lead investment in strategically important initiatives in economic areas, and stimulate private investment to achieve concrete results.",""],[1,"242","2","Regulatory Reform and Special Economic Zone Development","Including removing regulations that impede and obstruct trade/investment, and pushing forward special economic zone development to create a conducive business environment that promotes trade and investment, and allows Thailand to become a regional services hub.",""],[1,"246","4","Dawei and Thai Special Economic Zone Development","To develop Dawei Special Economic Zone, and Thailand's Special Economic Zones (SEZs) to link economic activities with neiboring countries.",""]],"21":[[1,"123","1","Service Sector Capacity Development and Competitiveness Support","Developing the capacity of existing services - such as tourism, transportation and logistics services, wholesale and retail, real estate, construction services, ship building and ship repairing, and public utilities services, sports-related businesses, financial services, health services, meetings, incentives, conferences and exhibitions (MICE), etc. - by promoting investments to raise the competiveness of hospitality businesses, strengthening Thai entrepreneurs to be able to adapt to dynamic changes of context, developing standards accreditation systems and setting standards for businesses in the service sector according to international standards, raising the quality level to meet market demand, and developing and raising the level of infrastructure to create links domestically and internationally to facilitate businesses, as well as supporting research and development by encouraging entrepreneurs to utilize innovation in order to develop their businesses in order to keep up with changes in the digital economy era, which includes supporting the use of suitable social media to expand the market for products and services, both locally and abroad.",""],[1,"123","2","Service Business Modernization and Growth Promotion","Raising the level of new service businesses that are likely to expand and have growth potential, such as digital businesses, international education, entertainment content businesses, and occupational services in order to modernize these services by utilizing new technologies such as Cloud Services, financial application, e-learning, etc., as well as creating connections between potential hospitality businesses for integrated growth, and promoting competition based on business development and benefit incidence throughout the supply chain.",""],[1,"123","3","Service Sector Coordination and Governance Mechanism","Creating a mechanism to unify the service sectors by defining a core host agency to drive the country's service sector strategy at both the policy and operational levels; integrating cooperation from all related sectors, which include the public sector, private sector, and the civil society sector, in order collectively to support and promote the development and regulation of the entire services sector; monitoring the results of the developments to ensure they are moving in the right direction and meeting the defined objectives and targets; and establishing a committee and a subcommittee to drive the development of the overall service sector and potential branches of the hospitality business.",""]],"22":[[1,"190","3","Domestic Rail Industry Development Programme","Accelerating the development of the domestic rail industry to reduce imports and increase economic opportunities for the country by: (1) improving the procurement process for railway infrastructure, including the mass transit system and rolling stock, to help stimulate the growth of related industries; (2) increasing knowledge transfer into and between Thailand's public and private operators, as well as academic institutions; (3) increasing the capacity of railway-related human resources in Thailand; (4) improving investment incentives for railway-related businesses; and (5) encouraging more railway- related research, development, and innovation.",""],[1,"190","4","Aviation Industrial Estates Development","Encouraging the development of the aircraft parts manufacturing and maintenance industries by establishing aviation industrial estates containing world-class aircraft maintenance facilities.",""],[1,"190","4","Aviation Investment Incentive Regulatory Reform","Laws and regulations should also be revised to give better incentives for foreign companies to expand their production bases in Thailand.",""],[1,"190","4","Aviation Human Resources and Innovation Development","Human resources and innovation should continuously be fostered for the country to sustain the development of its aviation industry and eventually become the region's aviation hub.",""]],"23":[[1,"6","2","International Trade and Investment Cooperation Agreements","Thailand needs to make agreements on international trade and investment, and cooperate with allied nations to expand development through bilateral and multilateral arrangements, together with strengthening regional and sub- regional linkages and pursuing a proactive investment strategy boost for the regions.",""],[1,"6","2","Regional Regulatory and Institutional Linkage Strengthening","Therefore, the Twelfth Plan focuses on enhancing international regulatory and institutional linkages at the implementation level and at each border check-point, side-by-side with developing domestic physical infrastructure networks to link with those of neighboring countries.",""],[1,"6","2","Transborder Economic Corridor Development","The Twelfth Plan emphasizes using physical infrastructure linkages as a basis for the development of areas, economies and communities along transborder economic corridors, upgrading their competitiveness and distributing wealth to the communities, provinces, and cities along these economic corridors as well as other domestic linkage areas.",""],[1,"6","2","Entrepreneurial Society and Outward Investment Support","Additionally, Thailand must execute a proactive strategy for creating an entrepreneurial society and intensively supporting Thai entrepreneurs to invest abroad in order to gain capital revenues and potential business opportunities.",""],[1,"6","2","Regional Value Chain Linkage Promotion","The aim is also to promote value chain linkages within the region, especially with Cambodia, Lao PDR, Myanmar, Vietnam (CLMV) and ASEAN.",""],[1,"7","1","Expansion of Bilateral and Multilateral Cooperation Agreements","Not only must existing bilateral and multilateral agreements be efficiently utilized, but also new agreements will be constructed based on the concept of free trade and competitiveness improvement, in particular promoting the use of the cooperation frameworks of ASEAN and with development partners outside ASEAN.",""],[1,"7","1","Development Cooperation and Poverty Reduction Support","Thailand should play a constructive role in supporting development cooperation in every aspect, and in strengthening poverty and inequality reduction in the sub-region and region.",""],[1,"7","1","Adoption of SDGs and International Standards for Enforcement","Additionally, Thailand should adopt the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and international regulations and standards concerning the quality of goods and services, labor rights, environmental suitability, security, transparency, etc. to guide its practices and enforcement.",""],[1,"25","2","New Economic Zones and Border Gateway Development","The development of new economic zones and potential economic border gateways should drive Thailand to become a high-income country in the future.",""],[1,"26","3","Production Network and R&D Product Diversification","Forming production network and utilizing R&D to create a variety of products that respond to the demands of the market should lead to an increase in economic value, a strong production chain as well as an expansion of the economic base.",""],[1,"26","3","Regional Transport, Logistics, and Telecommunications Connectivity Enhancement","In order to enhance the logistics system and lower its costs, connectivity in transportation, logistics and telecommunications within the following cooperation frameworks must be promoted: Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS), Ayeyawady - Chao Phraya - Mekong Economic Cooperation Strategy (ACMECS), Indonesia-Malaysia-Thailand Growth Triangle (IMT-GT), Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multi-Sectoral Technical and Economic Cooperation (BIMSTEC), Joint Development Strategy for Border Areas (JDS), as well as cooperation within the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN).",""],[1,"26","3","ASEAN Connectivity Master Plan Implementation","Development according to the ASEAN connectivity master plan should have continuity and aim at delivering a complete network.",""],[1,"26","3","Transport and Logistics Efficiency and Standards Upgrade","Transportation and logistics should be efficient and meet international standards.",""],[1,"26","3","Transport and Goods Movement Regulatory Revision","Laws and regulations concerning the transportation of people and goods should be revised.",""],[1,"26","3","Transport and Logistics Workforce Development","Manpower in the fields of transportation and logistics should be developed.",""],[1,"28","1","Domestic Connectivity and Economic Corridor Network Expansion","the government plans systematically to increase connectivity within sub-regional and ASEAN framework through domestic networks that connect economic corridors.",""],[1,"28","3","Economic Corridor Physical Linkages Development","Thailand is prepared to be the gateway to the east and the west of Asia, and to enhance physical linkages between economic zones and communities along economic corridors to increase competitiveness and distribute wealth to communities, towns, and provinces along the core economic corridors and along other key transit corridors.",""],[1,"85","2","Transport, Logistics, and Value Chain Connectivity Improvement","Transportation, logistics, and value chains should be interconnected.",""],[1,"109","1","Infrastructure and Logistics Investment Acceleration","The next five years is planned as a period of Thai economic recovery and expansion by expediting investment in infrastructure and logistics, as well as creating a favorable atmosphere to encourage private investors to expand their investment, particularly in key target sectors.",""],[1,"112","1","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Investment Expansion","Public and Private Partnership (PPP) investment in infrastructure projects will increase.",""],[1,"184","2","Infrastructure and Logistics Capacity Expansion","Hence, during the Twelfth Plan, the goal is to expand the capacity of infrastructure and logistics in the country, both in terms of quantity and quality, to support the expansion of urban areas and key economic zones, and to help improve the quality of life.",""],[1,"184","2","Sub-Regional and ASEAN Connectivity Infrastructure Networks","Connectivity within the sub-region and the ASEAN community will also systematically be increased by building infrastructure networks to support areas alongside the economic corridors.",""],[1,"184","2","Infrastructure Management and Regulation Upgrade","Systems of management and regulation will be upgraded to meet international standards in order to increase operational effectiveness and safety, whilst ensuring consumers' rights and providing equal and widespread access to basic infrastructure.",""],[1,"184","2","Support for Infrastructure-Related Industries and Logistics Entrepreneurship","Lastly, the country will support infrastructure-induced industries, as well as logistics entrepreneurship and organizations that have potential to expand their businesses internationally.",""],[1,"184","3","Transport and Trade Infrastructure Improvement and Regulatory Efficiency Measures","To improve transportation and trade facilities and infrastructure, while having effective regulatory mechanisms to ensure efficiency and transparency in transportation businesses, in order to increase the country's competitiveness and improve the people's quality of life.",""]],"24":[[1,"185","6","Rail and Waterway Freight Transport Expansion","to increase the proportion of freight transportation that uses the railways and waterways",""],[1,"187","1","Meter-Gauge Railway Network Upgrade","Improving the meter-gauge railway network to become the main transportation network by accelerating the advancement of the existing rail, signaling and telecommunications infrastructure, as well as upgrading locomotives and rolling stock.",""],[1,"187","1","Dual-Track Railway Development Phase","Further, the country should implement the next phase of its dual-track railways development, starting with the construction of routes within a 5 0 0 -kilometer radius of Bangkok, such as Pak Nam Pho-Den Chai, Chira-Ubon Ratchathani and Chumphon-Surat Thani.",""],[1,"187","1","Rail Corridor Feasibility Studies and Cross-Border Cooperation","In addition, feasibility studies should be conducted for routes along the economic corridors connecting to other ASEAN countries, as well as routes that could act as feeder lines from economic and industrial areas in different provinces to the main rail network.",""],[1,"187","1","Railway Services Cooperation with Neighboring Countries","Cooperation with neighboring countries on railway services should be strengthened.",""],[1,"187","2","Railway Electrification Transition Road Map","Devising a road map to shift from diesel to electrical locomotives in order to accommodate future changes in railway technology",""],[1,"187","3","High-Speed Rail Network Development","During the course of the Twelfth Plan, at least one high-speed railway route should be constructed, while urban development plans for areas along the route should be devised in order to decentralize development to regional cities, raise the standard of public transportation services, and create opportunities for the Thai people to be familiar with the advanced rail technology.",""],[1,"187","4","Railway Gauge Standardization and Mass-Transit Rail Standardization","Standardizing the meter-gauge and standard-gauge railway systems as well as the mass-transit city-rail system to help streamline the procurement bidding process and to ensure a higher quality of services, which will thereby help reduce operation and maintenance costs for railway operators.",""],[1,"198","15","Meter-Gauge Double-Track Railway Expansion","A total of 14 routes of meter-gauge double-track railway projects covering 2,500 kilometers, including 7 cabinet-approved routes",""],[1,"199","1","Railway Section Development and Feasibility Study Programme","Kaeng Khoi section, Thanon Chira Junction-Khon Kaen section, Map Kabao-Thanon Chira Junction section, Prachuap Khiri Khan-Chumphon section, Lopburi-Pak Nam Pho section, Nakhon Pathom-Hua Hin section, and Hua Hin-Prachuap Khiri Khan section) and 7 routes under the process of conducting feasibility studies or designing the specifics (Pak Nam Pho-Den Chai section, Thanon Chira Junction-Ubon Ratchathani section, Khon Kaen-Nong Khai section, Chumphon-Surat Thani section, Surat Thani-Hat Yai-Songkhla section, Hat Yai-Padang Besar section (driven by electric energy), and Den Chai-Chiang Mai section).",""],[1,"199","2","High-Speed Railway Project","At least one high-speed railway project.",""],[1,"199","3","Construction of New Railway Routes Along Economic Corridors","Projects constructing new railway routes along important economic corridors (Kanchanaburi-Bangkok-Aranyaprathet section, Kanchanaburi-Bangkok- Laem Chabang section, and Den Chai-Chiang Rai-Chiang Khong section).",""]],"25":[[1,"185","6","Urban Public Transport Use Expansion","to raise the proportion of passengers using public transportation systems in urban areas",""],[1,"188","1","Urban Public Transport System Development","The country should accelerate the construction of mass-transit city-rail projects as planned in the Mass Rapid Transit Master Plan in the Bangkok Metropolitan Region (M-Map).",""],[1,"188","1","Regional City Public Transport Development","Moreover, the public transport systems in regional cities should be developed according to the characteristics of each city, whether it be a light rail network, bus rapid transit (BRT), or trams.",""],[1,"188","2","Bus Service Quality Improvement and Route Rerouting","Improving the quality of bus services and rerouting bus lines so that they can help connect passengers to the main public transportation network and increase the use of public transportation.",""],[1,"188","2","Local Government Support for Regional Public Transport Development","Furthermore, local government organizations should be encouraged to increase their role in improving public transportation in order to accelerate the development of public transportation in regional areas.",""],[1,"188","3","Transit-Oriented Development and Station Area Facility Improvement","Developing facilities in transportation stations to be in line with the direction of land development, in order to maximize the use of public transportation systems in these areas.",""],[1,"188","3","Stricter Urban Planning Regulation Enforcement","the country should promote the stricter enforcement of urban planning regulations",""],[1,"188","3","Urban Character Enhancement and Transit-Oriented Development Promotion","the enhancement of urban areas' unique characteristics, and the pursuit of better transit-oriented development (TOD) at a level suited to the management capability of each city's local government.",""],[1,"188","4","Non-Motorized Transport Infrastructure Expansion","Expanding infrastructure and facilities to support non-motorized transportation (NMT) in urban areas by focusing on improving crosswalks, footpaths, and bicycle lanes along the local routes leading to the city's public transportation network.",""],[1,"188","4","Urban Pedestrian and Cyclist Safety Standards Improvement","Standards for the safety and protection of pedestrians and cyclists in urban areas should also be improved to facilitate the proportional increase in NMT, which in turn will help boost energy efficiency and reduce environmental impacts.",""],[1,"188","4","Universal Design Infrastructure Development","Moreover, infrastructure development in the next period must consider the accommodation of all users, particularly the disabled and seniors, by designing new infrastructure and improving the existing infrastructure to facilitate and serve all users under a universal design concept.",""],[1,"191","2","Common Public Transport Fare Structure Reform","Creating a common fare structure for the public transportation system to increase public transport usage, and selecting an appropriate mechanism to compensate both public and private transportation operators facing losses as they support efforts to encourage a greater proportional use of public transport.",""],[1,"191","3","Transportation Regulation Update and Streamlining","Updating and streamlining transportation-related measures, laws, and regulations.",""],[1,"191","3","Rail Transport Modal Shift Promotion","Related agencies should find effective ways to enforce regulations that will help push rail transportation to become the main mode of passenger and freight transportation.",""],[1,"191","3","Urban Vehicle Demand Management and Road Usage Fees","These measures and regulations include demand management for reducing personal motorized vehicles in urban areas, and collecting road usage fees to help the government reduce maintenance costs.",""],[1,"199","5","Bangkok Metropolitan Region Mass Rapid Transit Expansion","A total of 10 mass rapid transit lines (13 projects) in the Bangkok Metropolitan Region, covering 384 kilometers, consisting of 7 cabinet-approved projects ... and 6 projects under the process of conducting feasibility studies or designing the specific",""],[1,"199","6","Public Transport System Development Projects in Major Regional Cities","Public transport system development projects in major regional cities, including Khon Kaen, Chiang Mai, Songkhla, Hat Yai and Phuket.",""],[1,"225","2","Urban Public Transportation System Development","To develop urban public transportation systems in order to alleviate traffic congestion and to provide accessible, environmentally-friendly public transportation at low-cost.",""],[1,"225","3","Inclusive Urban Public Transport Development Guidelines","Employing safe, convenient, and inclusive public transport guidelines on urban public transport development, including the bus system, bicycle lanes, and pedestrian paths.",""],[1,"225","14","Urban Transport Hub Development","Developing urban transport hubs, e.g. Bang Sue.",""],[1,"226","5","Urban Transport, Flood Protection, and Wastewater System Efficiency Improvement","Enhancing the efficiency of transportation networks, flood protection systems, and wastewater treatment systems for the urban areas to be safe and livable.",""],[1,"226","8","Road Routing and Multimodal Transport Network Improvement","Improving road routing networks, public transportation, and multimodal transportation linking with other cities and surrounding areas.",""],[1,"226","11","Public Transportation and Infrastructure Connectivity Improvement","Improving public transportation systems and developing infrastructure connectivity both within the Northeastern region and with other regions.",""],[1,"227","1","Public Transportation and Information Technology Infrastructure Improvement","Improving public transportation systems and information technology infrastructure.",""]],"26":[[1,"26","2","Tourism Law Amendment for Sustainable Development","The focus is on amending laws to achieve a balanced and sustainable development in the tourism industry by giving more careful consideration to the carrying capacity of ecosystems in evaluating an area's potential for tourism development.",""],[1,"123","5","Tourism Value-Addition and Community-Based Tourism Promotion","Promoting revenue generated from tourism by: (1) encouraging the adding of value to tourism products and services by utilizing Thai identity that reflects local cultures and lifestyles in the community, such as tourism that links with One Tambon One Product (OTOP).",""],[1,"124","1","Creative Tourist Destination Development","developing man-made creative tourist destinations as new attractions for quality tourists from around the world;",""],[1,"124","1","Cluster Tourism Development","developing cluster tourism according to the capacity of an area that links with tourism activities based on market demand, such as community tourism, health tourism, agricultural tourism, marine tourism, green tourism, art and culture tourism, MICE tourism, sport tourism, and Halal tourism;",""],[1,"124","1","Thai Tourism Image Restoration Campaign","restoring confidence in and creating a good image of Thai tourism in the global vision;",""],[1,"124","1","Tourism Marketing Strategy Expansion","implementing both passive and active marketing strategies in target markets, both existing and new potential markets, by focusing on quality tourists in order to align with tourism activities that emphasize worthwhile experiences rather than cost-effective tourism, as well as encouraging Thai tourists to travel more domestically in order to reduce dependency on foreign markets;",""],[1,"135","1","Promoting Alternative Tourism Program","Promoting Alternative Tourism Program: Wellness Tourism, Cultural Tourism, Marine and Railway Tourism:",""],[1,"135","2","Alternative Tourism Development Program","To achieve this goal, the program will be designed for specific types of tourism which will match with niche market tourists, especially quality tourists who value alternative tourism and activities.",""],[1,"135","5","Tourism Development Zones","the Ministry of Tourism and Sports announced the ministerial regulations on Tourism Development Zones, including 5 tourism zones: Lanna Civilisation, Active Beach, Southern-Isan Civilisation, the Royal Coast and the Andaman Sea.","Ministry of Tourism and Sports"],[1,"135","5","Additional Tourism Development Zone for Local Area Connectivity","another tourism development zone will be launched to boost tourism in local areas and to connect travel routes from popular cities to nearby provinces.",""],[1,"135","8","Creative Man-Made Tourist Attractions Development","Establishing creative man-made tourist attractions would help to mitigate this problem, while development schemes and healthy surroundings will benefit local communities in economic terms.",""],[1,"214","14","Quality and Sustainable Tourism Development Initiative","To develop quality and sustainable tourism with healthcare-related services, high-standard education, and high-value creative products.",""],[1,"214","15","Tourism Cluster Development Initiative","Developing potential tourism clusters, namely: (1.1) Lanna Cultural Tourism Cluster and Ethnic Tourism in Eight Provinces of Upper Northern Provincial Clusters: by enhancing the uniqueness of Lanna culture with its distinct",""],[1,"215","1","Creative Tourism Services and Products Development","identities and local wisdom to develop creative tourism services and products;",""],[1,"215","1","World Heritage Tourism Cluster Development","(1.2) World Heritage Tourism Cluster by restoring the World Heritage Sites in Sukhothai1 and Kamphaengphet while developing tourism routes linking Sukhothai Historical Park-Si Satchannalai-Kamphaengphet to the surrounding tourist destinations;",""],[1,"215","1","Natural Tourism Cluster Development","(1.3) Natural Tourism Clusters in Chiang Mai, Chiang Rai, Mae Hong Son, Nan, Phetchaboon, and Uthai Thani by creating new tourist destinations in addition to tourism infrastructure and facilities improvement.",""],[1,"215","2","Quality Tourism Upgrading for Target Groups","(2) Upgrading quality tourism for specific target groups in Chiang Mai, Mae Hong Son and Nan, such as Meetings-Incentives-Conferences-Exhibitions (MICE), sports and adventure tourism, health tourism, long-stay tourism, and leisure tourism.",""],[1,"218","5","Cultural Tourism Development and Route Network Programme","Promoting cultural tourism in all areas ... by: (1.1) developing tourism service innovations to meet diverse market demand, (1.2) improving tourist attractions to meet high standards, (1.3) creating year-round tourism activities, and (1.4) developing tourism routes network linking tourist attractions from major cities to minor cities and local communities.",""],[1,"220","8","International Coastal Destination Development","Developing international coastal destinations in Chonburi, Phetchaburi, and Prachuapkhirikhan to distribute income and create job by upgrading tourism services to meet with international standards.",""],[1,"220","9","Eco-Tourism and Community-Based Tourism Rehabilitation and Improvement","Rehabilitating and improving eco-tourism, health tourism, agricultural tourism, and community-based tourism in Nakhonnayok,",""],[1,"221","1","Tourism Attraction and Service Development Initiative","improving tourist attractions as well as travel-related services and facilities, (2.2) creating tourism activities, and (2.3) developing tourism-related products and services to meet international standards.",""],[1,"221","2","Provincial Tourism Destination Improvement and Cluster Development","Supporting and promoting the development of tourism in Ayuthaya, Angthong, Lopburi, Chainat, and Kanchanaburi as centers of historical, cultural and agricultural tourism by improving tourist destinations and activities to be valuable, diverse, and sustainably connected with provincial clusters.",""],[1,"221","3","Khmer Cultural Tourism Rehabilitation and Conservation","Rehabilitating and conserving Khmer cultural tourism in Prachinburi and Sakaeo by: (4.1) rehabilitating and reconstructing archeological sites and antiquities, (4.2) improving and conserving the environment, and (4.3) ensuring suitable land use for sustainable development.",""],[1,"230","9","Lanna Culture Cluster for Creative Tourism Project","Developing a Lanna Culture Cluster towards Creative Tourism Project:",""],[1,"230","10","Lanna Creative Tourism Development Initiative","upgrading tourism activities in the Lanna culture cluster to embrace distinct identity and sustainability, as well as fostering value creation by using Lanna identity and wisdom to develop creative tourism products and services.",""],[1,"232","2","Upgrading International Beach Tourism Activities and Services in the Central Region Project","5.6 Upgrading International Beach Tourism Activities and Services in the Central Region Project:",""],[1,"232","3","Tourism Attraction Rehabilitation and Facility Upgrading","rehabilitating tourist attractions and improving adequate facilities for tourism activities, products and services towards international standards.",""],[1,"233","12","World Heritage City and Srivichai Culture Tourism Site Development Project","Developing the World Heritage City and Srivichai Culture Tourism Site in Nakhon Sri Thammarat Project:",""],[1,"234","1","Temple Improvement and Historical Tourism Site Development","improving Phra Borommathat Mahavoraviharn temple, improving and developing historical tourism sites, as well as developing the landscape in Nakhon Sri Thammarat city in correspondence with the development of a World Heritage City and the Srivijaya historical culture tourism site, to attract both Thai and foreign tourists in order to generate and distribute income to local people.",""],[1,"234","8","Inland Tourism Network Development","developing inland tourism locations and potential community attractions to create tourism networks linking popular tourism areas in Phuket, Phang Nga, Krabi, Surat Thani (Koh Samui, Koh Pha Ngan, and Koh Tao), Chumphon, and Nakorn Si Thammarat (Sichon and Khanom).",""],[1,"248","11","Historical and Cultural Tourism Attraction Development","To develop historical and cultural tourist attractions to raise local pride and preserve national heritage.",""]],"27":[[1,"105","7","Community-Based and Conservation Tourism Promotion","Community-based tourism and conservation tourism should also be promoted in communities with touristic sites.",""],[1,"106","1","Community Welfare and Resource Management Partnerships","Foster community participation in providing welfare, social services and resource management through partnerships with government agencies and local administrative organizations.",""]],"28":[[1,"134","5","Sustainable Tourist Attraction Development and Rehabilitation Scheme","Consequently, a development and rehabilitation scheme, through an improvement of image and surroundings by taking long-run carrying capacity into consideration, will be essential to develop sustainable tourist attractions.",""],[1,"147","3","Sustainable Tourism Management and Environmental Controls","Promote sustainable tourism by taking the carrying capacity of ecosystems (destinations) into account.",""],[1,"147","3","Community-Based Eco-Tourism Income Generation","Encourage communities to gain revenue from tourism while conserving natural resources, and preserving local culture and identity.",""]],"29":[[1,"218","6","Tourism Route Development and Cross-Border Tourism Linkages","(2) Developing transportation routes which link tourist attractions with neighboring countries, such as the Lan Xang Cultural Square links among Loei-Udon Thani-Nongbua Lamphu-Nong Khai-Lao PDR by: (2.1) expediting the construction of tourism routes to link tourist attractions geographically, and (2.2) connecting tourism activities between the private sector and local communities in Thailand and with neighboring countries, in accordance with tourist demand.",""],[1,"222","6","Yacht and Cruise Tourism Development in Southern Thailand","Supporting Phuket, Phang Nga, Krabi, and Koh Samui District, Surat Thani to attain continuously increasing income from tourism with due consideration to the carrying capacity of each area, for the Southern Region to become a destination of yacht and cruise tourism by: (1.1) encouraging all stakeholders to create value for quality and environmentally-friendly tourism services, (1.2) developing the yacht and cruise tourism businesses in Krabi and Koh Samui District of Surat Thani, (1.3) improving public infrastructure and facilities to be standardized and adequate, and (1.4) developing security systems according to international standards.",""],[1,"222","7","Tourism Connectivity and Inland Destination Development","Promoting and developing connectivity among tourist destinations along the coasts of the Andaman Sea and the Gulf of Thailand, including the high-potential inland tourist destinations, by: supporting the development of new inland tourist destinations such as Rajjaprabha Dam in Surat Thani, Khao Luang Natural Park in Nakhon Si Thammarat, and other high-potential community attractions in order to create",""],[1,"228","6","Seaport Development for Ferry and Cruise Connectivity","Develop seaports for ferries and cruise ships connecting the east and west coasts of the gulf of Thailand.",""]],"30":[[1,"161","4","Disease Surveillance, Prevention and Control System","Build partnerships with local, regional and international partners in the setting up of a system of surveillance, prevention and control of diseases and health hazards that meets international standards, to be ready to track, analyze and assess likely scenarios, and be prepared to take appropriate action.",""],[1,"165","1","Public Health Emergency Preparedness and Recovery Measures","be ready to track, analyze and assess likely scenarios in order to be prepared to tackle and take various actions to stop emergency situations, or to recover from severe epidemics and other public health emergencies in order to return to normal within the shortest possible time, most efficiently and effectively.",""],[1,"165","1","Disease Outbreak Prevention and Health Hazard Control","This applies particularly to the prevention of disease outbreaks and widespread health hazards, avoiding damage to the life of the people, the economy and the society, and includes post-crisis rehabilitation to return to normalcy.",""]],"31":[[1,"215","3","Chiang Mai High-Potential Services and Industries Development","Supporting Chiang Mai to be a hub for food and health products, medical and healthcare services, international educational services, as well as creative products, particularly digital creations, which are high-potential target services and industries of the Northern Region, by applying technologies and innovation to differentiate value-added products and services for niche markets.",""],[1,"234","11","Health and Medical Tourism Development Initiative","improving health/medical tourism by (1) utilizing natural resources and local wisdom, (2) restoring tourist attractions and landscape architecture, (3) developing infrastructure and facilities in natural tourist attractions, (4) promoting local cultures and communities, and (5) enhancing service quality.",""]],"32":[[1,"94","6","Health Literacy and Mental Health Access Improvement","Improving health literacy among Thai people and providing easier-to- access mental health consultations, as well as regulating health-related information publication, which should have an academic or scientific grounding.",""],[1,"94","7","Age-Specific Health Activities and Nutrition Support","Encouraging adequate age-specific heath activities and nutrition, and assisting local communities in allocating and managing public areas and facilities designed for physical activities and sports.",""],[1,"94","8","Healthy Food Production Incentives and Food Labeling Regulation","Improving relevant legal measures and tax incentives aimed at promoting entrepreneurs to start using technology and innovation in healthy food and beverage production as alternatives for consumers, promoting easy-to-understand food labels on product packaging, as well as regulating the advertisement of unhealthy products that may have harmful impacts on human health.",""],[1,"94","9","Health Impact Assessment Integration in Public Policy Design","Pushing forward the conducting of Health Impact Assessments (HIA) when designing and implementing public policies at all levels: national, spatial and local community.",""],[1,"98","5","Health Risk Behavior Awareness and Nutrition Education Initiative","emphasizes collaborative integration of all related parties' operations aimed at increasing awareness of health risk behavior among all Thais, thereby adjusting and improving such behavior through the following measures: 1) building positive attitudes towards good health and promoting learning of adequate nutrient intake by including knowledge on adequate nutrient intake in official curricula and promoting public-friendly and enthusiasm-triggering public communication means to educate the general public on healthy and unhealthy products, as well as self-assessment",""],[1,"99","1","Health-Friendly Environment Development Initiative","promoting health-friendly environments by developing health-friendly infrastructure and public services systems, and encouraging companies and organizations to allocate spaces/areas for physical activities",""],[1,"99","1","Tax Incentives for Organic Food Production and Use","promoting tax incentive measures designed to encourage business producers, distributors and restaurants to produce and use organic products as alternative food products for consumers to choose from, and financially subsidizing agriculturalists cultivating organic fruits and vegetables",""]],"33":[[1,"193","3","Energy Conservation Incentives and Public Awareness Campaign","Improving the subsidy system and other incentives to encourage behavioral changes in the industrial sector, the transportation sector, the business sector, and the households sector, such as incentives to improve energy conservation and policies to encourage more usage of the existing public transportation and rail systems.",""],[1,"193","3","National Energy Conservation Information and Responsibility Campaign","The government also should regularly keep the Thai people informed about energy conservation and energy efficiency, as well as cultivate understanding and a sense of responsibility regarding conservation and efficiency in energy consumption.",""],[1,"193","4","Energy Price Structure and Tax Incentive Reform","Revamping the energy price structure so it can better reflect real costs, and is fair to both consumers and producers.",""],[1,"193","5","Energy Conservation and Efficiency Law Enforcement","Increasing efforts in enforcing laws and regulations regarding energy conservation and energy efficiency, especially the enforcement of the Building Energy Code (BEC) for new buildings and the Energy Efficiency Resources Standard (EERS) for energy producers and distributors.",""],[1,"193","6","Energy Conservation Research and Standards Program","Encouraging both the public and private sectors to undertake research and develop technology related to energy conservation and energy efficiency for machinery, materials, and appliances in manufacturing processes, in business operations, and in everyday life.",""],[1,"194","5","Alternative Energy Data and Planning Database","Developing a database on the generation and utilization of alternative energy to help with the planning of infrastructure to support the expansion of alternative energy in the future.",""],[1,"194","5","Alternative Fuel Safety Standards Enforcement","standards should be set and enforced to ensure safety in the production and use of such fuels.",""],[1,"194","5","Public Information on Alternative and Clean Energy","The government should also work to keep the Thai people informed on alternative and clean energy.",""],[1,"194","6","Evaluation of Feed-in Tariffs for Alternative Energy","Evaluating the existing incentives (feed-in tariffs) that aim to increase the share of alternative fuels in power generation, to help develop other incentives that are fair to both the producers and consumers of alternative energy.",""],[1,"194","6","Private Sector Participation Mechanism for the Alternative Energy Development Plan","The government should also create a mechanism that allows the private sector to participate in driving the Alternative Energy Development Plan to the achievement of its objectives, whether in the process of material acquisition, fuel formulation, transportation, supply chain management, or energy generation.",""],[1,"194","7","Biofuel Market Mechanism for Transport Sector","Increasing the use of biofuels in the transportation sector by using market mechanisms to lower the price of biofuels to levels competitive with those of fossil",""],[1,"195","1","Alternative Energy Generation Promotion","alternative energy generation should be encouraged for power and heat generation in industrial factories, businesses, and households.",""],[1,"195","2","Alternative Energy Technology Research and Development","Continuously researching and developing alternative energy technology, including solar, wind, hydropower, biomass, biogas, energy crops, and waste, so that the costs of alternative fuels can be reduced to commercially viable levels.",""],[1,"195","3","Public Energy Literacy Campaign","The aim should also be systematically to educate Thai citizens regarding the process of energy acquisition and the various limitations of different energy sources, in order to cultivate a sense of responsibility in their energy consumption and raise people's understanding of policy directions.",""],[1,"201","9","Factory and Building Energy Management Plans and Measures","Factory and building energy management plans and measures, carried out by the Ministry of Energy, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Energy"],[1,"202","4","Rooftop Solar Installation Promotion","Promotion of rooftop solar installments, carried out by the Ministry of Energy, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Energy"],[1,"215","7","Alternative Energy Production Development in Nakhon Sawan and Kamphangphet","Developing areas in Nakhon Sawan and Kamphangphet for alternative energy production by: utilizing agricultural products and",""],[1,"218","3","Renewable Energy Production Expansion in Provincial Clusters","Enhancing renewable energy production in the Central and Lower Northeastern provincial clusters by: (4.1) balancing food and energy crop plantations, (4.2) suggesting suitable areas for farmers to grow energy crops, and (4.3) encouraging manufacturers, local communities, and local authorities to generate renewable energy from solar energy, wind power, biomass, and solid waste.",""],[1,"245","3","Support for Implementing the Roadmap for Expanded Energy Cooperation","Support for implementing the Roadmap for Expanded Energy Cooperation (2009-2018).",""]],"34":[[1,"6","1","Livable Cities Spatial Development Initiative","henceforth, the spatial development and enhanced economic potential of cities must be emphasized.",""],[1,"6","1","Urban Environmental Standards and Land Use Rationalization","This will be accomplished through improved environmental standards, rationalization of land use, organized city planning, and strengthened urban security which is consistent with Livable Cities benchmarks.",""],[1,"28","2","Strengthening Production and Service Bases","strengthening the existing production and service bases",""],[1,"28","2","Expansion of Production and Service Bases","expanding new production and service bases to generate more income for people in each region",""],[1,"28","2","Urban Quality Growth Support","supporting the quality growth of urban areas",""],[1,"28","2","Eastern Seaboard Development and Revitalization","developing and reviving the Eastern Seaboard areas to accommodate future industrial expansion",""],[1,"28","2","Border Economic Area Management","enabling the sound management of border economic areas to attain sustainable growth and competitiveness",""],[1,"28","2","Urban and Regional Development Implementation Mechanism Enhancement","enhancing the efficiency of urban and regional development implementation mechanisms to obtain concrete outcomes",""],[1,"64","3","Urban Planning and Management Improvement Package","various aspects of urban planning and management need to be improved, namely (1) public transport services, (2) traffic management, (3) urban planning, (4) public facilities and utilities extension, (5) solid waste and waste water management, (6) universal facilities to support an aging society, and (7) public safety and reduction of risk from natural disasters, crime and insurgency.",""],[1,"64","4","Integrated Economic, Social, and Environmental Infrastructure Planning","Provisions to support economic growth while improving people's livelihoods shall include planning for the development of economic, social, and environmental infrastructure to be standardized, sufficient, and responsive to economic expansion.",""],[1,"213","1","Regional Economic Development and Urban Infrastructure Improvement","With appropriate urban development in addition to infrastructure and logistics improvement, prospective cities can be developed to become livable cities with the capacity to accommodate increasing trade and investment.",""],[1,"213","2","Strengthening Existing Production and Service Bases","The Twelfth National Economic and Social Development Plan emphasizes key developments and activities to be undertaken in a timely manner, namely: (1) strengthening the existing production and service bases;",""],[1,"213","2","Creation of New Production and Service Bases","creating new production and service bases to generate income for people in all regions;",""],[1,"213","2","Urban Quality Growth Support","supporting the quality growth of urban areas;",""],[1,"213","2","Eastern Seaboard Development and Revitalization","developing and reviving the Eastern Seaboard areas to accommodate future industrial expansion;",""],[1,"213","2","Border Economic Area Management","enabling the sound management of border economic areas to attain sustainable growth and competitiveness;",""],[1,"213","2","Urban and Regional Development Implementation Mechanism Enhancement","enhancing the efficiency of urban and regional development implementation mechanisms to deliver concrete outcomes.",""],[1,"224","8","Public Utilities and Facilities Expansion","Providing high quality public utilities and facilities to accommodate both public and business demand.",""],[1,"224","9","Standardized Public Service System for Low-Income Housing","Organizing standardized public service systems including residences for low-income people.",""],[1,"225","7","Digital Economy for Urban Development and Town Branding","Applying digital economy to enhance urban development while encouraging the community learning process to create a brand identity of towns in order to reinforce valuable development for both economic and social benefits.",""],[1,"225","9","Urban Municipality Consolidation and Local Government Cooperation Reform","Merging urban municipalities to be appropriately sized while enhancing local governments' competitiveness and cooperation.",""],[1,"225","10","Participatory Urban Development Planning and Enforcement","Empowering local people in the participatory process for urban development, including urban planning and its enforcement.",""],[1,"225","11","Central Government Support for Urban Development","Expanding the roles of central government agencies to support urban development in both technical and budgetary aspects.",""],[1,"225","15","Urban Land Use and Service Planning","Organizing land use regulations, public utilities and facilities, social services, and residential areas to accommodate the increasing demand from the urban population.",""],[1,"226","4","Integrated Urban Zoning and Infrastructure Planning","Integrating urban zoning with infrastructure networks, public transportation systems, social facilities, and urban environmental management to accommodate a well-balanced urban expansion",""],[1,"226","7","Urban Center Development in Chiang Mai and Phitsanulok","Urban areas in Chiang Mai and Phitsanulok to be developed as centers of commerce, services, medical, education, and digital business:",""],[1,"226","9","Information Technology Network Efficiency Development","Developing efficiency of information technology networks to accommodate the digital society and urban environmental management systems for sustainable urban development.",""],[1,"226","10","Urban Center Development for Trade, Investment, Medical Services, and Education","Urban areas in Khon Kaen and Nakhon Ratchasima to be developed as centers of trade and investment as well as hubs of medical services and education:",""],[1,"227","2","Residential Area Development with Waste Management Systems","Developing residential areas to accommodate the growing population with appropriate waste management systems.",""],[1,"227","3","Strategic City Connectivity Development","Key strategic cities with major railway stations, such as the cities of Ayutthaya, Nakorn Sawan, Khonkaen, Thung Song, as well as border cities, namely Betong, Sadao, Phu Nam Ron, Aranyaprathet, Nakorn Phanom, Nong Khai, and Chiang Khong, to be developed according to each area's potential for connectivity development.",""],[1,"227","4","Transit-Oriented Development Adoption","Adopting the Transit-Oriented Development (TOD) concept.",""],[1,"227","5","Pilot Projects on Land Reform, Urban Planning, and Energy-Efficient Urban Development","Initiating pilot projects on land reform, urban planning, and energy-efficient urban development.",""],[1,"227","6","Eastern Seaboard Area Revival Program","by taking a balanced development approach and executing an efficient area revival program based on participatory processes, the ESB shall be able to accommodate future industrial expansion according to its potential.",""],[1,"235","4","Urban Environmental Improvement and Development Project","5.17 The Urban Environmental Improvement and Development Project:",""],[1,"248","1","Green Cities Initiatives Expansion","Green Cities Initiatives in Songkhla (Hat Yai and Songkhla municipalities) (2016-2018) (to be expanded to cover all provinces).",""]],"35":[[1,"94","3","E-Learning Materials Development Initiative","Creating e-learning materials that can be used or communicated through various easy-to-access and convenient communicative platforms, anytime and anywhere, and creating tax incentives to attract more private entities to produce high quality but inexpensive books and other learning materials.",""],[1,"94","3","Tax Incentives for Affordable Learning Materials","creating tax incentives to attract more private entities to produce high quality but inexpensive books and other learning materials.",""],[1,"94","4","Local Learning Center Transformation Initiative","Transforming local learning centers - such as libraries, museums, historical parks, and schools for the elderly - into more creative and living learning resources, as well as pushing forward better local wisdom management in local communities.",""],[1,"99","5","Development of Modern Learning Resource Centers","emphasizing the development of resource centers to become living, modern, quality and standardized learning centers in order to motivate people of all ages to have an interest in learning and taking part in educational activities",""],[1,"99","5","Development of Virtual Library and Edutainment Center","the development of new forms of resource centers that can help enhance Thai people's capacity to embrace any possible changes in the future, such as the Virtual Library and the Edutainment Center",""],[1,"100","1","Modern Local Library Services and Learning Access Expansion","promotion of reading through modern local library services, provision of opportunities to children and youths to gain easy access to quality, fast, and convenient learning services, establishment of learning parks at both the provincial and regional levels, as well as collaboration between all related parties in local communities to develop local museums as great culture and history learning centers.",""],[1,"100","1","Community Museum Development for Culture and History Learning","collaboration between all related parties in local communities to develop local museums as great culture and history learning centers.",""],[1,"107","4","Free Wi-Fi in Educational Institutions Nationwide","Having free wifi services at all educational institutions nationwide will enable students of all ages to access information that is useful for their learning and research.",""]],"36":[[1,"96","6","Public Access to Academic Research Initiative","providing free public access to academic research",""],[1,"96","6","Community-Based Spatial Development Research Programme","promoting educational institutions to conduct more research with interested local communities on spatial development",""],[1,"96","9","Private Sector Incentive Measures for Social Innovation Projects","Designing incentive measures aimed at attracting the private sector to take part in new social project developments that are considered social innovations, such as local products development, social stock exchange, social bonds, social enterprise, and media for learning.",""],[1,"105","5","Community-Level Transformational Leadership Development","Build and empower transformational leaders at community level to inspire members in community development, have good governance, and promote cooperation and self-reliance within the community.",""],[1,"105","6","Learning Communities Research and Knowledge Transfer System","Promote learning communities through a research and knowledge transfer system in order to resolve local issues as well as to transform knowledge for commercial use.",""],[1,"105","6","Information Technology for Community Knowledge Management","the use of information technology should be promoted as a tool for community knowledge management.",""],[1,"105","7","Community Training Center Support","Strengthen community economies by promoting community-level entrepreneurship, supporting community training centers and connecting industrial clusters with community economies.",""]],"37":[[1,"140","5","Forest Conservation and Restoration Programme","Target 1: Conserve and restore the stock of natural resources: increase the area of forest for conservation and commercial use, and reverse mangrove forest depletion; curb biodiversity loss; solve the problem of public land encroachment and provide the poor with common rights to use land.",""],[1,"142","3","Forest Conservation and Restoration Programme","Protect and restore forest and wildlife resources in a concrete manner: stop deforestration in order to maintain the country's forest areas of 102.3 million rai.",""],[1,"142","3","Community Forest Management and Participatory Restoration Network","Encourage community forest management for household use.",""],[1,"142","3","Community Forest Law and Participatory Restoration Networks","Advocate community forest law: creating participatory networks of forest restoration and protection.",""],[1,"142","3","Economic Forestry Expansion and Long-Term Tree Plantation Support","Increasing the economic forest areas up to 15 percents of the country's total area, promoting the plantation of long-term economically valuable trees such as teak, Afzelia siamica and Siamese rosewood, or change from short-term economically valuable trees to longer-term yield species.",""],[1,"142","3","Timber Market and Logistics Development","Set up a central market for timber trading, and develop logistic systems for trading and delivering timber, studying and piloting financial mechanisms for promoting forestarion, such as forest bonds, tree banks, or reforestation funds.",""],[1,"142","3","Forestry Research and Development Support","Support research and development (R&D) in various topics: identifying complementary plants for forestry plantation and agro-forestry to generate an additional stream of revenue for farmers while they are waiting to harvest economic forests; innovating with high-value wood products.",""],[1,"142","3","Conservation Tourism Revenue Development","Meanwhile, develop and foster approaches to creating revenue from conservation, such as sustainable tourism in conservation areas or community tourism for conservation.",""],[1,"152","6","Afforestation and Sustainable Forest Plantation Management","promote the growing of long-term economic value trees: develop afforestation procedures and the sustainable management of forest plantations.",""],[1,"152","6","High-Value Timber Industry Development","Create a high-value timber industry in the entire supply chain.",""],[1,"152","6","Forest Incentives and Timber Market Development","the government should set incentive measures, designate the suitable areas with potential in the ecological landscape and establish a central timber market.",""],[1,"152","6","Timber Logistics System Development","The logistics system for transporting timber should be developed.",""],[1,"152","6","Forest Financing Mechanisms","Introduce new financial mechanisms such as forest bonds, tree banks, and forestation funds.",""],[1,"152","6","Tree Genetic Improvement Research","Support the study of and research into the genetic improvement of tree varieties.",""],[1,"152","6","Wood Value-Addition Innovation Programme","Create innovations that add new value to wood and timber.",""],[1,"152","6","Wood Use Restoration for Conservation and Construction","Restore the use of wood in conservation, construction of houses, temples and other buildings, as well as wood carving as a national art.",""],[1,"153","1","Economic Forest Cultivation Strategy Formulation and Implementation","main mandate of this working group is to formulate the strategies of economic forest cultivaton in the entire system and implement these strategies to achieve the stated goals.",""]],"38":[[1,"151","3","ASEAN Environmental Cooperation Master Plan Advocacy","advocate the formulation of an ASEAN master plan on natural resources and environmental management.",""],[1,"151","3","ASEAN-GMS Cooperation Guidelines on Transboundary Environmental Management","Develop guidelines for cooperation between ASEAN and the Greater Mekong Subregion (GMS) in terms of transboundary transport, energy and natural resource management, and transboundary haze pollution.",""],[1,"151","3","International Environmental Law and Agreement Awareness Programme","Create knowledge, understanding, and good practice regarding international laws and agreements among stakeholders.",""],[1,"151","3","Trade and Environment Agreement Review Mechanism","Regularly review and follow updates of international laws and agreements on trade and the environment.",""],[1,"151","3","Studies on Commitments under International Environmental Agreements","Support detailed studies and research on the country's commitments resulting from endorsing any international environmental agreements.",""]],"39":[[1,"140","9","Watershed-Level Water Resource Management","manage water resources at the watershed level to achieve a balance between demand and supply; solve water shortages, and minimize the number of affected people; increase the efficiency of water use in both production and consumption, while decreasing loss and damage from floods and droughts.",""],[1,"144","2","Participatory Water Resources Management Improvement","Increase the efficiency of the management of water resources to achieve the goals of stability, balance and sustainability in both quantity and quality.",""],[1,"144","3","Water Resources Bill Promulgation","Expedite the promulgation of the Water Resources Bill of ... to be the principal law for water resources management.",""],[1,"144","3","National Committee on Water Resources Management","This law should establish a National Committee on Water Resources Management (NCWRM) as the main mechanism for formulating national policies as well as strategic plans for the development and management of water resources, both in normal and crisis states, including droughts and floods.",""],[1,"144","3","National Water Resources Database Development","The mandate of the NCWRM should comprise the building of a national water resources databases",""],[1,"144","3","Annual Integrated Water Resources Budget Planning","and preparation of annual integrated budget plans for water resources based on the selected programs or projects proposed by government agencies, local administrations and watershed committees.",""],[1,"144","4","Integrated Water Resources Management Planning in Main Watersheds","Accelerate the formulation of integrated water resouces management plans in the country's 25 main watersheds.",""],[1,"144","4","Watershed Committees under the NCWRM","Set up watershed committees under the NCWRM to be the key driver at the local level.",""],[1,"144","4","Watershed Coordination and Collaboration Frameworks","Their mandates should encompass setting up frameworks for management: developing and using water resources within the watersheds, preparing water resources programs and projects, both in normal and crisis conditions, and fostering effective networks of coordination and collaboration among local people, non-government organizations (NGO), community organizations, local administrations and government agencies.",""],[1,"144","5","Strategic Environmental Assessment for Watershed Planning","Advance the use of the Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) process to provide development options that fit with the potential of watersheds for decision-making at the policy, plan and program levels.",""],[1,"144","6","Small- and Medium-Sized Water Storage Facility Cluster Development","Build clusters of small- and medium-sized water storage facilities by placing an emphasis on rural areas where there is still a lack of clean surface and ground water for consumption.",""],[1,"144","6","Community Small Weir Construction Support","Encourage communities to build small weirs.",""],[1,"144","6","Groundwater Development Feasibility Studies","Conduct feasibility studies which provide economically viable options for groundwater development to alleviate water shortages for consumption and agriculture in drought zones.",""],[1,"144","6","Water Diversion Feasibility Study","Similarly, study the feasibility of water diversion, from both domestic and international watersheds, allowing for balance, sustainability and the participation of all related parties in the watersheds.",""],[1,"145","1","Industrial Wastewater Treatment and Reuse","Wastewater should be treated and reused in some industries located in the main economic zones.",""],[1,"145","1","Sustainable Water Supply and Shortage Relief Measures","Ensure the sustainable use and provision of water to relieve water shortages and reduce the number of people affected.",""],[1,"153","2","Strategic Environmental Assessment for Water Resource Management","Demonstrate the use of Strategic Environmental Assessment (SEA) as an important tool for managing water resources at the sector and watershed levels when making decisions about policy, programs and plans.",""],[1,"153","2","Public Participation in Water Planning","Adoping SEA should ensure meaningful public participation in the process.",""],[1,"153","2","Pilot Watershed Selection for Resource Management","The 5 pilot watersheds will be selected based on prevailing development trends which evidence threats to the stability of natural resources and environment, leading to a major shift in people's livelihoods throughout the areas.",""],[1,"216","4","Northern Watershed Water Management Systems Development","(2) Developing water management systems in the main watershed areas of the Northern Region, namely the Ping, Wang, Yom, and Nan basins by: (2.1) developing and improving irrigation systems to supply adequate water for agricultural areas, (2.2) conducting water diversion projects, (2.3) constructing tunnels to deliver water, (2.4) creating water storage facilities according to each area's potential, and (2.5) developing water storage facilities outside the irrigated areas in the form of lagoons or \"monkey's cheeks\" in the Lower Northern Provincial Cluster.",""],[1,"219","2","Water Supply and Storage Capacity Improvement","Improving existing water supply facilities and natural water resources to enhance water storage capacity by improving existing water reservoirs, swamps, weirs, and natural water resources to increase water supply volume in the Central Northeastern, Lower Northeastern 1 and Lower Northeastern 2 provincial clusters which are key cultivation bases for the major economic crops of the region.",""],[1,"219","3","New Water Resources Development in River Basins","Developing new water resources in the Loei, Chi, and Mun river basins while constructing new water reservoirs (monkey's cheeks), weirs, and ponds in suitable agricultural areas by: (2.1) acquiring areas to develop new water resources, (2.2) developing water distribution systems to reach plantation areas in the dry season, and (2.3) protecting underground water from salinization.",""],[1,"221","4","Eastern Region Water Management Efficiency and Dispute Mitigation","To enhance the efficiency of water management systems and to mitigate disputes over water use among industries, agriculture, tourism and communities in the Eastern Region:",""],[1,"221","5","Water Source Improvement and Conservation","Improving and preserving existing water sources.",""],[1,"221","6","Additional Water Source Development","Providing and developing additional water sources to support the increasing demand due to economic expansion and the growing population.",""],[1,"221","7","Small Pond Construction for Agricultural Water Supply","Constructing small ponds in the Upper Central Region's agricultural areas in order to cope with water shortages.",""],[1,"224","2","Participatory Watershed Water Management","Integrating the participatory process of all stakeholders in water management in watershed areas.",""],[1,"231","10","Integrated Water Resource Management for Sustainable Development in the Northeast Region Project","Integrated Water Resource Management for Sustainable Development in the Northeast Region Project:",""],[1,"231","11","Water Storage Capacity Expansion and New Water Resource Development","increasing the capacity of existing water storage facilities and natural water resources, developing new water resources in the Loei, Chi, and Mun river basins, constructing small Kaem-Ling reservoirs in high potential areas for agriculture, promoting reforestation and encouraging participatory resources management in local communities.",""]],"40":[[1,"185","1","National Water Supply Infrastructure Efficiency Improvement","To expand and improve the efficiency of water supply infrastructure services nationwide, reduce non-revenue water, and establish an integrated management mechanism for water supply operations.",""],[1,"186","10","Water Supply Capacity Expansion and Non-Revenue Water Reduction","Target 6: Water Supply: to enhance tap water production capacity; to expand coverage of water supply services nationwide; and to reduce non-revenue water in the water transmission and distribution systems.",""],[1,"197","3","Regional Long-Term Water Supply Master Plans","Developing master plans regarding long-term water supply services at regional level, considering raw water sources, water production, water transmission system, water distribution system, and water demand forecast, to provide a framework to be integrated into the Strategic Plan on Thailand's Water Resources Management and to be a guideline for providing and expanding the waterworks service coverage.",""],[1,"197","4","Water Supply Capacity Expansion and Network Development","Expanding production capacity and water transmission and distribution networks to meet increasing water needs in the future, giving priority to regional areas with potential water sources but insufficient water supply services, tourist destinations, and special economic zones.",""],[1,"197","5","Village Clean Water and Water Supply System Development","Providing clean water and developing villages' water supply systems to meet basic needs in all villages, giving priority to villages without access to clean water or water supply systems but having operational readiness.",""],[1,"203","2","Ninth Bangkok Water Supply Improvement Project","The Ninth Bangkok Water Supply Improvement Project, carried out by the Metropolitan Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 7 years (2016- 2022).","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","3","Tenth Bangkok Water Supply Improvement Project","The Tenth Bangkok Water Supply Improvement Project, carried out by the Metropolitan Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 4 years (2018- 2021).","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","7","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2016","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2016, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2016-2018).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","10","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2017","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2017, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2017-2019).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","11","PWA Khon Kaen-Nam Phong Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 2-3","PWA Khon Kaen-Nam Phong Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 2- 3: 2017, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2017-2019).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","12","PWA Chonburi-Phanatnikhom-(Phan Thong)-(Tha Bun Mi) Waterworks Expansion Project Phase 1","PWA Chonburi-Phanatnikhom-(Phan Thong)-(Tha Bun Mi) Waterworks Expansion Project Phase 1: 2017, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2017-2019).","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"203","13","PWA Phuket Waterworks Expansion Project","PWA Phuket Waterworks Expansion Project 2017, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2017-2019).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","1","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2018","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2018, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2018-2020).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","2","PWA Samutsakhon Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 1-4","PWA Samutsakhon Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 1-4: 2018, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2018-2020).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","3","PWA Om Noi Waterworks Expansion Project","PWA Om Noi Waterworks Expansion Project 2018, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2018-2020).","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","5","PWA Samutsakhon Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 5-7","PWA Samutsakhon Waterworks Expansion Project, Phases 5-7: 2019, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2019-2021).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","6","PWA Udon Thani-Nong Khai Waterworks Expansion Project","PWA Udon Thani-Nong Khai Waterworks Expansion Project 2019, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2019-2021).","Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","7","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2020","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2020, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2020-2022).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","9","PWA Chiang Mai Waterworks Expansion Project 2020","PWA Chiang Mai Waterworks Expansion Project 2020, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2020- 2022).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","10","PWA Koh Samui Waterworks Expansion Project, Phase 2","PWA Koh Samui Waterworks Expansion Project, Phase 2: 2020, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2020-2022).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","11","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2021","PWA Waterworks Development Project 2021, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2021-2023).","Provincial Waterworks Authority | Ministry of Interior"],[1,"204","12","PWA Pattaya-Laem Chabang-Sriracha Waterworks Expansion Project","PWA Pattaya-Laem Chabang-Sriracha Waterworks Expansion Project 2021, carried out by the Provincial Waterworks Authority, Ministry of Interior, with a timeline of 3 years (2021-2023).","Ministry of Interior"]],"41":[[1,"25","3","Agricultural Knowledge and Innovation Support","it is important to support knowledge creation in agriculture, science and technology, and the co-creation of innovations that link with bio-based natural resources.",""],[1,"25","3","Sustainable Agriculture System Development","This focuses on developing the system of sustainable agriculture while expanding opportunities for farmers to access arable land.",""],[1,"25","3","Farmer Cooperative and Partnership Development","Individual farmers are encouraged to collaborate with each other in the form of cooperatives, partnerships and companies in order to achieve economies of scale, decrease underemployment, apply appropriate technology, and use market mechanisms to manage risk.",""],[1,"110","9","Bio-economy Development and Risk Management System","Promoting and developing the bio-economy as a new significant source of income, which requires the development of a risk management system and resilience in the face of climate change.",""],[1,"115","2","Agricultural Production Insurance Scheme","Farmers would benefit from a production insurance scheme that can help reduce risks from a loss of revenue due to crop damage and climate change.",""],[1,"116","1","Agricultural Water Storage and Watershed Management","developing and maintaining water storage systems for agriculture, and planning the crop planting systems to match the availability of water.",""],[1,"116","2","Climate-Resilient Agricultural Research and Knowledge Transfer","Therefore, the following policies should be emphasised: (1) supporting research into and development of factor inputs, including plants, animals, aquatic animals, growing technology and agricultural machinery, which are responsive to climate change and the enhancement of competitiveness; (2) conducting research and development on production technology and new agricultural processed products, which is accessible to farmers and entrepreneurs, in order to add value and diversify the attributes of the agricultural products; (3) developing models and processes of knowledge transfer in agricultural practice to farmers in order to change their production systems to become compatible with climate change and to realise the potential of their land.",""],[1,"118","1","Alternative Farming for Unsuitable Land Conversion","Converting the cultivation of unsuitable lands to other alternative farming practices.",""],[1,"118","1","Sustainable Livestock and Fishery Production Systems","Furthermore, promoting sustainable livestock and fishery production systems;",""],[1,"118","1","Agricultural Risk Management Mechanisms","setting up management mechanisms to reduce risks in agricultural production, including the Agricultural Futures Exchange, the Fund for Agricultural Crop Insurance, and the Early Warning System for Agriculture;",""],[1,"119","1","Agricultural Data and Disaster Warning System","creating an accurate and reliable database of demand and supply in agriculture that can be used in market-driven strategic planning.",""],[1,"130","7","Organic Agriculture Promotion and Pilot City Support","Promoting organic agriculture in order to expand the farming area and supporting pilot areas such as Yasothon Province as an 'Organic Agriculture City' by strengthening existing farmers and extending knowledge networks of successful farmer groups in the areas.",""],[1,"145","1","Agricultural Water Efficiency and Zoning Reform","Increase the efficiency of water usage and allocation per unit of production, thereby delivering higher value, both inside and outside the irrigation areas.",""],[1,"145","1","New Theory Agriculture Adoption Programme","Encourage farmers to adopt New Theory Agriculture into their day- to-day practices.",""],[1,"147","2","Sustainable Agriculture Transition Support","Support the transition towards sustainable agriculture.",""]],"42":[[1,"131","8","IUU Fishing Compliance Regulation","Regulating activities to comply with the preventive measures against Illegal Unreported and Unregulated (IUU) Fishing, continuously.",""],[1,"131","8","Fisheries Labor Protection Standards Enforcement","Managing and protecting labor in the fisheries sector according to pertinent standards and laws.",""],[1,"131","8","Fisheries Standards Harmonization for Trade","Adjusting the standards of fisheries, aquaculture, processing, transporting, and marketing to meet bilateral requirements and procedures, as well as realize the potential of marine and coastal resources, between Thailand and other trade partners.",""],[1,"220","5","Livestock Husbandry Promotion and Market Efficiency Improvement","(3) Promoting livestock husbandry, such as dairy and beef cattle in Saraburi and Ratchaburi, and pig, chicken, and duck farming in Ratchaburi, Nakhon Pathom, Chonburi, and Chachoengsao, in order to produce quality and safe products which meet the needs of international and domestic consumers by (3.1) enhancing farmers' ability to utilize modern production technologies as well as to select suitable livestock breeds, and (3.2) improving market management efficiency.",""],[1,"220","6","Coastal Fisheries and Marine Aquaculture Capacity Development","Developing capabilities in coastal areas along the Gulf of Thailand in fisheries and marine culture in Prachuapkhirikhan, Phetchaburi, Samut Songkram, Samut Sakorn, Samut Prakarn, Chonburi, Rayong, Chanthaburi, and Trat for the coastal natural resources to remain abundant and sustainable by: (4.1) conserving, restoring, and managing fishery resources, (4.2) adopting research and technological transfer on aquaculture management to improve quality and create value-added products, (4.3) promoting artisanal fisheries, and (4.4) supporting and developing the fishery business.",""],[1,"221","9","Rubber and Palm Oil Productivity Enhancement Programme","Strengthening the productivity of rubber and palm oil by: (1.1) promoting and supporting technologies to increase productivity, (1.2) conducting research to create value-added products, and (1.3) promoting small-scale farmers to be able sustainably to improve productivity, such as mixed agricultural practices and New Theory Agriculture, to accentuate the Southern Region as Thailand's key producer of rubber and palm oil in order to increase income and minimize the risk of fluctuating rubber and palm oil prices.",""],[1,"221","10","Southern Region Identity Fruit Export Development Programme","Developing and promoting the identity fruits of the Southern Region, such as coconut, cavendish banana, mangosteen, and durian, to meet international standards for export by: (2.1) improving technologies concerning harvesting and fresh produce storage, and (2.2) supporting research and development on fruit production",""],[1,"222","2","High-Potential Agro-Processing Area Development","Developing high-potential areas with efficient transportation infrastructure to be the agro-processing base by developing and promoting the establishment of: (3.1) a comprehensive palm oil processing industrial center as well as biodiesel production in Krabi and SuratThani, and (3.2) a rubber-processing industrial center in Songkhla.",""],[1,"222","3","Environmentally Friendly Shrimp and Marine Culture Upgrading","Upgrading the environmentally-friendly industries of shrimp culture and marine culture in Surat Thani, Nakorn Si Thammarat, Songkhla, and Pattani in order to promote the Southern Region as the main source of seafood products which meet international standards by: (4.1) supporting and promoting standardized farm management systems with efficient and hygienic production procedures in accordance with international standards, (4.2) developing market systems, and (4.3) enhancing the efficiency of seafood processing in order to create value-added products and generate income for local populations.",""],[1,"222","4","Srivichai Beef Cattle Development Programme","Supporting and promoting the development of Srivichai beef cattle in Chumphon, Surat Thani, Nakhon Si Thammarat, and Patthalung to become the production base for high-quality beef by: (5.1) improving breed development, (5.2) expanding farming areas, and (5.3) setting standards and developing beef product quality to support the tourist market as well as to be the key export products of the region.",""],[1,"233","1","Developing and Promoting the Production of Rubber Products in the Southern Region Project","5.9 Developing and Promoting the Production of Rubber Products in the Southern Region Project:",""],[1,"233","2","Rubber Product Diversification and Value-Addition Programme","developing and promoting the production of rubber with diversified products, higher value, as well as responding to market demands in order to generate sustainable income for both farmers and para-rubber processing entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"233","5","Increasing Palm Oil Productivity and Cultivation Areas Project","5.10 Increasing Palm Oil Productivity and Cultivation Areas in the Southern- Most Provinces Project:",""],[1,"233","6","Cultivated Area Expansion and Farmer Production Technology Support","developing and promoting the expansion of the cultivated areas, including provision of knowledge on production technology to farmers in order to increase production efficiency and the quality of palm oil and crops to be used as raw material responding to investment demands in the Southern border provinces.",""],[1,"233","9","Srivijaya Beef Cattle Industry Development Project","Developing the Srivijaya Beef Cattle Industry in the Southern Region (Thai Gulf) Project:",""],[1,"233","10","Srivijaya Beef Cattle Production and Processing Development","promoting and developing production and processing of high-quality Srivijaya beef cattle, which is a local strain of the Southern region (Thai Gulf), responding to the needs of the tourism markets in the Southern Region, and being strategic local commodities to be exported by using new technology and innovations ranging from breeding to processing and distribution and defining geographical indication to gain international acceptance.",""],[1,"234","3","Environmentally-Friendly Coastal Aquaculture and Shrimp-Farming Industry Development Project","5.13 The Environmentally-Friendly Coastal Aquaculture and Shrimp-Farming Industry Development Project:",""],[1,"234","4","Farm Management System Development","developing farm management systems",""],[1,"234","4","Efficient and Hygienic Agricultural Production Improvement","improving the production process to be efficient and hygienic according to international standards, rules and regulations",""],[1,"234","4","Agricultural Market System Development","developing market systems",""],[1,"234","4","Marine Aquaculture Product Processing Promotion","promoting marine aquacultural product processing in order to create higher value and generate incomes for local populations",""],[1,"249","12","Surath Red Goat Breed Development Programme","Development of the Surath Red Goat Breed to strengthen the sub-regional food production base (2017-2021).",""]],"43":[[1,"26","3","Border Economic Zone and Inland Production Linkage","Economic development along the border lines and within border economic zones should be connected with the production sector in the inner parts of the country.",""],[1,"28","2","Border Economic Area Management","enabling the sound management of border economic areas to attain sustainable growth and competitiveness",""],[1,"70","1","Border Town and Border Economic Zone Development","Thailand still has to develop border towns and border economic zones along the economic corridors to link with neighboring countries, by conducting feasibility studies, integrating development plans on joint border economic zones with neighboring countries, and formulating investment strategies, human resources and skilled labor development schemes to prepare for economic zone and border economic zone development.",""],[1,"84","6","Regional Distribution of Production and Service Bases","Production and service bases should be distributed to different regions across the country in order to reduce inequality.",""],[1,"109","2","New Economic Zones and Corridors Development","Moreover, the strategy focuses on the use of biological resources; the support of value chain linkages; the development of new economic zones and corridors; the integration of the service sector and the trade sector, coupled with preparing the service sector to underpin freer competition; the enhancement of SME competitiveness; and the establishment of a culture for entrepreneurs to produce and sell by responding to rapid",""],[1,"228","13","Link Key Economic Sectors to the Community Economy","Connect the key economic sectors (industry, services, and tourism) to the community economy (SMEs, community enterprises, and social businesses).",""],[1,"229","4","Border Town Development for Urban Expansion and Economic Growth","Develop border towns to be able to accommodate urban area expansion and economic growth.",""],[1,"229","6","Sectoral Activity Upgrading Program","Upgrade activities in manufacturing, trade, logistics, services, and the tourism sectors to be in line with each area's location, resources, identity, culture, and opportunities.",""],[1,"229","9","Community Enterprise and Local Business Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capacity of community enterprise and local businesses.",""],[1,"237","2","Economic Corridor Connectivity and Community Development","It is also an opportunity for Thailand to emerge as a gateway to the east and the west, expand physical connectivity to enhance economic zones and community development along the economic corridors to boost the level of competitiveness and distribute wealth to communities, cities, and provinces along the economic corridors, and other key areas in the vicinity of the country.",""],[1,"244","7","Border Area Development for Production Network Linkages","To uplift the competitiveness of the Thai private sector in providing and managing logistics services, and carry out border area development to link the border production networks with the rest of the country and neighboring countries.",""],[1,"246","4","SME Competitiveness and Economic Corridor Support","To boost the competitiveness of Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs), expand the production network along the economic corridors with neighboring countries, improve the workforce, and minimize the social impact of economic corridor development in the six GMS countries.",""],[1,"248","4","Border Area Development and Cross-Border Production Cluster Initiative","To develop potential border areas with neighboring countries with support from various development initiatives.",""],[1,"251","1","MSME Competitiveness and Opportunity Enhancement","enhance competitiveness and opportunities of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs);",""]],"44":[[1,"156","5","Security Cooperation with Allied Countries","To strengthen security cooperation with allied countries in support of maintaining peace and national interests.",""],[1,"158","1","International Security Cooperation","Thailand will collaborate and cooperate on security issues with ASEAN member countries, allied countries, and various other countries in preventing threats of various forms, together with maintaining the national interests:",""],[1,"160","5","International Cooperation for Transnational Security Threats","Take a proactive role by making use of international cooperation frameworks, both at regional and multilateral levels, to protect the national interests of Thailand, together with strengthening, exchanging, and studying best practices, and collaborating to deal with transnational security threats such as drugs problems, terrorism, illegal immigration, human trafficking, cyber-crime, disasters, plague, pestilence, emerging and recurring diseases, and other public health emergencies.",""],[1,"160","8","Foreign Relations Cooperation for National Interests","Balance foreign relations to facilitate, promote and protect the national interests, and the economic and social development of the country, by developing cooperation with neighboring countries and ASEAN member states, and allied countries, in intelligence exchange and joint proactive action to prevent, troubleshoot and reduce the",""],[1,"161","2","Border Security Strategic Partnerships and Cooperation","Strengthen trust with neighboring countries and promote cooperation in security management along the borders to resolve existing problems and promote \"a border of cooperation\" along common borders with neighboring countries by developing strategic partnerships on border security to prevent illegal migration and immigration, boost economic development along the borders, and strengthen public-level relationships.",""]],"45":[[1,"223","7","Infrastructure Development for Domestic and Thailand-Malaysia Connectivity","Developing infrastructure to improve both domestic and Thailand-Malaysia connectivity.",""],[1,"228","9","Integrated Transportation Infrastructure Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capacity of every mode of transportation infrastructure to be integrated and interconnected, such as international airports (Suvarnabhumi, Donmuang, and U-Tapao), roads, railways, and waterways in order to support increasing activities in the area and connect the ESB to the global market.",""],[1,"229","3","Soft Infrastructure and Border Station Upgrading","Improve soft infrastructure and border stations to facilitate cross-border investment and transportation.",""],[1,"230","7","Eastern Seaboard Transportation Infrastructure Development Plan","Transportation Infrastructure Development Plan in the Eastern Seaboard Area",""],[1,"237","2","Sub-regional and Regional Connectivity Enhancement","The next five-year period will be fundamentally crucial in pushing forward institutional connectivity at the sub-regional and regional levels to implementation, extending linkages across borders under various sub-regional and regional frameworks, and reducing Non-Tariff Barriers (NTBs), while also improving physical infrastructure both domestically and internationally with respect to infrastructure investment schemes.",""],[1,"239","11","Regional Connectivity Hub Development Framework","Establish a clear timeframe equipped with enabling regulations to become a regional connectivity hub, and expand economic and social opportunities to the provinces and local areas by connecting external economic corridors with domestic spatial development by:",""],[1,"239","12","Transport and Logistics Connectivity Scheme","Implementing the transport and logistics connectivity scheme with ASEAN and other sub-regions, in alignment with the strategies and development plans of the neighboring countries, Great Powers, and the newly emerging economies of the world.",""],[1,"240","2","Transport Network Efficiency and Connectivity Development","Covering land (road and rail), air, maritime, and coastal transport, development of border checkpoints, and border procedure facilitation.",""],[1,"240","2","Cross-Border Trade Facilitation and Border Checkpoint Development","development of border checkpoints, and border procedure facilitation.",""],[1,"240","2","ASEAN and Sub-Regional Transport Linkage Enhancement","Assuring linkages among economic areas in the sub-region and between sub-regions in ASEAN, and domestic linkages that support spatial, regional, and urban development.",""],[1,"240","3","Cross-Border Transport Agreement Implementation","Implementing the Cross-Border Transport Agreement (CBTA), which all the GMS member countries have ratified, comprising the implementation of the pilot scheme at the Thailand-Lao PDR-Vietnam border at the Mukdahan-Savannakhet checkpoint, operations between Thailand-Cambodia at the Aranyaprathet-Poipet checkpoint, operations between Thailand-Lao PDR-China at the Chiang Khong-Huay Xai checkpoint, negotiations with Myanmar to commence a CBTA at the Mae Sot-Myawaddy and Mae Sai-Tachileik checkpoints, and to establish the Phu Nam Ron-Dawei and Sinkhon-Marid checkpoints, the Thailand-Myanmar bilateral cross-border agreement, and the Thailand-Cambodia bilateral cross-border agreement.",""],[1,"240","5","Transportation and Logistics Linkage Development for Export Gateway and Regional Operations","Establishing transportation and logistics linkages between resources and production bases throughout the international production chain, ensuring a standardized and efficient export gateway; fostering economic linkages between large economic zones in neighboring countries and Thailand's border and domestic economic zones, based on Thailand's interdisciplinary services and ideal location to establish regional operation centers or parent companies.",""],[1,"244","7","Cross-Border Transport and Logistics Connectivity Improvement","to advance seamless and full connectivity in the six GMS countries, improve transport and logistics services to be effective and meet international standards, and streamline regulations on the cross-border transport of goods and people under the CBTA.",""],[1,"245","2","Support for Implementing the GMS Cross-Border Transport Agreement Action Plan","Support for implementing the Action Plan for the GMS Cross-Border Transport Agreement (CBTA).",""],[1,"245","6","Cross-Border Goods Transport Facilitation","To enhance economic competitiveness by facilitating cross-border goods transport to increase the capacity of the Thai private sector in logistics management.",""],[1,"246","4","Regional Connectivity and Economic Corridor Development","To advance connectivity between Thailand and the economic zones in the six GMS countries, ASEAN, East Asia, South Asia, as well as the 21 st Century Maritime Silk Road.",""],[1,"246","5","Southern Economic Corridor Development","The Southern Economic Corridor Development, including: (1) Dawei Special Economiz Zone; (2) Dawei deep seaport to link with Laem Chabang and Map Ta Phut deep seaports; (3) four-lane highway at the Thai-Myanmar border to link with Dawei Special Economic Zone; (4) road from Chedi Sam Ong-Phaya Tong Su-Thanphyuzayat border crossing point, and customs facility; (5) dual-track train along the Southern Economic Corridor (Laem Chabang-Kanchanaburi); (6) highway network at Nong Ian border crossing point, Aranyaprathet, Sa Kaew, customs facility and road to Highway 5 at Steung Bot, Poipet, Banteay Meanchey, Cambodia; (7) operations between Thailand-Myanmar and Thailand- Cambodia under the Cross-Border Transport Agreement (CBTA); (8) SME development along the economic corridors; (9) human resources development and labor improvement along the economic corridors; and (10) social impact reduction of economic corridor development in the GMS.",""],[1,"246","6","East-West Economic Corridor Development","The East-West Economic Corridor Development, including: (1) the Second Thai-Myanmar Friendship Bridge (Mae Sot-Myawaddy), and customs facility at Mae Sot-Myawaddy border crossing point; (2) electricity grid development in Yanggon, Myanmar; (3) bridge over the Mekong River at Beung Kan-Paksan; (4) bridge over the Mekong River at Ubon Ratchathani-Salawan; (5) high voltage power transmission poles and cables between Thailand-Lao PDR to handle 500 kilowatts; (6) operations between Thailand-Lao PDR-Vietnam under the Cross-Border Transport Agreement (CBTA);",""],[1,"247","2","North-South Economic Corridor Development","The North-South Economic Corridor Development, including: (1) Den Chai-Chiang Rai train; (2) power transmission cables to handle 115 kilowatts, and Namtong-Houay Xai power station in Lao PDR; (3) Hongsa-Ban Chiang Mai road; (4) operations between Thailand-Lao PDR-China under the Cross-Border Transport Agreement (CBTA); (5) SME development along the economic corridors; (6) human resources and labor improvement along the economic corridors; and (7) social impact reduction of economic corridor development in the GMS.",""],[1,"247","4","Cross-Border Infrastructure and Transport Connectivity Programme","to improve domestic infrastructure and transport networks to link with neighboring countries, provide cross-border trade and investment facilitation, and make use of the border areas as gateways to international trade.",""],[1,"247","5","Sadao CIQ and Border Post Facilities Construction","Construction of the new Sadao CIQ in Songkhla (2016- 2019), and construction of Sadao Border Post facilities in Songkhla (arrival) (2016-2017).",""],[1,"247","9","Bu Ke Ta Customs House Upgrade","Upgrading of Bu Ke Ta customs house in Narathiwas (2016-",""],[1,"247","10","New Tak Bai CIQ Construction","Construction of the new Tak Bai CIQ in Narathiwas (near the new bridge over the Kolok River) (2017-2019).",""],[1,"247","12","Second Kolok River Bridge Construction","Construction of the second bridge over the Kolok River in Sungai Kolok, Narathiwas-Rantau Panjang, Kelantan (2016-2018).",""]],"46":[[1,"28","3","Support for Thai Overseas Investment","Thailand will use strategic approaches that support Thai entrepreneurs to invest overseas, which will help to expand the value chain in ASEAN, boost competitiveness,",""],[1,"29","1","Trade and Investment Opportunity Expansion","and create more trade and investment opportunities, particularly in CLMV and ASEAN.",""],[1,"29","1","ASEAN and Non-ASEAN Cooperation Framework Utilization","Thailand will utilize the benefits to be derived from cooperation frameworks with the ASEAN community as well as with non-ASEAN countries, and will highlight its creative role in global fora by supporting the country's efforts to achieve the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).",""],[1,"35","4","Competitive Trade and Investment Strategy Development","Thailand must therefore set more precise competitive strategies as well as cooperation strategies between countries, including the marketing bases in both trade and investment in the sub-region, region and within the global economy, especially in those areas of production and services in which Thailand has the capacity to compete.",""],[1,"35","4","Foreign Investment Attraction Policy","All this would take advantage of: (1) the country's strategic location, using policy to attract foreign investment and to promote Thailand as an International Trading",""],[1,"75","2","Trade and Investment Liberalization and Facilitation Programs","programs that support trade and investment liberalization, reduce barriers, and facilitate trade, with a particular focus on multilateral trade, achievement of the Bogor Goals (trade and investment liberalization by 2020), the establishment of the Free Trade Area of the Asia-Pacific (FTAAP), and global value chain cooperation",""],[1,"78","1","Regional Cooperation and Connectivity Promotion","Thailand should promote the role it plays in diverse cooperation frameworks to boost connectivity in all forms to further expand opportunities in trade and investment in the region, and integrate the regional production chain to the global level.",""],[1,"84","2","International Connectivity and Trade Promotion Initiative","To strengthen the connectivity between Thailand and other countries at the sub-regional, regional, and international levels.",""],[1,"85","2","Export and Investment Expansion to Regional Markets","The rate of investment and exports from Thailand to sub-regional, regional, and ASEAN countries should increase.",""],[1,"212","3","Support Thai Entrepreneurs in Global Production Networks","Encourage Thai entrepreneurs to participate in global production networks, particularly in competent industries such as Thailand's R&D Hub.",""],[1,"237","1","Liberalized Trade and Investment Policy Reform","promoting liberalized, open, and transparent trade and investment policies to ensure a conducive business environment",""],[1,"237","1","New Market Identification Strategy","implementing a strategic approach to identify new markets",""],[1,"237","1","Overseas Investment Promotion for Thai Entrepreneurs","encouraging Thai entrepreneurs to invest overseas",""],[1,"239","10","Trade Agreement Utilization and Market Diversification Strategy","Fully utilize existing economic agreements, strengthen cooperation with emerging markets both bilaterally and multilaterally, and employ a proactive strategy in public and private partnership to identify new markets and trade partners.",""],[1,"241","4","Trade and Investment Promotion for a Trading Nation","Increasing the return benefits from capital, knowledge, and technology in the production and services in which Thailand specializes, and supporting Thailand to become a trading nation.",""],[1,"241","4","Entrepreneur Support and Workforce Internationalization","Supporting Thai entrepreneurs in production and trade, internationalizing the Thai workforce, creating smart traders with the use of technology in regional trade management, and advocating demand-oriented trade by:",""],[1,"241","5","Thai Entrepreneurial Capacity Building for International Standards","building the Thai entrepreneurial capacity to meet international standards to promote cross-border businesses",""],[1,"242","4","Target Market Identification for Economic Cooperation","Expanding economic cooperation by identifying target markets by taking their trade importance and level of economic growth or development into consideration.",""],[1,"243","3","Active Participation in Regional Trade Frameworks","Actively monitoring and taking part in newly established frameworks, such as the RCEP and TPP.",""],[1,"243","3","Feasibility Studies for New Free Trade Areas","Conducting feasibility studies to establish free trade areas with new trade partners to open up trade and investment opportunities in the global market.",""],[1,"244","2","Trade and Investment Externality Mitigation Mechanisms","By: (1) preparing mechanisms to minimize negative externalities from trade and investment policy to prevent further inequality and unfairness as a result of free trade and investment policies and international cooperation;",""],[1,"244","3","Support and Encourage Thai Overseas Investment Initiative","Initiative to support and encourage Thai entrepreneurs to invest overseas:",""],[1,"244","4","Cross-Border Investment Facilitation for Thai Entrepreneurs","To support and encourage Thai entrepreneurs to invest in the neighboring countries, in the sub-region, and in ASEAN by streamlining regulations, and supporting value chain linkages in competitive production areas and services to improve Thailand's target industries in the sub-region and ASEAN.",""],[1,"244","4","Border Area Business Expansion Initiative","To expand business opportunities for Thai entrepreneurs in border areas, particularly along the economic corridors.",""],[1,"248","14","Halal Products and Services Cooperation and Market Access Initiative","To strengthen cooperation and raise the quality of Halal products and services in Thailand and neighboring countries to gain international recognition.",""],[1,"248","14","Halal Export Promotion Initiative","To support Halal products and services to enter the global market.",""],[1,"250","6","Food Sector Trade Barrier Removal","To remove trade barriers in the food sector to promote regional food trade, increase agricultural productivity, enhance farmers' competitiveness, support local farmers to enter the global value chain, and increase income for Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), following the Boracay Action Agenda 2016-2020.",""],[1,"250","6","MSME Participation in Services and Global Value Chains","To increase MSMEs participation in services and the global value chain, with the APEC Strategy for Green and Sustainable MSMEs.",""]],"47":[[1,"67","3","Technical and Financial Assistance for Sub-Regional Development","Thailand intends to play a leading role in economic and social development in the sub-region, acting as a development partner offering technical and financial assistance in education, public health, and the environment.",""],[1,"67","3","Social Cooperation and Cultural Exchange Promotion","Moreover, Thailand promotes social cooperation and cultural exchange, provides assistance on major infrastructure development, such as roads, rails, energy, and deep seaports, and supports potential state enterprises and the private sector to invest in specialized businesses.",""],[1,"67","3","Regional Infrastructure Assistance Programme","Moreover, Thailand promotes social cooperation and cultural exchange, provides assistance on major infrastructure development, such as roads, rails, energy, and deep seaports, and supports potential state enterprises and the private sector to invest in specialized businesses.",""],[1,"67","3","Support for Specialized Business Investment","Moreover, Thailand promotes social cooperation and cultural exchange, provides assistance on major infrastructure development, such as roads, rails, energy, and deep seaports, and supports potential state enterprises and the private sector to invest in specialized businesses.",""],[1,"68","1","3Cs Strategy for Sub-Regional Economic Development","The program focuses on economic and social development to promote sub-regional growth, narrow the economic development gap, and raise the standard of living and the well-being of peoples through economic zone development, competitiveness enhancement, and community relations, or altogether the 3Cs Strategy (Connectivity, Competitiveness, and Community).",""],[1,"68","1","Cross-Border Infrastructure Support to Neighboring Countries","Key development progress in Thailand includes: (1) providing assistance to neighboring countries on infrastructure development such as Highway 11 in the Lao PDR, the Tha Na Lang- Vientiane railway in the Lao PDR, the Tin Ka Ying Nong-Kawkareik road link in Myanmar with assistance from the Thai government, renovation of the First Thailand-Myanmar Friendship Bridge over the Moei River, commencement of the Second Thailand-Myanmar Friendship Bridge, opening of the Fourth Thailand-Lao Friendship Bridge over the Mekong River at Chiang Khong-Huayxai, the Thailand-Lao PDR-China railway and high-speed train development;",""],[1,"68","1","GMS Human Resources and Sectoral Knowledge Sharing Support","providing assistance to other GMS countries on human resources development, and experience-sharing in agriculture, public health, energy, and others;",""],[1,"68","1","GMS Regional Coordination Office Hosting and Focal Point Role","becoming a center for the GMS Mekong Tourism Coordinating Office (MTCO), the Regional Power Coordination Center (RPCC), and a focal point for cooperation on environment, agriculture, and railways in the future.",""],[1,"69","2","IMT-GT Priority Connectivity Projects","The IMT-GT is attempting to implement priority connectivity projects to expand sub-regional linkages for the IMT-GT to accomplish connectivity according to the Master Plan on ASEAN Connectivity.",""],[1,"69","3","IMT-GT Sub-Regional Cooperation Implementation Blueprint","With the abovementioned Implementation Blueprint, the IMT-GT also focuses on six areas of cooperation: (1) transport and infrastructure development to promote sub-regional connectivity in economic zones along corridors and inner areas; (2) trade and investment to create high value within the sub-region and between sub-regions through cross-border production linkages, such as border economic zones; (3) tourism that promotes unique touristic products to accommodate domestic and international markets; (4) Halal products and services that support Halal certification, Halal brand development, and joint markets; (5) human resources development to strengthen human skills in all sectors; and (6) agriculture, agro industry, and the environment that support value-added products while promoting sustainable development.",""],[1,"72","2","ASEAN Connectivity Post-2015 Agenda","The post-2015 Agenda for ASEAN Connectivity is formulated to carry on operations under the Master Plan on ASEAN Connectivity (MPAC), with five new cooperation areas: (1) sustainable infrastructure; (2) digital innovation; (3) seamless logistics; (4) regulatory excellence; and (5) people mobility.",""],[1,"72","3","ASEAN Joint Agreements Implementation","Joint agreements have to be implemented.",""],[1,"73","1","International Measures and Transnational Labor Management","the focus is placed on implementing international measures, managing transnational labor, and improving skills in English and the languages of the neighboring countries.",""],[1,"75","2","APEC Technical Cooperation and Policy Learning Programs","programs that promote technical cooperation, mutual learning, and sharing of experiences and best practices, particularly those regarding rules and regulations, international standards, enforcement, efficiency and transparency in the public sector, and environmental regulations and standards",""],[1,"75","2","Sectoral Development Cooperation Programs","programs for sectoral development, including the food industry, science and technology cooperation, growth and sustainable development in the tourism industry, human resources development, natural disaster warning and response, clean energy consumption, corruption of all forms in public and private sector, and infectious disease prevention",""],[1,"78","1","Regional Cooperation and Connectivity Promotion","Thailand should promote the role it plays in diverse cooperation frameworks to boost connectivity in all forms to further expand opportunities in trade and investment in the region, and integrate the regional production chain to the global level.",""],[1,"85","2","International Norm-Setting and Cooperation Initiative","Thailand, alongside other countries, should collaboratively determine and set international norms, and become a vital partner in sub-regional, regional, and international cooperation.",""],[1,"237","1","Sub-regional and Regional Cooperation Expansion","promoting collaboration with countries in the sub-region, region, and beyond",""],[1,"237","1","Innovation Development through International Cooperation","The strategy also calls for innovation development based on various cooperation initiatives, such as in regulation, accountable and transparent government, public sector reform under APEC (Asia- Pacific Economic Cooperation), labor skills development to meet international standards, measures and best practices for eco-friendly development, and human resources development.",""],[1,"238","1","Alignment of National Development with International Standards and Agreements","Efforts as a member country include showing a strong commitment to and compliance with standards at all levels, and aligning country development with international practices and agreements, such as the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), the CO2 emissions protocol, aviation laws, human rights treaties, and international labor standards.",""],[1,"238","1","Domestic Mechanism Adjustment for Regional Integration","The Twelfth Plan focuses on adjusting domestic mechanisms towards integration, promoting creative, fair, and inclusive mechanisms at the sub-regional and regional levels, and refining Thailand's role with our neighbors in sub-regional and regional development.",""],[1,"241","1","Regional Cooperation and Investment Attraction for R&D","Providing educational, financial, health, and logistics services, and attracting investment to contribute to research and development.",""],[1,"241","3","Joint Production Network Development","Establishing a joint production network to deliver services, distribution, and natural resource and labor allocation that benefit all countries.",""],[1,"241","3","Future Joint Production and Services Clusters","Possibly inaugurating joint production and services clusters in the future once all the countries have reached the same level.",""],[1,"241","3","Sub-Regional Production Chain Market Orientation","Product development in the production chain with neighboring countries should mainly take into account the supplying of the sub-regional and target markets.",""],[1,"241","4","ASEAN Economic Community and RCEP Market Integration","Playing an active role in the ASEAN Economic Community Post-2015 to support a single market and production base, and utilizing the RCEP to become a new investment and export base.",""],[1,"241","5","Technical Assistance for Transport and Logistics Regulation and Human Resources","Acting as a development partner in providing technical assistance to neighboring countries to help improve regulations and human resources in the transportation and logistics sectors",""],[1,"242","4","Regional Development Finance and Technical Assistance","Building trust, and generating mutual benefits by providing finance, techniques, and technical assistance to neighboring countries.",""],[1,"242","5","Bilateral and Multilateral Cooperation for Regional Stability","Strengthening cooperation with various countries, bilaterally and multilaterally, to increase stability in the sub-region, region, and beyond.",""],[1,"242","7","Development Cooperation for Connectivity, R&D, and Human Resource Development","Providing assistance to developing economies to help strengthen connectivity, research and development, and human resources development.",""],[1,"243","2","Balanced Foreign Policy and International Connectivity Strategy","Defining Thailand's foreign policy alternatives on the global stage to maintain balanced relations with the Great Powers in the region and the world.",""],[1,"243","5","Alignment with Regional and Global Regulations and International Practices","Adapting to the regulations and mechanisms at the regional and global levels, as well as international practices, such as anti-slavery and human trafficking treaties, aviation laws and regulations specified by the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), Trafficking in Persons Report (TIP Report), Illegal, Unreported, and Unregulated (IUU) Fishing, the United Nations' 21st Conference of the Parties (COP21), ASEAN Mutual Recognition Agreement (MRA), and Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) to support Thailand's creative and influential role in the region and the world.",""],[1,"243","7","Domestic Mechanism Review for International Cooperation","Reviewing domestic mechanisms to promote international cooperation in all aspects and at all levels, based on mutual understanding of Thai agencies on common goals and strategies.",""],[1,"243","7","Team Thailand Coordination Framework","Advocating operations under \"Team Thailand\" to ensure consistency and",""],[1,"244","2","Public Awareness for Regional Cooperation Benefits","By: (3) changing attitudes, and creating awareness and understanding among Thai people to realize mutual benefits derived from sub-regional and regional cooperation, and under other cooperation initiatives in a wider aspect.",""],[1,"245","6","Sub-Regional Labor Skills and Capacity Development","To strengthen the agricultural production network between Thailand and neighboring countries, enhance labor skills and capacity in the sub-region, and promote tourism for Thailand to emerge as a regional tourist hub.",""],[1,"245","12","Greater Mekong Sub-region SDG Implementation Initiative","To implement:",""]],"48":[[1,"28","3","Institutional Linkage and Border Regulation Streamlining","In the next 5 years, the focus will be on defining and streamlining institutional linkages and regulations at the implementation level and in border areas, reducing non-tariff barriers on trade and investment, advancing physical infrastructure development within the country and with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"68","1","Cross-Border Trade Agreement Implementation","implementation of the Cross-Border Trade Agreements (CBTA) at Mukdahan-Savannakhet between Thailand and the Lao PDR, Aranyaprathet-Poipet between Thailand and Cambodia, and Chiang Khong-Huayxai-Boten-Bohan between Thailand, the Lao PDR and China;",""],[1,"72","2","ASEAN Trade Facilitation Measures","ASEAN has to expedite the measures to facilitate trade, such as transport and customs measures, the ASEAN single window, ASEAN Rules of Origins, trade database, and the product mutual recognition agreement.",""],[1,"72","3","Regulatory Liberalization Reform","Thailand has to revise regulations that oppose liberalization, such as for free labor movement, financial liberalization, and capital flow.",""],[1,"72","3","Services and Financial Sector Liberalization Preparation","Preparations for liberalization in the services and the financial sectors should be completed.",""],[1,"72","3","Research and Development and ASEAN Product Promotion","The production sector has to advance research and development to produce unique and quality products with added value, promote ASEAN products, and address market needs to increase the income of the country.",""],[1,"74","2","Tariff and Non-Tariff Trade Facilitation Measures","Thus, Thailand should prepare both tariff and non-tariff measures, such as trade facilitation to support products with comparative advantage - machine and electric appliances, rubber and plastic, air conditioners, ribbed smoked sheets, and polymer ethylene.",""],[1,"76","1","Regional Common Standards Harmonization","action plans among the member countries will lead to setting up common standards in the region, such as customs procedures, and industrial product standards and certification.",""],[1,"77","1","RCEP Regulatory Review and Coordination Study","Therefore, Thailand has to conduct a study to review threats and opportunities under RCEP, examine the benefits and ramifications the country will experience, and at the same time raising the country's capacity to review regulations and ensure coordination among them to better prepare for more market opening.",""],[1,"77","1","Regulatory Review for Market Opening","Thailand should review rules and regulations to ensure their practicality, especially drug patents, and plant and animal patents.",""],[1,"77","1","Competition and Private Sector Competitiveness Reform","The country should also remove barriers to competition and enhance the competitiveness of the private sector, improve the labor force to meet international standards, strengthen SMEs in clusters, and advance the services and investment sector.",""]],"49":[[1,"124","1","Hospitality and Tourism Skills Development","developing the skills of personnel in the hospitality and tourism sector, organizing training for foreign tour guides nationwide;",""],[1,"124","2","Tourism Law and Standards Update","Updating tourism-related laws, and setting and enforcing tourism standards by: (1) expediting the updating of the laws and regulations that will facilitate the future development of the industry and services by emphasizing the integration of principles and the enforcement of laws and regulations that are consistent with one another in order to facilitate and develop the production and services sectors effectively in the defined direction; (2) reviewing, updating, and developing laws, rules, regulations and policy relating to sport tourism, hospitality and tourism business in the country according to situation, and bringing laws relating to Thai tourism up to international standards; and (3) promoting tourism accessibility to every group of people according to their personal rights.",""],[1,"124","3","Tourism Management Restructuring Mechanism","Restructuring tourism management as a mechanism for managing and setting a clear direction for development by focusing on the participation of all sectors - the public sector, private sector, academia, and the civil society sector - in raising the level of the country's tourism industry to create balanced and stable growth, as well as fair and equal benefit incidence.",""],[1,"136","2","Tourism Carrying Capacity Management Study","attempts to control and limit the number of tourists to fit with the capacity of ecosystems have led to the initiation of this study in order to evaluate its appropriateness and to acquire effective tourism management mechanisms.",""],[1,"136","2","Environmental Awareness for Travelers","The study will also raise environmental awareness among all travelers.",""],[1,"136","5","Improving Human Resources and Entrepreneurship in Tourism Program","Improving Human Resources and Entrepreneurship in Tourism Program:",""]],"50":[[1,"193","5","Electric Vehicle Charging Infrastructure Initialization","The government should also have a clear set of policies and implementing measures to initialize the first stage of electricity infrastructure for electric vehicles (EV), in order to lay the ground for future EV expansion.",""],[1,"194","1","Smart Grid Technology Development","development of smart grid technology covering all stages in the process, whether it be generation, transmission, distribution, or consumption, so that the results can be further developed to be commercially viable.",""],[1,"202","1","Pilot Building Energy Management Systems and Grid Flexibility Projects","Pilot projects for building energy management systems (BEMSs), demand response measures, micro grids, and energy storage systems, carried out by the Ministry of Energy and the Office of the Energy Regulatory Commission, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Energy | Office of the Energy Regulatory Commission"]],"51":[[1,"132","7","National Automotive and Tyre Test Center Establishment","The establishment of the National Automotive and Tyre Test Center will initially focus on testing to UN R117 standard, and will expand for testing other tyre standards and automotive parts in the further phases.",""]],"52":[[1,"184","5","National Digital Services Expansion and Cybersecurity Development","To increase the efficiency and coverage of digital services to be country-wide at reasonable cost, as well as encourage new digital businesses and innovations while developing appropriate cyber security systems and ensuring consumers' rights.",""],[1,"186","5","National High-Speed Internet Expansion","to expand the coverage of high-speed internet services to be countrywide",""],[1,"186","5","Digital Business and Innovation Promotion","to increase the number of digital businesses and innovations",""],[1,"186","5","Cybersecurity System Upgrading","to improve cyber security systems to be in compliance with international standards in order to tackle online threats",""],[1,"195","8","Telecommunications Infrastructure Improvement","Improve the country's telecommunications infrastructure coverage and efficiency by:",""],[1,"196","1","National Broadband and Basic Telecommunications Coverage Expansion","Working to achieve country-wide coverage of high-speed broadband networks, wired or wireless, as well as ensuring basic telecommunications services.",""],[1,"196","2","International Telecommunications Network Development","Developing international telecommunication networks, including international submarine cables, satellites, and terrestrial networks connecting ASEAN countries.",""],[1,"196","3","Shared Use of Telecommunications and Mass Communication Infrastructure","Facilitating shared use of telecommunication and mass communication infrastructure while devising a clear plan to utilize unused frequencies as well as frequencies near the end of their concession agreements, in order to ensure optimal utilization of resources, reduce redundancy, and decrease government spending.",""],[1,"202","7","High Speed Packet Access (HSPA) Project","High Speed Packet Access (HSPA) Project, carried out by CAT Telecom Public Company Limited, with a timeline of 13 years (2013-2025).",""],[1,"202","9","High-Speed Broadband Expansion","The Expansion of High-Speed Broadband (1.6 million ports), carried out by TOT Public Company Limited, with a timeline of 3 years (2017-2019).",""],[1,"202","10","High-Speed Internet Telecommunications Network Development Plan","Development plans for a high-speed internet telecommunications network, carried out by the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Digital Economy and Society"]],"53":[[1,"5","3","Research and Development Investment Expansion","Thailand must accelerate the improvement of fundamental strategic development factors in all respects, such as: increasing investment in research and development; developing science, technology, and innovation; this has to be accomplished together with accelerating the enhancement of labor skills, both of new entrants to the labor market and existing workers, in order to be compatible",""],[1,"5","3","Science, Technology, and Innovation Development","Thailand must accelerate the improvement of fundamental strategic development factors in all respects, such as: increasing investment in research and development; developing science, technology, and innovation; this has to be accomplished together with accelerating the enhancement of labor skills, both of new entrants to the labor market and existing workers, in order to be compatible",""],[1,"7","2","Research and Development Investment","Thailand faces a severe challenge to accelerate the development of various strategic fundamental factors, including: investing in research and development;",""],[1,"7","2","Science, Technology, and Innovation Development","developing science, technology and innovation;",""],[1,"7","2","Creativity and Innovation for a New Value-Added Economy","Accordingly, the Twelfth Plan focuses on incorporating creativity and innovation to generate a new value-added economy, including manufacturing processes and forms, new products and services, technology changes, and business patterns.",""],[1,"7","2","Knowledge-Based Development Strategy","Therefore, development in the next five years will focus on knowledge-based development which results from the use of wisdom, skills, science, technology, research and development, and innovation in all aspects of development.",""],[1,"12","2","Expansion of Knowledge, Technology, and Innovation as Core Development Mechanisms","The roles of knowledge, technology and innovation are increased to become the main development mechanisms in every sector.",""],[1,"21","2","National Research Agenda Alignment and Innovation Strategy Integration","the focus of the National Research Agenda must be clear, specific and in line with the development targets of different sectors, and innovation strategies should be fully integrated.",""],[1,"21","2","Multi-Stakeholder Research and Innovation Cooperation Framework","This should be performed along with promoting cooperation and partnerships involving all stakeholders, including government, the academic sector, the private sector in all areas of manufacturing and services, and communities in order to create an environment and system that supports research and strengthens innovation development.",""],[1,"21","2","R&D to Innovation Commercialization Integration","Furthermore, R&D should be integrated with innovation development and commercialization by defining the National Research Agenda in parallel with the country's goals and key social development issues according to the demands of the market and society.",""],[1,"21","2","Private Sector Participation in Innovation Development","The private sector should participate in every stage of development, including the R&D process, the innovation development process, and the commercialization process by providing necessary funds, resources, knowledge, ideas and expertise in specific areas.",""],[1,"21","2","Private Sector Green Growth Innovation Initiative","Meanwhile, the private sector should use innovation to create green growth, to support communities to generate ideas, and to build a quality society.",""],[1,"21","4","Strategic Technology R&D and Production Upgrade","Supporting R&D as well as modifying and developing strategic technology.",""],[1,"22","2","Technopreneur Linkage and Commercialization Programme","Production sectors such as farming, community enterprises, and Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) will be linked to research institutes and education institutes in order to allow the production sector to access and use available research for commercialization, along with nurturing competent entrepreneurs.",""],[1,"22","3","STEM Researcher Development and Private Research Laboratory Promotion","The objective is to prepare for rapid technological change, especially to accelerate the development of researchers in the fields of STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics), and to promote private sector research laboratories particularly in new science and in technological fields which are important for the country's future innovation development, such as cognitive science, synthetic biology, stem cells, and so on.",""],[1,"22","4","Multi-Stakeholder Innovation Network Support","Supporting the implementation of networks among research institutes, education institutes, the public sector, the private sector, and civil society/communities.",""],[1,"22","4","Social Innovation for Inclusive Growth","Social innovation will be used as a mechanism to promote inclusive growth and to improve the quality of life, especially for the elderly and disabled.",""],[1,"22","5","National R&D System Mechanism Adjustment","Adjusting the mechanisms of the national R&D system.",""],[1,"25","2","Technology-Enabled R&D for Environmentally Friendly Innovation","there is a need to improve the value chain by utilizing technology in R&D as a means of creating environmentally friendly and innovative production which responds to the needs of the market, as well as boosting product and service standards.",""],[1,"25","4","Industrial Development Foundation and Cluster Network Mechanisms","This aims to lay the foundation for future industrial development both in terms of personnel and infrastructure, as well as establishing mechanisms and networks in the form of clusters.",""],[1,"29","2","Human Resources, Technology, and Innovation Investment","investing in human resources, technology, and innovation",""],[1,"38","1","Reverse Engineering for Technology Development","For other groups with less capability, reverse engineering could be applied in order to accelerate technology development in order to cope with change in the world.",""],[1,"38","1","Increased Investment in Basic Science Research and Development","Meanwhile, investment in research and development in basic science, which is the platform for technology development, must be increased.",""],[1,"38","1","Foreign Researcher Participation in Technology Advancement","Human development must be emphasized by motivating foreign researchers to partake in the country's technology advancement in the short term, while developing domestic researchers and personnel in the basic and interdisciplinary sciences in the long term, in order to leverage science and technology knowledge for economic development and to enhance the quality of life in the longer term.",""],[1,"53","2","Patent Registration System Development","Therefore, Thailand needs to keep developing the patent registration system to increase the number of patent applications being filed by Thais, especially invention patents.",""],[1,"53","2","Intellectual Property Human Resource Development","the government should consistently develop human resource potential in intellectual property management",""],[1,"53","2","International Standard Intellectual Property Registration System","develop an effective system for intellectual property registration according to international standards",""],[1,"53","2","Intellectual Property Commercialization Support","support IP commercialization.",""],[1,"109","1","Innovation and Human Resource Development Measures","Key factors required to build economic vitality include the use of innovations, quality of human resources, as well as improvements to rules and regulations, and good governance.",""],[1,"109","2","Science, Technology, and Innovation Development Programme","Driving economic growth during the Twelfth Plan requires the development and incorporation of more advanced science, technology and innovation, the development of the digital economy, the development and up-grading of labor force quality, as well as the use of creativity for building new economic and income foundations together with increasing the productivity of the current production base and building upon existing modes of production and services by employing robotics, digital inputs and technology.",""],[1,"110","8","Innovation Development for Productivity and Service Efficiency","Promoting the development of innovations that will help increase the value and efficiency of production and services.",""],[1,"205","2","Public-Private R&D Cooperation Reform","The new era of science, technology, research and innovation development in Thailand should focus on reforming working practice with the aim of strengthening cooperation between the public and private sectors with regards to R&D investment.",""],[1,"205","2","National R&D Priority Identification and Action Plan","The action plan will include identifying the main R&D issues which must be addressed in order to enhance the capabilities of those components of the country's agricultural, industrial, and service sectors which already have a competitive advantage.",""],[1,"205","2","Innovation Society and Human Resource Development Measures","Next, there is a need to expand the capabilities of new target industries by building an innovative society, including creating innovations for the benefit of society, especially for the elderly and the disabled; developing human resources; developing laboratories and a world class body for certification and accreditation; issuing measures to strengthen national science, technology and R&D; revising law and enforcement; and restructuring the intellectual property (IP) system.",""],[1,"205","3","Science, R&D, Technology, and Innovation Utilization and Investment Promotion","the 5-year 12th National Economic and Social Development Plan of Thailand emphasizes the importance of the intensive utilization by both the private and public sectors of knowledge in science, R&D, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"205","3","R&D Investment-Friendly Environment Development","Moreover, it is also important to create an environment that welcomes R&D investment and facilitates the development of research",""],[1,"207","1","R&D and Technology Investment in Competitive Industries","Invest in R&D and technology in competent industries, such as food and agricultural technology, medical technology, environmental technology, creative industrial technology, and cultural technology in order to build new economic bases by continuously allocating sufficient budget to create innovations along the value chain, and by focusing on applied and experimental R&D which includes product prototypes, marketing, product testing, and pilot plants.",""],[1,"207","2","Research and Development and Technology Investment Programme","Invest in R&D and technology, causing a leap in the growth of such areas as medical hubs, biological technology ... robotics and smart devices, next generation automotive ... digital technology, Internet of Things, artificial intelligence, embedded systems, and rail and aviation technology.",""]],"54":[[1,"30","1","Service and Digital Economy Restructuring","The Thai cconomic system should be restructured toward a service and digital economy by supporting new entrepreneurs and becoming an entrepreneurial society.",""],[1,"84","6","Economic Structure Transformation toward Services and Digital Technologies","The structure of the economy should be transformed to one that is based on services and digital technologies.",""],[1,"109","2","Digital Economy Development Programme","Driving economic growth during the Twelfth Plan requires the development and incorporation of more advanced science, technology and innovation, the development of the digital economy, the development and up-grading of labor force quality, as well as the use of creativity for building new economic and income foundations together with increasing the productivity of the current production base and building upon existing modes of production and services by employing robotics, digital inputs and technology.",""],[1,"196","5","Digital Business and E-Commerce Promotion","Encouraging businesses to transition to digital by encouraging digital business and e-commerce platforms in the agricultural sector, the manufacturing sector, and the business sector, while promoting online shops and standards for online merchandise, and supporting digital start-ups, digital small and medium-sized enterprises (digital SMEs), and digital community enterprises.",""],[1,"196","6","Standards for Online Products and Services","Developing standards for coding online products as well as standards for online services to increase the reliability and competitiveness of Thailand's online businesses, and to ensure the efficiency and security of e-Commerce transactions, electronic supply chain management (e-SCM), and electronic payments (e-Payments).",""],[1,"196","8","Telecommunications Research and Development Commercialization Programme","Promoting telecommunications research and development to be used commercially, particularly developments regarding digital technology, high-speed wireless communication technology, software systems, transceivers, high-speed internet systems, satellite communication systems, and space and geoinformatics technology.",""],[1,"196","9","Digital Skills and Human Resource Development Initiative","Improving human resources in the public sector, private sector, and academia to be able to support the development of digital technology and to meet future labor demand of the digital industry.",""],[1,"197","1","Digital Economy Legal and Regulatory Reform","Update laws and regulations to better support the country's information and communication businesses and digital economy development, including electronic commercial laws, standards for online identity verifications, and right-of-way regulations for telecommunications infrastructure.",""],[1,"197","1","Digital Service Professionals Council","A council of digital service professionals should also be established to help facilitate collaboration between the government and the private sector in digital industry development.",""]],"55":[[1,"165","3","Cybersecurity Prevention Measures and Legislation Tightening","This problem needs to be addressed, with a focus on preventive measures against cyber threats in line with the changing environment, particularly the tightening of measures and legislation related to cyber security from the national level to the individual level.",""],[1,"196","10","Cyber Security Council Establishment","Ensure cyber security by establishing a cyber security council to monitor and respond to threats or incidents that are rapidly changing with technology development, particularly threats to the security of personal information and the financial sector.",""],[1,"203","1","Cyber Security Systems Development Plan","Development plans for cyber security systems, carried out by the Ministry of Digital Economy and Society, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Digital Economy and Society"]],"56":[[1,"126","2","SME Internationalization and Overseas Market Access Measures","Meanwhile, providing opportunities for starting a business overseas by designing policy or measures that persuade the international trading and investment companies to draw SMEs into international markets and integrate them into global value chains, in line with enhancing the role of the private sector to participate in the development of SMEs.",""],[1,"126","3","Outward Investment Promotion Line Agency","promoting the establishment of a line agency related to outward investmentment promotion, especially in Cambodia, Lao",""],[1,"127","1","Outward Direct Investment Support Measures","providing measures that support and provide incentives for outward direct investment by Thai investors, in line with reducing the obstacles to cross border flows and exchanges of money, and also supporting sources of funding",""],[1,"127","1","Trade Risk Protection Services Expansion","supporting the facilitating factors of investment through promoting risk protection services in trade, and also promoting the expansion of branches of Thailand's commercial banks into foreign countries",""]],"57":[[1,"103","11","Land Allocation and Livelihood Support for Landless Poor Farmers","Measures include land allocation to landless poor farmers, with conditions preventing the transfer of land to investors; skills-training; financial provision for job-creation; and expansion of opportunities to access professionally-relevant information, news and knowledge.",""],[1,"103","11","Marketing and Financial Management Support for Land Beneficiaries","Moreover, support with marketing and financial management should also be promoted.",""],[1,"104","1","Land Bank for Distribution of Land Holdings","bank should be established as a mechanism for distributing land-holdings to farmers and poor households such that they would have land to earn a living as well as for shelter.",""],[1,"104","3","Urban Slum Shelter and Utility Support","support with the shelter and utility system to resolve bad conditions in urban slums",""],[1,"105","1","Affordable Housing Expansion for Low-Income Earners","Expand the provision of housing for low-income earners such that it can be accessible throughout the country.",""],[1,"105","2","Universal and Inclusive Infrastructure Development","Foster universal and tailor-designed infrastructure which emphasizes appropriateness for children, women, disabled persons, the elderly and disadvantage groups.",""],[1,"105","2","Inclusive Access to Public Services and Participation","This aims to enable these groups of population to have equal access to public services and equal opportunity to develop themselves to their fullest potential.",""],[1,"105","2","Participation in Local and National Decision-Making","In addition, participation of these groups in local and national management and decision-making should also be promoted.",""],[1,"106","1","Community Land Title Act Advancement","The Community Land Title Act should be pushed forward so that communities can collectively manage land and natural resources efficiently.",""]],"58":[[1,"91","1","Safe School Environment Creation","urgently creating safe school environments for all students.",""],[1,"103","9","Holistic Support Measures for Poor Students in Remote Areas","Holistic measures should be implemented for poor students in remote areas, covering income-creation for their families and support with school-related transportation expenses.",""],[1,"103","9","Improved Scholarship Selection Process for Poor Students","Also, the selection process for the scholarships for poor students given by the Office of the Basic Education Commission (OBEC) should be improved.",""],[1,"103","9","Higher Education Scholarships to Prevent Drop-Outs","At the same time, scholarships for higher education should be put in place to prevent drop-outs.",""]],"59":[[1,"90","15","Parent-Child Daily Activity Child-Rearing Programme","Promoting a style of child-rearing that emphasizes self-reliance, honesty, discipline, morals, ethics, and responsibility, through the use of daily activities that help parents engage with their children in order that the children can observe first-hand and learn from their parents as role models.",""],[1,"91","8","Parent and Guardian Nutrition and Child-Rearing Education","Educating parents or guardians on adequate nutrition, child-rearing practices that can help stimulate development in children aged 0-3 years old, as well as promoting among mothers the breastfeeding of their children for at least 6 months after birth.",""],[1,"91","9","Work-Life Balance Measures for Parents with Young Children","Setting up measures designed to create a work-life balance for parents with young children, so that they can bring up their children themselves, such as incentive measures for workplaces to have more flexible working hours, and promoting men to participate more in household responsibilities, including looking after their children.",""],[1,"91","10","Research-Based Curriculum and Childcare Center Improvement Programme","Developing research-based curricula and improving childcare centers nationwide in order to deliver quality that is up to par with predefined standards, with more emphasis placed on skills development, including brain development, cognitive skills, emotional skills, planning and systematic thinking skills, and self-evaluation skills.",""],[1,"92","2","Creative Media Production for Early Childhood Development","Promoting creative media production in various forms to be embedded with child-rearing skills and knowledge for young children (aged 0-5 years old), such as family studies, health for mothers and children, and brain and social skills development.",""],[1,"92","3","Early Childhood Development Legislation Expansion","Pushing forward related early childhood development legislation to have more coverage on skills development, formal education system entrance preparation, health and sanitation development adequate for each age group, and all-round social skills development.",""],[1,"97","13","Early Childhood Family Support Measures","setting up policy/measures aimed to facilitate families in taking care of their children at their utmost capacity by designing appropriate measures to attract both the public and private sectors to have more flexible working patterns and to have a designated area for breastfeeding and a sanitized storage room for equipment",""],[1,"97","13","Early Childhood Workforce and Center Quality Improvement","enhancing the quality of early childhood personnel and early childcare centers by requiring all early childhood education institutes to have teachers and babysitters that have qualifications in early childhood or other related fields, by setting up an early childhood curriculum that emphasizes child development in connection with the promotion of morals and ethics, and by creating a standardized evaluation system for all early childhood development centers",""],[1,"97","13","Early Childhood Learning Environment Development","arranging adequate environments that encourage learning by allocating areas for (i) creative activities designed to encourage the learning of sciences, arts, cultures, music and",""],[1,"98","1","Early Childhood Development Law and Interagency Collaboration","promulgating laws on early childhood development, emphasizing integrated collaboration between related agencies.",""]],"61":[[1,"39","1","Research and Innovation for Elderly Care Goods and Services","This therefore provides an excellent opportunity for Thailand to conduct research and to develop new innovations and consumer goods, including medical and care-giving services to supply the needs of the elderly in the developed countries, such as nursing homes and hospitality for the elderly.",""],[1,"95","8","Long-Term Care Legislation and Sustainable Financing System","Pushing forward long-term care legislation to cover quality accessible services provided by the public sector, private sector, and civil society, as well as a sustainable financing system.",""],[1,"95","9","Medium-Term Aftercare System Development","Developing a medium-term aftercare system, designed to provide essential support to recovering patients, that is seamlessly connected with the long-term care system",""],[1,"95","9","Long-Term Care Service Business Promotion","promoting long-term care service businesses whose standards are up to par to what is required, for dependent elderly people in urban areas",""],[1,"95","9","Long-Term Care Insurance Financing Study","studying suitable financing models for long-term care insurance",""],[1,"95","10","Elderly Support Facilities Research and Development","Conducting research and development on the necessary facilities required by elderly people to sustain quality living on a daily basis, and developing medical",""],[1,"96","1","Elderly Health and Injury Prevention Technology Initiative","technology and innovations to be used in improving the health and well-being of elderly people, as well as injury prevention technology and a treatment monitoring system.",""],[1,"104","3","Community-Based Elderly Services","encourage communities to provide services needed by the elderly.",""],[1,"115","2","Guaranteed Retirement Income Products for Older Persons","elderly people will need guaranteed retirement income.",""],[1,"216","7","Elderly Employment and Income Generation Support","Promoting employment for the elderly and income generation for the elders by supporting occupational groups and community enterprises for the local elders to have the opportunity continuously to earn incomes and develop their abilities.",""],[1,"216","8","Long-Term Elderly Care Innovation Development","(2) Developing innovations for the long-term care of the elderly to cope with the increasing numbers of dependent elders and the shortage of care- providers.",""],[1,"216","9","Strengthening Family Institutions and Community-Based Social Safety Nets","Strengthening family institutions and communities in order to foster communities to play an important role in sustainable welfare provision and to create a social safety net for the elderly.",""]],"62":[[1,"24","2","Social Protection Gap Closure Initiative","Also, gaps in social protection will continue to be closed, along with enhancement of labor skills and the implementation of labor policy, to improve labor productivity and income.",""],[1,"24","3","Quality Public Services for Disadvantaged and Remote Populations","Measures include: provision of quality public services - both in education and health - to disadvantaged persons and population in remote areas;",""],[1,"24","3","Land Allocation for Poor Landless Farmers","allocation of land to poor landless farmers, with conditions that prevent subsequent change of ownership;",""],[1,"24","3","Land Bank Establishment","Establishment of a land bank and development of a crop insurance system and microfinance organizations will also be emphasized during the Plan.",""],[1,"24","3","Crop Insurance System Development","Establishment of a land bank and development of a crop insurance system and microfinance organizations will also be emphasized during the Plan.",""],[1,"24","3","Microfinance Organization Development","Establishment of a land bank and development of a crop insurance system and microfinance organizations will also be emphasized during the Plan.",""],[1,"24","4","SME, Community Enterprise, and Social Enterprise Support","Measures include: support for SMEs, community enterprises and social enterprises;",""],[1,"24","4","Microfinance Organization Development and Financial Access Expansion","development of microfinance organizations, along with improvement in financial access;",""],[1,"24","4","Fair-Price Access to High-Quality Inputs","enhanced access to high-quality inputs at fair prices.",""],[1,"25","1","Community-Based Social Welfare and Service Provision","and promoting the provision of social welfare and services by the community.",""],[1,"25","1","Community Land Distribution and Management System","The land distribution and management system at the community level will also be fostered in order to resolve the landlessness issue and establish rights in local resource management.",""],[1,"29","4","Social Welfare Benefit Rationalization","a reduction of redundancy in social welfare benefits.",""],[1,"29","4","Sustainable Public Finance for Social Protection","There is also a need to establish sustainable public finance for the social protection system, including an improvement of the retirement savings system as well as of the health insurance system, in order to minimize financial dependency on the government.",""],[1,"30","1","Income and Poverty Inequality Reduction","Income and poverty inequality are reduced.",""],[1,"30","1","Equal Access to Quality Social Services","All Thai people should be able to access quality social services equally.",""],[1,"101","1","Integrated Inequality Reduction Strategy","Accordingly, the issue of inequality needs to be tackled urgently in the Twelfth Plan such that it does not become an impediment to the country's economic and social development towards high-income status.",""],[1,"102","1","Closing Social Protection Gaps","closing the social protection gaps should continue from the Eleventh Plan",""],[1,"102","1","Targeted Assistance for Low-Income and Disadvantaged Groups","Assistance should also be linked to increasing the productivity of the 40 percent of population with the lowest income, the disadvantaged, women and elderly persons",""],[1,"103","8","Bottom 40 Percent Public Services, Social Protection, and Skills Training Measures","Measures to achieve this include:",""],[1,"104","3","Additional Social Welfare for the Lowest-Income Population","Provide additional social welfare for the 40 percent of population with the lowest income in a sufficient and appropriate manner.",""],[1,"104","3","Expanded Disability and Old-Age Allowances","provide additional disability allowances and old-age allowances for the poor group to a level sufficient for a living",""],[1,"105","1","Informal Worker Social Security Awareness Campaign","Raise awareness among informal workers of the benefits of the social security system and income security after retirement.",""]],"63":[[1,"102","1","Microfinance and Financial Access for Job Creation","development of microfinance and of financial access for job-creation",""],[1,"105","4","Community Capacity Building and Microfinance Support under the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy","Foster communities' capacity in economic development and strengthen microfinance based on the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy (SEP), such that communities are self-reliant and capable of managing their own land and human capital.",""],[1,"105","8","Community Financial Management and Microfinance Network Development","Provide financial management knowledge to communities, restructure communities' financial organizations toward fully-functioning local-level financial institutions, and set up microfinance networks with the Government Savings Bank (GSB) and the Bank of Agriculture and Agricultural Cooperatives (BAAC) as network hosts.",""],[1,"111","2","Community-Based Financial Institutions and Cooperatives Strengthening","Strengthening community-based financial institutions and cooperatives in order to encourage the availability of financial services at the grassroots level for the people and small farmers.",""],[1,"115","1","Community Development Financial Institutions Strengthening","To strengthen Community Development Financial Institutions (CDFIs), efforts should be made to: (i) improve their management and administrative processes with assistance from SFIs and co-operatives; (ii) create a database of all customers to be shared among financial institutions; and (iii) develop the capabilities of CDFIs in order to obtain legal status.",""],[1,"115","3","Specialized Financial Institutions Efficiency and Governance Reform","Increasing the efficiency and stability of Specialized Financial Institutions (SFIs) as well as promoting SFIs to be a supportive mechanism of fiscal policy implementation without creating additional risks.",""],[1,"115","3","Digital Modernization of SFI Internal Administration","To promote SFIs to be modern, flexible, and active, their internal administration should be improved through technology.",""],[1,"115","3","Financial Sector Human Resource Capacity Development","Finally, it will be necessary to increase the quality of human resources in the financial sector to cope with the changing financial environment.",""]],"64":[[1,"96","4","Family Cohesion and Parent-School Relationship Strengthening Initiative","Creating enabling social environments that can help strengthen family cohesion, with the use of appropriate communication means aimed at promoting the importance of families in human development, developing innovations designed to help facilitate communication between family members, creating more opportunities for family members to spend time together, and establishing networks between homes and schools through relation-strengthening activities between parents, teachers, and children.",""],[1,"96","5","Support Measures for Vulnerable Families","Setting up measures designed to protect and care for vulnerable families so that they can look after their family members more effectively, including adequate income earned from appropriate jobs, accessibility to healthcare services, developing monitoring systems for assistance to elderly people, as well as encouraging elderly people to partake in looking after vulnerable family members in their own communities.",""],[1,"98","3","Family Information Database Development","1) development of a family information database which can be used for further analysis and planning suited to the characteristics and nature of families in each area;",""],[1,"98","3","Community Family Cohesion and Child Cultural Activities","2) organization of activities and creation of opportunities in local communities for family members to get to spend time together, thereby strengthening relationships, as well as provision of opportunities for children to show their artistic and cultural talents in order to create among them a pride of being Thai;",""],[1,"98","3","Family Education Integration in School Learning","3) insertion of knowledge concerning family education in the learning process of school-age children, with more participation and contribution from families in formal curriculum design and planning, as well as in the organization of activities that encourage learning, management and problem-solving regarding children-related issues.",""],[1,"107","7","Integrated Child Data Collection and Monitoring System","A comprehensive data collection and monitoring system that efficiently incorporates information for every child from birth should be established and linked with civil registration.",""],[1,"107","7","Shared Education Information System Integration","All educational institutions and related agencies should also use the same information system and thereby integrate data.",""],[1,"107","7","Expansion of Electronic Monitoring and Evaluation System and Data Management Center","At the initial stage, the Electronic Monitoring and Evaluation System (e-MES) and Data Management Center (DMC) of the Ministry of Education may be expanded to cover educational instutitutions in all areas and all types.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"107","7","Child Support Grant Data Collection","In addition, data on children under the Child Support Grant Program - which gives 600 Baht per month to poor families with children aged 0-3 years - should also be collected as poor children are those with the highest likelihood of dropping out.",""]],"65":[[1,"177","8","Legal Services Expansion and Professional Standards Reform","Expanding services to cover other law services, such as law consultancy and supervision of international law consultants.",""],[1,"177","8","Legal Profession Standards and Licensing Reform","Furthermore, the standards for the legal profession should be set higher, life-long lawyer licenses should be cancelled, and allowing lawyers to counsel for the defense of public organizations and local administrations should be encouraged.",""],[1,"178","2","Justice Process Evaluation System Development","Developing evaluation systems for the efficiency of the whole justice process, with qualitative indicators.",""],[1,"178","2","Publicly Accessible Justice KPI Monitoring Framework","Also, the process of determining KPIs to allow the government and the public to monitor the quality and efficiency of justice processes in both the medium and long terms should be publicly accessible.",""],[1,"178","4","Alternative Judicial Proceedings and Judicial Assistance","Promoting fair and easily-accessible alternative judicial proceedings and judicial assistance for citizens by promoting an understanding of the legal system, judicial proceedings, mediation processes, and protection mechanisms for victims of wrongful judicial proceedings and victim of public-private-community conflicts.",""],[1,"178","5","Legal Literacy and Judicial System Awareness Mechanism","Developing mechanisms for supervising and promoting legal literacy and knowledge regarding the legal system and judicial proceedings of the country.",""],[1,"181","8","Public-Private Participation in Alternative Judicial Processes","Promoting public-private participation in alternative judicial processes.",""],[1,"181","9","Community Justice Centers Nationwide","Supporting wide and easy access by the public to justice procedures by establishing community justice centers countrywide.",""],[1,"181","10","Public Legal and Judicial Literacy Education","(3) Educating the public with basic knowledge and understanding of the law and judicial processes.",""],[1,"181","11","Inclusive Legal Assistance for Judicial Process Participants","(4) Inclusively providing legal assistance to people who are involved in judicial processes.",""],[1,"182","4","Judicial Proceedings IT Access System","Developing an IT system as a channel to support citizens' timely and convenient access to judicial proceedings, both for civil and criminal suits.",""]],"66":[[1,"139","3","Climate Change Adaptation and Greenhouse Gas Reduction Readiness","accelerating readiness for greenhouse gas reduction while enhancing capacity for climate change adaptation and management in order to reduce risks from natural disasters",""],[1,"140","4","Greenhouse Gas Reduction and Climate Adaptation Capacity Building","To improve the capacity for greenhouse gas reduction and adaptation.",""],[1,"140","4","Climate Change Impact Mitigation and Disaster Response Improvement","To lessen the impacts from climate change, and improve the response to natural disasters.",""],[1,"148","2","Climate Change Law and Regulation Reform","Draft and amend laws and regulations related to climate change so that they can respond to international climate change agreements in an integrated and comprehensive manner.",""],[1,"148","2","Greenhouse Gas Reduction Reporting Support","Contribute to the reporting systems of greenhouse gas reduction under the Nationally Appropriate Mitigation Actions (NAMAs).",""],[1,"148","2","Public-Private Greenhouse Gas Reduction Mechanisms","Facilitate the setting up of new mechanisms between the government and private sector in the efficient reduction of greenhouse gases.",""],[1,"148","3","Greenhouse Gas Reduction Measures and Mechanisms","Prescribe measures and mechanisms to support greenhouse gas reduction in all sectors, with an emphasis on the following sectors: electricity generation, transport, industry, households and buildings.",""],[1,"148","3","Renewable Energy, Energy Saving, and Waste-to-Energy Promotion","Reduce the use of fossil fuels in generating power while promoting the use of renewable energy, energy saving, and waste-to-energy.",""],[1,"148","3","Renewable Energy Workforce Capacity Building","Build the capacity of manpower to excel in various forms of renewable energy.",""],[1,"148","3","Sustainable Transport Systems Support","Support sustainable transport systems, and increase the efficiency of engines, machines and instruments.",""],[1,"148","3","Public-Private Climate Finance Mechanisms","Foster the establishment of financial mechanisms between the public and private sectors in order to support climate change actions that generate cobenefits: a few examples are carbon credits, carbon markets and carbon taxes.",""],[1,"148","3","Private Sector Greenhouse Gas Reduction Investment Promotion","Moreover, encourage the private sector to invest more in greenhouse gas reduction.",""],[1,"148","4","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Data Collection and Reporting Support","Promote the private sector, state enterprises, and local administrations to collect and report information regarding greenhouse gas emissions, particularly from energy usage.",""],[1,"149","2","Low-Carbon Technology Transfer Initiative","Facilitate the transfer of low-carbon and environmentally-friendly technology.",""],[1,"155","3","NAMA Roadmap Implementation","The goal of the NAMA Roadmap is to reduce greenhouse gases by 7 percent compared to the business as usual (BAU) emissions in 2020.",""],[1,"155","3","Renewable Energy and Sustainable Transport Measures","Important measures include electricity generation from renewable energy, efficiency improvement in production and energy use, biofuel utilization, and other sustainable transport measures.",""],[1,"155","3","Greenhouse Gas Inventory and MRV System","Therefore, a greenhouse gas inventory is also critital for the development of a reliable monitoring, reporting and verification (MRV) system.",""],[1,"155","3","Financial and Market Mechanisms for Emissions Reduction","Moreover, financial and market mechanisms could potentially increase efficiency in greenhouse gas reduction.",""]],"67":[[1,"139","3","Environmental Management System Reform","setting up a transparent and fair environmental management system",""],[1,"139","3","Sustainable Consumption and Production Promotion","promoting and scaling up sustainable consumption and production",""],[1,"146","4","Sustainable Consumption and Production Promotion","Encourage sustainable consumption and production (SCP): place emphasis on managing resources efficiently and sustainability while adopting the Philosophy of the Sufficiency Economy as the guiding principle, as well as applying the life cycle concept.",""],[1,"147","4","Sustainable Consumption Behavior Change Incentives","Create incentives for behavioral change towards sustainable consumption.",""],[1,"147","4","Consumer Information Provision Initiative","Provide accurate and adequate information to consumers.",""],[1,"147","4","Education for Sustainable Lifestyles","Promote sustainable ways of life in harmony with nature via both formal and informal education.",""],[1,"148","1","Sustainable Consumption Public Awareness and Incentive Measures","Provide public relations in a varieties of forms.",""],[1,"148","1","Environmentally Creative Media Research and Development","Promote the production of environmentally creative media.",""],[1,"148","1","Sustainable Consumption Research and Development Initiative","Conduct research and development for technology and innovation that raises public awareness concerning sustainable consumption and production.",""],[1,"148","1","Targeted Consumer Incentive Scheme","Selectively provide incentives that fit with each target group.",""],[1,"148","1","Economic Instruments for Environmentally Friendly Consumption","Apply economic instruments for changing consumers' behavior towards being more environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"148","1","Pollution Cost Internalization Measure","Incorporate the cost of natural resource extraction and waste treatment into the price of products as an incentive to reduce long-term environmental impacts.",""],[1,"148","1","Natural Material Container Promotion","Promote the use of containers made from natural materials instead of plastics.",""],[1,"148","1","Sustainable Consumption Consumer Network Outreach","Provide public relations communication and foster consumer networks of sustainable consumption via online social media, urban department stores, and local markets.",""],[1,"148","1","Green Public Procurement Expansion","Expand the green public procurement program to the regional and local levels.",""],[1,"148","1","Organic Product Listing Expansion","Increase the number of listed products to cover organic farm products.",""],[1,"154","3","Green Public Procurement Expansion","The number of green products and services in the market could escalate due to higher demand from green public procurement (including state enterprises and local administrations) and the private sector.",""],[1,"154","3","Public Awareness Campaign on Green Products","Simultaneously, public awareness and understanding regarding the importance of green products and services in relation to environmentally and socially responsible producers, should be cultivated continuously.",""]],"68":[[1,"145","3","Integrated Solid Waste Management Reform","Rapidly manage the cumulative solid waste in the crisis areas: advocate laws and mechanisms to enforce waste separation (or sorting), promote methods of turning waste into energy, apply economic instruments to reduce waste generation, and create discipline among all Thais in sustainable waste management.",""],[1,"145","3","Provincial and Local Solid Waste Planning Support","Support the preparation of solid waste management plans at the provincial and local levels.",""],[1,"145","3","Local Solid Waste Management Clusters","Encourage local administrations collectively to set up solid waste management clusters while building partnerships with the private sector to enhance the efficiency of solid waste management.",""],[1,"145","3","Integrated Waste Value Chain Management","Promote integrated solid waste management, including the entire chain of waste production from sources to treatment facilities.",""],[1,"145","3","Waste-to-Energy Recycling Promotion","Champion waste recycling by turning waste into energy using innovation and technology that fit with local conditions.",""],[1,"145","3","Household Hazardous Waste Control Measures","Advocate the passing of laws and measures for managing household harzadous wastes, especially from electronic and electrical appliances.",""],[1,"145","3","Nationwide Hazardous Appliance Collection and Import Restrictions","Implement both voluntary and mandatory measures, including import restrictions on those appliances, and the provision of collection and management facilities nationwide.",""],[1,"145","3","Industrial Hazardous Waste Tracking System","Develop tracking systems for industrial hazardous waste transport consistent with international standards.",""],[1,"145","3","Public Awareness for Sustainable Waste Management","Cultivate discipline in the habits of Thai citizens towards sustainable management by providing knowledge, creating consciousness and raising the awareness of the general public, students and youth groups.",""],[1,"153","4","Roadmap for Solid and Hazardous Waste Management","The Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment has formulated the Roadmap for Solid and Hazardous Waste by integrating all 77 provincial solid waste management plans, including the BMA.","Ministry of Natural Resources and Environment"],[1,"153","4","National Master Plan on Waste Management","Recently, the National Master Plan on Waste Management (2016-2021) has been adopted as the guideline for practical, efficient, and sustainable solid waste management.",""],[1,"153","5","Integrated Solid and Hazardous Waste Management Master Plan","The Master Plan is comprised of several key measures, including: (1) reducing the generation of solid and hazardous waste at source; (2) increasing the potential for solid and hazardous waste management; and (3) supporting the management of solid and hazardous waste.",""],[1,"153","5","Integrated Solid and Hazardous Waste Management Centers","set up an Integrated Center for Solid and Hazardous Waste Management, covering areas of different sizes ranging from large, medium and small clusters;",""],[1,"153","5","Solid and Hazardous Waste Transfer Stations","build Transfer Stations for Solid and Hazardous Waste;",""],[1,"154","1","Local Solid Waste Management in Spatial Clusters","promote the local management of solid waste in 349 spatial clusters.",""]],"69":[[1,"163","5","Environmental Quality Management Plan","Environmental Quality Management Plan, 2017-2012",""],[1,"163","5","Integrated Biodiversity Management Master Plan","Master Plan for Integrated Management of Biodiversity",""],[1,"163","5","Second Phase Fishery Management Master Plan","Master Plan for the 2nd Phase of Thailand Fishery Management, 5 years (2014-2018)",""]],"70":[[1,"27","2","Transparent and Fair Environmental Governance System","Simultaneously, it is critical to build a transparent and fair management system as well as promote sustainable consumption and production.",""],[1,"62","3","Conflict-Resolution Mechanisms for Development Projects","Thus, to reduce inequality the government needs to set up conflict-resolution mechanisms and build good governance and equality of access, allocation and sharing of benefits from the use of natural resources in a fair manner.",""],[1,"62","3","Good Governance and Fair Benefit-Sharing for Natural Resources","Thus, to reduce inequality the government needs to set up conflict-resolution mechanisms and build good governance and equality of access, allocation and sharing of benefits from the use of natural resources in a fair manner.",""],[1,"68","1","Environmental Impact Assessment for Bang Yai-Kanchanaburi Highway Motorway Project","environmental impact assessment of the Bang Yai-Kanchanaburi highway intercity motorway project;",""],[1,"118","2","Agricultural Chemical Control and Organic Substitution Measures","Controlling strictly the use of agricultural chemicals that are a danger to health and the environment, particularly pesticides.",""]],"71":[[1,"142","4","Biodiversity Resource Value Creation and Fair Benefit Sharing","promote use and value creation from biodiversity resources whilst facilitating fair benefit sharing.",""],[1,"142","4","Biodiversity Product Research and Development Programme","Create research programs systematically to develop products from biodiversity resources: champion new business development, and support development strategies for herbal medicines and cosmetics with a high potential market demand.",""],[1,"142","4","Integration of Bio-product Development with OTOP","Link new and high-value bio- product development with the \"One Tambon, One Product\" (OTOP) development process by",""]],"72":[[1,"132","5","Eco-Industrial Town Project","The Ministry of Industry will take a leading role in initiating the eco-industrial town project.","Ministry of Industry"],[1,"146","5","Environmental Standards Support for Industrial Production and Investment","Support industrial production and investment that are environmentally friendly.",""],[1,"147","1","Clean Industrial Investment and Eco-Design Promotion","Promote industrial investment that employs clean technology.",""],[1,"154","3","Green Supply Chain Upgrading Support","Towards greening the supply chain, small and medium producers are encouraged to upgrade their production processes with assistance from the large producers.",""],[1,"154","3","Low-Interest Green Production Financing and Incentives","The government could offer special low-interest loans or use economic instruments as incentives for producers to improve their production and to request green labelling certification.",""],[1,"154","3","Green Product Criteria and Specification Development","Moreover, the development of criteria and specifications for green products and services should be expanded to cover a greater varieties, particularly those with high market demand.",""]],"73":[[1,"149","4","Disaster Risk Reduction Mainstreaming and Risk Mapping","Integrate disaster risk reduction into the planning process at the national, provincial and local community levels, and in various production sectors.",""],[1,"149","4","Risk Assessment Knowledge and Mapping Support","Create knowledge that supports risk assessment and maps both for local communities and high- priority production sectors.",""],[1,"149","5","Local Disaster Risk Mapping Support","Support risk mapping at the local level.",""],[1,"149","5","Community-Centered Disaster Response Approach","Encourage a disaster response approach which puts communities at the center.",""],[1,"149","5","Private Sector Business Continuity Planning","Encourage the private sector to prepare Business Contingency Plans (BCP).",""],[1,"149","5","Public-Private Disaster Risk Reduction Collaboration","Champion both the private sector and local communities to work together in the prevention and reduction of disaster risks.",""],[1,"149","6","Disaster Response System for Emergency Periods","Set up a disaster response system for emergency periods.",""],[1,"149","6","Disaster Warning System Development","Develop disaster warning systems that are accurate, reliable, and efficient.",""],[1,"149","6","Integrated Disaster Information and Database Systems","Support information access mechanisms via new technology: create integrated database systems with common standards that connect with domestic and international organizations.",""],[1,"149","6","Integrated Collaborative Emergency Management Mechanism","Develop integrated collaborative mechanisms to increase the capacity for emergency management.",""],[1,"149","8","Disaster Management Curriculum Development","Construct curricula related to disaster management.",""],[1,"150","1","Voluntary Emergency Rescue and Assistance Networks","voluntary networks by linking closely with the government sector.",""],[1,"159","8","Preparedness and Response Mechanism Development","Develop efficient preparedness and response mechanisms that are readily available to respond, both in normal times and in crisis situations, to traditional and",""],[1,"160","2","Integrated Emergency Preparedness Systems Management","Develop integrated preparedness systems management for the emergency response to emerging infectious diseases, pre-disaster, during a disaster, and post-disaster, including a knowledge management system that links information from the national level to the provincial level and the community level.",""],[1,"166","2","National Preparedness System Development","develop a National Preparedness System, including associated infrastructure development, to prevent the loss of land and to handle natural disasters, both on land and at sea, by formulating policies, strategies, plans, operations plans and immediate action plans",""]],"74":[[1,"145","2","Green Cities Development Initiative","Build environmentally- friendly cities or green cities to create a good environment for the people.",""],[1,"146","3","Urban Green Growth Regulatory and Planning Reform","Revise regulations and develop urban infrastructure to support green growth.",""],[1,"146","3","Environmentally Friendly and Disaster-Resilient Infrastructure Development","Promote large infrastructure development projects that are environmentally friendly and resilient to natural disasters.",""],[1,"146","3","Green Cities Scaling and Benchmarking Initiative","Scale up existing \"green cities\" in different shapes and forms to be prototypes such as for livable cities, low-carbon cities, smart cities, and eco-industrial towns, green agriculture cities, and sustainable tourism cities.",""],[1,"154","5","Green City Integration in Local Development Plans","encourage the executives of local administrations to adopt the green city (green growth in the city) into their local development plans and implement these plans accordingly.",""],[1,"154","5","Local Authority Green City Knowledge Exchange","it is helpful to promote information exchange among local authorities so that good lessons can be shared and learned.",""],[1,"154","5","Green City Replication and Scaling Initiative","Then, the replication of new green cities is possible while building on exsisting succesful cases.",""],[1,"154","5","Financial Support Measures for Green Urban Growth","Create new financial measures to support the green growth of cities.",""],[1,"154","5","Legal Reform for Green City Development","Revise and reform related laws",""],[1,"155","1","Local Municipal-Community Coordination Mechanisms","Foster local authorities to set up coordination mechanisms between municipalities and communities.",""],[1,"155","1","Community Conscientiousness and Participation Campaign","Cultivate conscientiousness of individuals in communities via different channels.",""],[1,"155","1","Inclusive Urban Green Growth Implementation","Allow all parties to participate in implementing action towards the green growth of cities.",""]],"75":[[1,"148","5","ST&I Research and Adaptive Technology Support for Climate Change Adaptation","Enhance the capacity of R&D in science, technology and innovation (ST&I) to support climate change adaptation.",""],[1,"148","5","Agricultural Adaptive Technology Development through Local Wisdom","Stimulate R&D in ST&I while applying local wisdom to offer the adaptive technology necessary for the agricultural sector.",""],[1,"148","5","Support Measures for Vulnerable and High-Risk Populations","Provide supportive measures to assist vulnerable and high-risk populations with a low",""],[1,"149","1","Climate Change Adaptation Planning and Urban Protection Measures","Plan to protect cities that might be affected by sea-level rise, extreme weather and seasonal variation.",""],[1,"149","2","Climate Change Awareness and Capacity-Building Programme","Create knowledge and understanding, and raise awareness and public participation from all stakesholders in response to climate change impacts.",""],[1,"149","2","Climate Risk Knowledge Creation and Capacity Development","Foster knowledge creation with respect to the impacts and risks of climate change.",""],[1,"149","2","Multi-Level Climate Adaptation Capacity Building","Enhance the capacity of individuals and organizations at various levels at both the central and local levels.",""],[1,"149","2","Community Climate Resilience Capacity Programme","Communities should gain knowledge and have the capacity to cope with climate change impacts.",""],[1,"149","2","Environmental and Sufficiency Economy Curriculum Development","Create environmental curricula accompanied by a Sufficiency Economy curriculum for compulsory education from primary level upwards.",""],[1,"155","3","National Adaptation Plan and Vulnerability Assessment","Thus, NAP fosters vulnerability assessments and mapping.",""],[1,"155","3","High-Risk Sector Adaptation Alternatives","In addition to NAP, it is important to focus on the following: providing adaptation alternatives to the sectors or areas that are in high risk; putting emphasis on the adaptation plans of cities and agriculture; protecting urban and coastal areas, the health sector, and preventing floods; building the database system and creating related knowledge.",""]],"76":[[1,"121","2","Aviation Maintenance, Repair, and Overhaul Skills Development","Meanwhile, the development of skilled labor and human resources should be accelerated to support the establishment of an aviation maintenance, repair, and overhaul service sector (MRO) in the future;",""],[1,"121","3","Workforce Development Plan for Targeted Future Industries","Formulating a workforce development plan to prepare human resources for the targeted future industries, both for a prompt response to industrial demand in the immediate phase, and for establishing a foundation for competitiveness in the long-term phase.",""],[1,"122","1","Private Sector Skills Training Investment Support","it is necessary to promote and facilitate the private sector's investment in developing special skills training institutes or training programs for producing qualified skilled labor to serve rapidly the immediate needs of the targeted future industries.",""],[1,"122","1","Long-Term Workforce Planning for Future Industries","Simultaneously, holistic and systematic planning for the efficient and effective supply of labor in the long-term and the development of targeted human resources for future industries should be deliberately undertaken, with a focus on developing specific skills and competencies to meet the requirements of future industries effectively.",""],[1,"133","1","Extension of the Automotive and Auto-parts Human Resource Development Academy","Extension of the Automotive and Auto-parts Human Resource Development Academy (AHRDA):",""],[1,"133","2","Automotive Cluster Development Support Project","The project aims to support the government's policy for automotive cluster development.",""]],"77":[[1,"92","5","Active Learning Curriculum Reform","Adjusting learning processes, aiming at encouraging and promoting active learning among children, so that they can learn by doing and experiencing things themselves, with more emphasis placed on the sciences, technology, engineering, mathematics, the arts and foreign language subjects.",""],[1,"92","6","Life Skills and Continuous Learning Development for Children","Encouraging children to take part in life skills and continuous learning skills development, both inside and outside the classroom, including reading, community service, taking care of health, team working, and life planning.",""],[1,"93","8","Small-Scale School Management and Administrative Adjustment","Adjusting the management and administrative systems of small-scale schools where the number of students and the size of the schools falls below benchmarks, in order to pool their resources and adjust their size and number of students to be appropriate to the area and to a population structure with a diminishing number of children.",""],[1,"93","9","Competency-Based Teacher Training Reform","Adjusting teacher training programs, with more emphasis placed on competency-based programs, professionalism, coaching skills, and the ability to stimulate learning.",""],[1,"93","9","Teacher Recruitment Incentive Mechanism","creating incentive mechanisms designed to attract high-potential individuals to become teachers",""],[1,"93","9","Teacher Performance Evaluation Reform","adjusting the teachers' academic standing evaluation method to reflect students' performance",""],[1,"93","9","Teacher Knowledge Exchange Network","building teaching knowledge exchange networks for teachers as a platform for continuous competency development among teachers.",""],[1,"93","10","Quality Assessment System Development","Developing a quality assessment system that can truly reflect learners' improvement of skills, knowledge, capability, and competency in accordance with the learning standards of each educational level.",""],[1,"104","6","Teacher Distribution Incentive Scheme","This can be done by: (1) providing incentives for teachers such that they are dispersed more efficiently.",""],[1,"104","6","Educational Accountability System","This can be done by: (2) setting up an educational accountability system by incorporating educational outcomes into the evaluations of teachers and institutions;",""],[1,"108","3","School Budget Devolution and Outcome-Based Financing Reform","The project aims at devolving authority to educational institutions to manage their own budgets, with an emphasis on outcome evaluation.",""],[1,"108","3","Shift from Supply-Side to Demand-Side Education Financing","The proportion of supply-side financing - e.g. operating budget, personnel budget and investment budget - should be reduced because these types of budget do not relate to students' needs.",""],[1,"108","3","Remote Area School Subsidy Expansion","Moreover, a larger amount of subsidy should be allocated to schools in remote areas in order to enhance educational access opportunities.",""]],"78":[[1,"92","9","Labor Training Center Standards and Competency-Based Skills Assessment Reform","Developing labor training centers to have standards that are up to par with those of the Professional Qualifications Framework and the National Skills Standard, as well as creating occupational standards guidelines for occupations required by targeted high-potential industries and promoting the use of competency-based skills evaluation.",""],[1,"92","10","Integrated Labor Demand and Supply Database Development","Accelerating the development of an integrated labor demand and supply database that can be further used for labor projections in accordance with anticipated labor market trends.",""],[1,"93","1","One-Stop Labor Information and Data Services Centers","Establishing one-stop labor information and data services centers in order to provide relevant information and consultation on suitable financing and marketing for new entrepreneurs and freelancers, as well as encouraging education institutions to provide short-term courses on essential skills development for this target group.",""],[1,"93","4","Working Skills Development Courses for Older Persons","Developing working skills development courses that are suitable for young-old elderly people according to their age, competencies, physical abilities, and job characteristics",""],[1,"93","4","Intergenerational Teamwork Skills Promotion","promoting team-working skills among people from different generations",""],[1,"99","4","National Labor Training Center Improvement Programme","improving labor training centers all around the nation in order to enhance and develop the competencies required by both the national professional qualification framework and national labor standards","Thailand Professional Qualifications Institute (Public Organization) | Department of Skills Development"],[1,"102","1","Labor Skills and Productivity Enhancement Policy","with an emphasis on rasing labor skills and pursuing labor policy that enhance labor productivity and income",""],[1,"109","2","Labor Force Quality Upgrading Programme","Driving economic growth during the Twelfth Plan requires the development and incorporation of more advanced science, technology and innovation, the development of the digital economy, the development and up-grading of labor force quality, as well as the use of creativity for building new economic and income foundations together with increasing the productivity of the current production base and building upon existing modes of production and services by employing robotics, digital inputs and technology.",""]],"79":[[1,"5","3","Labor Skills Enhancement Initiative","this has to be accomplished together with accelerating the enhancement of labor skills, both of new entrants to the labor market and existing workers, in order to be compatible",""],[1,"6","1","Education, Skills, and Public Health Enhancement","human society should be developed in such a way as to achieve well- being in all age groups and to have the capacity to cope adequately with daily life changes through the leverage provided by quality education, learning and skills enhancement, and through quality public health services in all areas, and by promoting the role of social institutions to imbue good, disciplined people with strong values and social responsibility.",""],[1,"7","2","Human Resources Development","efficient human resources development;",""],[1,"20","3","Human Development Investment","Critical issues are therefore economic and social structural adjustment, infrastructural investment, human development, and the transformation of values and living culture in work, learning, discipline and responsibility.",""],[1,"23","2","Early Childhood Physical, Mental, and Life Skills Development","Promoting physical and mental health among young children to allow them to have sound neural and cognitive development, as well as enhancing their life skills in order to become a valuable asset for the country.",""],[1,"23","4","Lifelong Skills and Human Resource Development Programme","Developing necessary skills and knowledge in each age span in order to lay a firm foundation for creating well-rounded citizens.",""],[1,"23","6","Primary Education Quality Management Improvement","by improving the management of primary education quality in small schools",""],[1,"23","6","Teaching and Learning Methods Reform","reforming teaching and learning methods",""],[1,"23","6","Teacher Quality Development Programme","developing the quality of teachers within the whole system",""],[1,"23","6","Dual Vocational and Cooperative Education Expansion","through Dual Vocational Education3 and Cooperative Education,4 in order to prepare the workforce to have the requisite skills before entering the labor market",""],[1,"23","6","Lifelong Learning Environment Development","there is a need to create an environment for lifelong learning which features diverse learning materials and centers",""],[1,"24","1","Health Education and Healthy Behavior Promotion","This will be implemented by changing health-related behavior and reducing risk factors that have impacts on health through prioritizing health education promotion, promoting physical activity and nutrition that is suitable for each age group, adopting legal mechanisms and incentives in regulating food and products that impact health, and establishing a public policy-making process that takes health impacts and the creation of a healthy environment into account.",""],[1,"24","2","Social Services Quality Improvement Programme","In the next 5 years, emphasis will be on improving the quality of social services throughout the country, particularly those that concern education and public health.",""],[1,"24","2","Labor Skills Enhancement and Labor Policy Implementation","Also, gaps in social protection will continue to be closed, along with enhancement of labor skills and the implementation of labor policy, to improve labor productivity and income.",""],[1,"24","3","Skills Training for Target Population Groups","skills training for target population groups to enable them to have decent jobs and income.",""],[1,"24","6","Community Skill-Training Centers Support","This will be done by promoting community-level entrepreneurship, supporting community skill-training centers to upgrade the skills of members,",""],[1,"25","2","Entrepreneur Business Skills Development","Building conditions where entrepreneurs can possess the business skills needed to keep pace with technological change should be encouraged.",""]],"80":[[1,"159","4","Peaceful Conflict Resolution in the Southern Border Provinces","Prevent and resolve the unrest in the southern border provinces by peaceful means with local public participation based on differences in identity and ethnicity to eliminate conflict and reduce violence according to the royal-initiated strategy of His Majesty King Bhumibol Adulyadej, Rama 9, following the principles \"Understand, Access and Develop\"",""],[1,"164","3","Southern Border Peacebuilding and Conflict Resolution Effort","tackling the unrest in the southern border provinces is the duty of all government agencies and the Thai people, both of which must help with brainstorming to seek a peaceful solution to the conflict.",""],[1,"164","3","Conflict Root-Cause Analysis and Violence Reduction Measures","This can be achieved by determining all dimensions of the basis of the conflict in order to find ways to terminate the violence and resolve the issues in a peaceful way.",""],[1,"164","3","Southern Border Inclusion and Local Identity Support","This will involve eliminating every condition that contributes to the conflict, avoiding giving the impression that the local people are unfairly treated and uncared for by the state when compared to the people in the rest of the country, and making the people in the southern border provinces feel proud that they can live a normal life peacefully under their own identity without pressure or assimilation, and are given opportunities to contribute to economic and social development in the area.",""]],"81":[[1,"159","6","Armed Forces Capability and Readiness Development","Develop the capability and readiness of the armed forces to defend and protect the national interests by developing human resources to be competent and prepared to respond to any situations in a timely and adequate manner, and to be fully equipped with suitable and affordable armaments, munitions, modern technologies to support the country's development, humanitarian assistance and disaster relief, and other important national issues, effectively and efficiently.",""],[1,"160","4","Defense Industry Research, Development, and Innovation Collaboration","Develop the defense industry by strengthening research and development, together with initiating collaboration between government agencies, the private sector and allied countries for knowledge creation and exchange of technologies for empowering capabilities in weapons, munitions, and ammunition development, and concurrently promote innovation in the defense industry by government agencies.",""]],"82":[[1,"159","7","Intelligence System and Threat Information-Sharing Mechanism","Develop an efficient intelligence system, mechanisms to strengthen cooperation, and cognitive development to analyze the trends of threats, including a database for sharing news and information between both local and international agencies in a systematic manner, with the availability of supporting data to help prepare the response to security threats, both locally and internationally.",""],[1,"160","3","Terrorism Data Sharing and Analysis System","Develop a system for compiling and sharing data and information related to terrorism, both between internal departments and with external international agencies for tracking, analyzing and synthesizing knowledge to counter terrorist and security threats, coupled with the development of appropriate guidelines to support the operations in all sectors, efficiently and effectively.",""],[1,"161","3","Personal Data Retention and Cross-Border Data Exchange Regulation System","Develop a system of retention of personal data related to cyber security, and regulate the system for international exchange of personal data according to international standards.",""]],"83":[[1,"116","1","Agricultural Land Protection and Zoning Reform","protecting potential agricultural land and expanding opportunities for farmers to access land for their livelihood.",""],[1,"116","1","Farmer Knowledge and Plant and Animal Improvement Support","encouraging farmers to be knowledgeable in the collection, selection and improvement of plants, animals, aquatic animals, and local microorganisms.",""],[1,"118","1","Agricultural Research, Technology, and Machinery Upgrading","conducting research and development (R&D) while using new technology and machinery in production procedures, both pre- and post-harvesting, and in processing procedures, to increase efficiency and reduce production cost along the production chain;",""],[1,"119","1","New Generation Farmer Development Programme","producing manpower in agriculture by developing new generation farmers via the graduates returning home program.",""],[1,"119","1","Agricultural Laws and Regulations Update","amending related laws and regulations to keep them up-to-date.",""]],"84":[[1,"109","2","Biological Resources Utilization Initiative","Moreover, the strategy focuses on the use of biological resources; the support of value chain linkages; the development of new economic zones and corridors; the integration of the service sector and the trade sector, coupled with preparing the service sector to underpin freer competition; the enhancement of SME competitiveness; and the establishment of a culture for entrepreneurs to produce and sell by responding to rapid",""],[1,"117","1","Agricultural and Food Product Standards, Inspection, and Traceability System","developing systems of agricultural and food product standards that are internationally accepted both in food and non-food products such as herbs, supplements, medicines, renewable energy, and bio-materials.",""],[1,"117","1","Good Agricultural Practice and Food Safety Promotion","Educating farmers about standardized production processes such as Good Agriculture Practice (GAP).",""],[1,"117","1","Organic Agriculture Promotion and Certification Support","promoting organic agricultural production actively.",""],[1,"117","2","Agroindustry Value Chain Capacity Strengthening","Strengthening the production capacity of the agroindustry value chain: (1) enhancing the capacity of farmers' institutions and group formation to be the main management mechanisms in the entire agroindustry value chain.",""],[1,"117","2","Agricultural Zoning and Precision Farming Support","(2) fostering farmers to grow crops, raise livestock and fishing that is consistent with the land's potential and market demand (the zoning approach) to enhance efficiency and to reduce the cost of production.",""],[1,"118","1","Geographical Indication Agricultural Product Development","Developing agricultural products that are registered for geographical indications (GI).",""],[1,"118","1","Agricultural Value Addition and Biodiversity-Based Product Development","promoting the creation of value for agricultural products and harnessing the biodiversity base to further create knowledge and develop new high- value products.",""],[1,"118","1","Agricultural Value Chain Integration and Cooperative Networks","Using the results from R&D to add value to agricultural and commercial products, so that they are diverse and meet market demand, via co-operative networks of farmers, the private and public sectors;",""],[1,"118","1","Integrated Agricultural Production Planning and Sector Linkages","Planning production to meet the demands of industry in order to achieve a balance in production at all levels, ranging from the local, provincial, regional, and national levels.",""],[1,"118","1","Agricultural Production Linkages with Services and Tourism","Linking agricultural production with other production sectors, such as services and tourism, in order to rely less on basic agricultural exports;",""],[1,"118","2","Sustainable Agriculture Support and Replication Programme","Supporting and replicating agricultural practices based on the Sufficiency Economy Philosophy (SEP): (1) fostering farmers to take part in the formulation of agriculture policy at every step from design to action, resulting in their agricultural development.",""],[1,"118","2","Sustainable Agriculture Infrastructure, Knowledge, Finance, and Marketing Support","Modifying mechanisms and infrastructure necessary for sustainable agriculture, such as developing a database system for sustainable agriculture, creating knowledge, supporting finance in the form of green credit, and promoting marketing activities;",""],[1,"129","12","Agricultural Input Cost Reduction and Low-Interest Capital Support","Collaborating with the private and government sectors to reduce input costs, including chemical fertilizers, animal feed, labor costs, service charges for agricultural machinery, land rents, electricity costs for agricultural activities, and provide capital with low interest rates.",""],[1,"129","12","Farmer Training on Agricultural Input Use and Soil Improvement","Providing farmers with training in the appropriate uses of agricultural inputs and soil improvement.",""],[1,"129","12","Agricultural Product Standards, Value Addition, and Market Linkage Development","Developing product standards, value creation, and marketing connectivity.",""],[1,"130","5","Large-Scale Agricultural Production in Pilot Areas","Promoting large-scale agricultural production in pilot areas initiated by farmers in order to reduce costs and increase yields.",""],[1,"130","5","Integrated Agricultural Management and Marketing Approach","Managing and marketing by all stakeholders in an integrated approach.",""],[1,"131","3","Development of Learning Centers for Farming Productivity","Developing learning centers to increase productivity in farming and scaling up service provision by the centers.",""],[1,"132","2","Local Cooperative Development Plan Implementation","Moving forward the national co-operative development plan to concrete implementation at local level.",""],[1,"132","2","Cooperative Production, Marketing, and Finance Linkage Strengthening","Enhancing the linkage potential of production networks as well as marketing and finance of cooperatives to strengthen the entire system and connect with business sustainably.",""],[1,"215","4","Agricultural Productivity and Agro-processing Development","To improve agricultural productivity, value-added products, safe and organic agriculture under Good Agricultural Practice (GAP), as well as to develop various agro-processing products to serve market demand:",""],[1,"215","5","Upper and Lower Northern Provincial Cluster Agricultural Production Development","Developing the Upper Northern Provincial Clusters to be an organic agricultural production base, and the Lower Northern Provincial Clusters to be a safe agricultural production base (smart farms) by: (1.1) reducing chemical use in order to transform chemical-based agriculture into organic agriculture with GAP, (1.2) applying green technologies in the production process, and (1.3) supporting farmer groups or cooperatives for effective joint production planning and marketing networks.",""],[1,"215","6","Agro-processing Industry Upgrading and Value-Added Agricultural Production","Upgrading agro-processing industries by: (2.1) Chiang Mai, Chiang Rai, Lampang and Lamphun becoming the main producing areas for vegetables, fruits, and herbal products, and (2.2) Phichit, Kamphangphet, and Nakhon Sawan becoming the main producing areas for rice, field crops and energy crops.",""],[1,"217","3","Organic Jasmine Rice Production Base Development","Developing the Thung Kula Rong Hai plateau in Yasothon, Surin, Roi-Et, Maha Sarakham, and Sisaket, and including other high-potential areas, to become a premium Thai jasmine rice production base by: (1.1) improving production processes according to organic agricultural standards, (1.2) developing the organic agricultural value chain, (1.3) expanding organic farmlands, (1.4) fostering participatory guarantee systems among farmer groups and local communities, (1.5) supporting research and innovation development in responding to the domestic market for healthy products, as well as for export, (1.6) initiating organic agricultural funds and green markets in local communities, and (1.7) encouraging farmers and farmer associations to utilize e-commerce to reach domestic and international markets.",""],[1,"217","4","Alternative Agricultural Product Cultivation Promotion","Promoting the cultivation of alternative agricultural products according to each area's potential through: (2.1) vegetable, fruit, and flower plantations in Loei, Nong Khai, Bueng Kan, Nakhon Phanom, Sisaket, and Ubon Ratchathani, (2.2) high-grade beef cattle husbandry in Sakon Nakhon, Mukdahan, and Nakhon Phanom, and (2.3) dairy production in Nakhon Ratchasima and Ubon Ratchathani.",""],[1,"217","5","Farmer Self-Sufficiency Support Programme","(3) Reinforcing farmers and farmer institutes to be self- sufficient in Amnat Chareon, Kalasin and Khon Kaen by: (3.1) supporting the establishment of farmer groups, community enterprise networks and agricultural cooperatives, (3.2) encouraging saving while improving financial services accessibility for farmers, (3.3) developing young smart farmers by adopting the Philosophy of the Sufficiency Economy, the New Agricultural Theory, and the 1-Rai-1-Hundred Thousand-Baht Scheme, (3.4) supporting successful farmers to be role models for others, and (3.5) promoting the wide expansion of local agricultural markets and e-commerce.",""],[1,"231","1","Quality and Safe Agricultural Production System Development","developing a quality and safe agricultural production system in the Lower Northern Sub-region in order to create value-added from agricultural commodities, as well as generating greater income to farmers.",""],[1,"231","8","Organic Agriculture Value Chain Development","creating a value chain for organic agriculture",""],[1,"231","8","International Organic Certification Upgrade","upgrading the Thai organic certification service to become an internationally-recognized organic certification service",""],[1,"231","8","Organic Research and Innovation Support","promoting research and innovation in responding to the domestic and export healthy-products markets",""],[1,"232","7","Quality and International Standard Agricultural Production Systems Development","developing quality and international standard agricultural production systems to meet quality, safety, and standards requirements",""],[1,"232","7","Agricultural Research and Development for Modern Production and Breeding","fostering research and development in the use of modern technological production and appropriate breeding",""],[1,"232","7","Diversified Agricultural Processing Development","including diversified processing in response to the demands of both domestic and international consumers",""],[1,"232","7","Efficient Agricultural Market Management System","delivering an efficient market management system",""]],"85":[[1,"122","4","Business Environment Regulatory Reform","Revamping and renewing laws and regulations to expedite a sound business environment for enhancing the competitiveness of the targeted future industries, particularly laws and regulations regarding investment promotion, import- export, product testing and standardization, research and development, and human resource development.",""],[1,"126","3","Investment Protection and Investor-State Dispute Settlement Mechanism","The domestic investment should, thus, emphasize: (1) developing the mechanism of Investment Protection and Investor-State Dispute Settlement in order to increase investor confidence through strengthening Thailand's arbitration system, reducing disputation between government and the private sector through an emphasis on developing administrative and contract management, and the appointment of arbitrators;",""],[1,"126","3","Labor Mobility Procedure Simplification","reducing obstacles within labor mobility procedures in order to facilitate the free flow of foreign workers by reducing the period of time taken for notification, and also extending the period for applying for a work permit.",""],[1,"127","2","Trade and Investment Regulatory Reform","Amending laws, rules and regulations to support fair trade and facilitate trade and investment, including SMEs business operations, through adjusting rules, regulations and guidelines on customs formalities in order to assure transparent enforcement and meet international standards.",""],[1,"127","2","Trade Competition Act Amendment","It is important to amend the Trade Competition Act in order to promote fair market competition.",""],[1,"127","2","E-Commerce Legal and SME Support Reform","The efficiency of law enforcement should be enhanced in a timely manner in line with the economic situation, and laws and rules should be revised to support start-up enterprises and SMEs in parallel with enforcing effective laws related to electronic transactions and privacy protection in order to build the confidence of entrepreneurs and comsumers to make more use of e- commerce.",""],[1,"137","9","Trade Competition Act Amendment and Regulatory Revision","Encouraging the amendment of the Trade Competition Act in parallel with revising relevant definitions and rules in order to enforce laws effectively and be able to respond to the changing trading environment in a timely manner.",""],[1,"137","17","Foreign Worker Notification Streamlining","putting emphasis on reducing the period of making notification for foreign workers, offering",""],[1,"138","1","Business Visitor Visa Facilitation","visas on arrival for business visitors who are participating in meetings less than 15 days",""],[1,"138","1","Extended Work Permit Application Period","extending the period for work permit application",""],[1,"138","1","Expatriate Income Tax Reduction","reducing personal income tax for expatriates",""],[1,"138","1","International Money Flow Liberalization","reducing obstacles to international money flows",""]],"86":[[1,"29","4","Tax Base Broadening Reform","Major reforms include: a broadening of the tax base;",""],[1,"29","4","Budget Proposal System Adjustment","an adjustment of the budget proposal system;",""],[1,"29","4","Integrated Budgeting Reform","budget allocation; integrated budgeting, both development issue- based and area-based;",""],[1,"29","4","Budget Spending Monitoring and Evaluation","monitoring and evaluation of budget spending;",""],[1,"29","4","Decentralized Tax and Fees Collection","decentralization of tax and fees collection to Local Administrative Organizations (LAOs);",""],[1,"102","1","Area-Based and Integrated Budgeting Efficiency Improvement","efficiency in area- based budgeting and integrated budgeting should be enhanced to reduce inequality effectively",""],[1,"104","2","More Redistributive Fiscal Policy","Impose a more-redistributive fiscal policy that effectively favors the low-income population by imposing more wealth-based taxation and enhancing the efficiency of tax collection.",""],[1,"104","2","Integrated and Area-Based Budgeting Reform","Also, budget allocation should be restructured by giving priority to integrated budgeting and area-based budgeting that targets poverty- and inequality- reduction.",""],[1,"106","8","Personal Income Database and Tax Registration Expansion","This plan aims at motivating the population functioning outside the formal income database (i.e. tax system) to enter the system, such that low-income earners can be identified for effective assistance.","Revenue Department, Ministry of Finance"],[1,"113","7","Budget Preparation Procedure Enhancement","Enhancing the effectiveness of budget preparation procedures, including the prioritization of programs and projects, budget allocation, management and evaluation, in order to allow government expenditure effectively and efficiently to support economic growth and inequality reduction.",""],[1,"113","8","Government Revenue Collection and Tax Base Expansion","Enhancing the effectiveness of government revenue collection and tax base expansion in order to cover all employed persons who are required to pay tax and have accurate and completed tax forms.",""],[1,"113","8","Negative Income Tax Scheme Implementation","to expedite the implementation of a negative income tax scheme which can identify target groups by income level.",""],[1,"113","9","Environmental Tax and Surcharge Collection","This may be done by expediting the collection of an environmental tax or surcharge on products or materials that generate pollution, and on the exploitation of natural resources.",""],[1,"114","1","Local Revenue Collection Strengthening","Improving the effectiveness of revenue collection of Local Administrative Organizations in order to reduce revenue dependency on the central government.",""],[1,"114","1","Transfer of Tax and Fee Collection Functions to Local Administrative Organizations","This also includes accelerating the transfer of functions on some forms of tax and fee collection to Local Administrative Organizations so that they can determine appropriate tax rates and collection methods to be in line with the problems and demand in each local area.",""]],"88":[[1,"29","3","Financial Sector Regulatory Reform","There is necessity for the government to amend rules and regulations for the financial sector in order to enhance competitiveness, improve efficiency and fairness in service provision for consumers and private sector.",""],[1,"29","3","Financial Risk Monitoring Mechanisms","Furthermore, it is necessary to have monitoring mechanisms to avoid potential risks emanating from the changing patterns and greater volume of financial connectivity and dynamic capital movements.",""],[1,"29","3","Financial Technology and Access Expansion","Financial technology utilization, the development of financial tools for funding mega project investments, as well as an expansion of accessibility to financial services at reasonable cost are also emphasized in order to facilitate the business sector's and every other sector's access to finance services.",""],[1,"29","3","Grassroots Financial Institutions Development","Grassroots financial institutions should also be developed.",""],[1,"35","2","Financial Sector Regulatory and Security Reform","This has brought about new financial instruments including financial applications, crowd funding, and financial platforms.",""],[1,"114","3","Financial System Efficiency Enhancement Measures","To achieve these goals, it is necessary to: (i) increase competition among financial institutions; (ii) promote the use of electronic financial services such as E-Money, E-payment, as well as financial innovations in the form of Fintech (Financial Technology); and (iii) further develop the financial infrastructure by reforming laws and regulations, improving customer protection schemes, strengthening the supervision system, and improving the capabilities of human resources in the financial sector, as well as supporting any policy measures under the National E-payment Master Plan and the Thailand Digital Economy and Society Development Plan.",""],[1,"114","4","Financial Services Accessibility Network","Improving the accessibility of financial services by creating a network among financial institutions, including commercial banks, non-bank financial institutions, Specialized Financial Institutions (SFIs), and microfinance institutions.",""],[1,"115","2","Development of New Financial Innovations","Developing new financial innovations that meet the needs of all customers within the circumstance of a changing financial landscape.",""],[1,"115","2","Customer-Specific Financial Product Development","financial institutions should be encouraged to launch financial products that respond to the needs of each group of customers.",""],[1,"115","2","SME Venture Capital and Crowdfunding Support","Small and Medium Enterprises may need venture capital or crowd-funding, and so on.",""]],"89":[[1,"30","1","National Security and Social Cohesion Strengthening","National security, independence and sovereignty, social security, social cohesion, positive image, and country confidence are increased.",""],[1,"85","2","National Security and Social Conflict Reduction Measures","National sovereignty, security, safety, reconciliation and the country's confidence should be improved.",""],[1,"85","2","Anti-Crime, Anti-Piracy, Smuggling, and Human Trafficking Reduction Measures","Social ideological conflicts, crimes, and losses from piracy and the smuggling of goods and human trafficking should be reduced.",""],[1,"85","2","Citizen Terrorism and Disaster Preparedness Strengthening","Preparedness to protect citizens from terrorism and natural disasters should be strengthened.",""]],"90":[[1,"27","2","Water Resource Efficiency Improvement","Therefore, it is important to increase efficiency in water resource management, foster green growth, and clean up pollution.",""],[1,"27","2","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Preparedness","In terms of climate change, it is necessary to be prepared for greenhouse gas mitigation, raise adaptive capacity, whilst reducing natural disaster risks.",""],[1,"30","1","Natural Capital and Environmental Quality Improvement","Natural capital and environmental quality can support green growth as well as food, power, and water security by: increasing the country's forest area to cover up to 40 percent of the country's total area in order to maintain a balanced ecosystem; reducing greenhouse gas emissions in the energy and transport sectors by at least 7 percent by the year 2020, compared to a business as usual scenario; increasing efficiency in solid waste disposal; conserving and restoring the quality of water and air in severely affected areas so they should also be able to stabilize the ecosystem up to a healthy standard;",""],[1,"40","1","Climate Change Response and Sustainable Resource Management","urgently responding to climate change and related impacts.",""]],"91":[[1,"92","7","Incentives for Dual Vocational and Co-operative Education Participation","Creating more incentives designed to attract more children to take part in either Dual Vocational Education or Co-operative Education programs in order to equip them with the essential skills required by the labor market.",""],[1,"94","1","Incentive Mechanisms for Workplace Participation in Vocational Education","Promoting more incentive mechanisms aimed at attracting medium- scale workplaces to expand their potential to take part in either the Dual Vocational Education or Co-operative Education programs, as well as educating entrepreneurs/employers and coaches/mentors collaboratively to plan teaching materials and programs, and collectively evaluate learners.",""],[1,"94","2","Curriculum Development and Research-to-Innovation Cooperation","Expanding cooperation between vocational institutions, tertiary institutions, the private sector, and Thai and international experts in developing curricula for certain subject fields that Thailand is specialized in, turning research into innovation, as well as developing competency-based curricula to cover more subjects and educational levels nationwide.",""],[1,"120","2","Dual Vocational and Cooperative Education Systems","This cooperation can be done through different approaches and systems, such as a dual vocational training system, a cooperative education system, or other appropriate systems.",""]],"92":[[1,"95","1","Traffic Safety Communication Campaign","Promoting a traffic safety culture through available means of public communication that are suitable for each target groups, in order to reduce traffic accident- prone behavior, as well as setting up a systematic road traffic accident management service.",""],[1,"95","1","Systematic Road Traffic Accident Management Service","Promoting a traffic safety culture through available means of public communication that are suitable for each target groups, in order to reduce traffic accident- prone behavior, as well as setting up a systematic road traffic accident management service.",""],[1,"104","7","Patient Transfer System Improvement","Ensure full coverage of quality public health services through enhancing the efficiency of the patient transfer system from the community level through to the national level.",""]],"93":[[1,"95","3","Health Resource Management System Adjustment and Referral Emergency System Development","Adjusting the resource management system among all scales of sanatoriums under all jurisdictions located in all health areas in terms of human resources, medical equipment and related infrastructure, to be seamlessly connected in order to provide quality health care services at all community, general and regional hospitals nationwide, as well as developing fast and effective referral and emergency medical systems.",""],[1,"95","4","Health Expenditure Oversight Measures","Setting up measures designed to oversee health-related expenditures between the public sector and patients, taking into account socioeconomic status, accessibility of low-income earners to essential treatments, and the nation's public finance discipline.",""],[1,"95","5","Health Insurance System for Foreign Workers and Tourists","Developing a health insurance system for foreign workers and tourists to provide more quality coverage of healthcare services, with adequate regulations, that will not have any negative impacts on national security, in terms of both financial and public health aspects.",""],[1,"95","6","Integrated Health Insurance Database","Integrating related data and information from all health insurance systems into one database, comprising of data and information on entitled benefits, usage of service, budget disbursement and performance evaluation.",""],[1,"103","10","Community Health Access Support Mechanisms","Provide additional mechanisms to ensure accessibility of the bottom 40 percent to public health services, particularly those in remote areas.",""],[1,"103","10","Community Welfare Transport Assistance for Health Access","Mechanisms to assist and support community welfare that cover transportation expenses to the closest public health facilities should be promoted.",""],[1,"103","10","Community Proactive Health Services Expansion","Also, proactive health services e.g. counseling, control and prevention of non-communicable diseases (NCDs), and sanitation promotion should be fostered at the community level.",""],[1,"104","5","Equitable Distribution of Public Services","Distribute high-quality public services in education, health and social welfare more evenly as well as improve the business environment.",""],[1,"104","7","Disease Control Management System","At the same time, a system of management for disease control should be fostered, along with the use of technology, particularly information and communications technology, in providing distance health assistance to resolve personnel shortages in remote areas.",""],[1,"104","7","Telehealth Support for Remote Areas","At the same time, a system of management for disease control should be fostered, along with the use of technology, particularly information and communications technology, in providing distance health assistance to resolve personnel shortages in remote areas.",""],[1,"107","9","Telemedicine Support for Remote Health Services","The project aims at mitigating health personnel shortages in remote areas as well as reducing the number patients who need to travel into major cities for treatment.",""]],"94":[[1,"93","5","Monetary and Fiscal Incentives for Elderly Employment","Promoting the use of more monetary and fiscal incentives to encourage more employers to consider providing adequate employment opportunities for elderly people.",""],[1,"93","6","Elderly Employment Access Support","Promoting more marketing channels and financial sources as well as information services for elderly people to enable them to access employment opportunities in local communities.",""],[1,"96","2","Elderly-Friendly Urbanization with Universal Design","Promoting elderly-friendly urbanization with universal designs, including public transportation, buildings, public areas, and accommodation that is suitable for the quality living of elderly people and everyone in society.",""]],"95":[[1,"28","1","Logistics Sector Outward Investment Promotion","Additional strategy guidelines include development in downstream industries to bring about new economic opportunities, and promotion of entrepreneurs in the logistics sector to invest abroad.",""],[1,"109","1","Private Investment Promotion Measures","The next five years is planned as a period of Thai economic recovery and expansion by expediting investment in infrastructure and logistics, as well as creating a favorable atmosphere to encourage private investors to expand their investment, particularly in key target sectors.",""],[1,"109","1","Economic Reform Agenda for High-Income Transition","In the meantime, the coming five years will be a significant period for many aspects of economic reform in order to establish the fundamentals for Thailand to become a high-income country by 2037, in line with the twenty-year National Strategy.",""],[1,"109","1","Macroeconomic Stabilization and Fiscal Discipline Framework","The strategy for building economic strength and competitiveness emphasizes the stabilization of macroeconomic management, improving the efficiency of the financial sector, and maintaining fiscal discipline.",""]],"96":[[1,"121","1","Standards-Based Local Procurement Reform","One measure, in so-doing, is to improve the local procurement system to be more standards-focused.",""],[1,"121","1","Expansion of Compulsory Product Standards","In parallel, compulsory standards should increasingly be applied to more locally-produced and imported products.",""],[1,"121","1","Consumer Standards Awareness Campaign","On top of this, knowledge of standards and quality should be dissiminated to wider groups of consumers to create awareness and increase domestic demand for high-quality products.",""],[1,"121","1","Entrepreneur Capability Upgrading for High-Value Market Expansion","Additionally, the capabilities of Thai enterpreneurs must be enhanced to enable them to expand their markets into the high-valued-added segments, especially in creative businesses or niches markets, i.e. the elderly segment, the environment-focused segment, the health-conscious segment, the new lifestyle segment, the high-purchasing power segment, and so on.",""],[1,"130","1","Agricultural Product Standards and Certification Development","Developing the standards of targeted agricultural products (plants, fisheries and livestock) to meet international standards, as well as passing inspection and quality assurance throughout the value chain.",""],[1,"130","1","Halal and Organic Agricultural Standardization Support","Supporting the standardization of both Halal and organic agricultural products.",""],[1,"130","1","Food and Agricultural Product Certification Standards","Developing standards for the certification of food and agricultural products to create reliability and provide safety to individual customers and the country's traders.",""]],"97":[[1,"124","1","Integrated Transport Network Development","developing the transportation system in order to create a network between land, water, and air transport.",""]],"98":[[1,"124","4","Sports Industry Promotion and Value-Addition Support","Therefore, it is expedient to propose and support all dimensions of the sports industry in order to add value to the sports industry in terms of both production and business relating to sports equipment, hospitality business, hotel business, restaurant business, food supplements and beverages,",""],[1,"125","1","Sports Industry Promotion and Sports Event Support Programme","promoting sports activity to create income, as well as supporting international sporting events, hosting global sporting events, and organizing international conferences in terms of sports, sports medicine, and sports science",""],[1,"125","1","Sports Business and Entrepreneurship Promotion Initiative","promoting businesses and entrepreneurs related to sports in both the sports industry and sports-related hospitality business such as the sports equipment business, sports venue business, and athletes training business",""],[1,"125","1","Sports Awareness and Public Relations Campaign","promoting marketing and public relations activities to create awareness and for people to realize the importance of sports and encourage more sports and recreational activities",""],[1,"125","2","National Sports Policy Committee","establishing a management mechanism in the form of a national committee to be responsible for making and driving national sports policy",""],[1,"125","2","Public-Private Sports Industry Promotion","promoting the operations of the public sector and private sector in raising the levels of the sports industry",""],[1,"125","2","Sports-Specific Institutions Development","establishing sports-specific institutions in order for Thailand to become a regional hub for sports and sports science",""],[1,"136","9","Innovative Development to Create Value-Added in the Sports Industry Program","Innovative Development to Create Value-Added in the Sports Industry Program:",""],[1,"136","10","Sports Industry Innovation and Commercialization Support Program","Supporting sports industry stakeholders to create innovative research and further develop it for commercialization.",""],[1,"136","10","Sports Production and Services Value-Addition Program","Furthermore, the program also aims to increase value-added in sports production and services.",""]],"99":[[1,"125","3","Proactive Marketing and Export Promotion Initiative","Promoting proactive marketing in order to increase domestic demand and exports by focusing on creating quality and standard-achieving goods and services, creating brands, developing product packaging, exploring new markets, extending cross-border trade between Thailand and nearby countries, and creating networks of international business partnerships.",""],[1,"125","3","International Headquarters and Trading Center Support","It is also important to support the establishment of international headquarters and international trading centers (ITC), utilizing international trade and investment agreements and cooperation frameworks, and encouraging enterprises to develop the skills and talents that are relevant to gaining benefits from international trade.",""],[1,"125","4","Trade Facilitation and Trade Support Reform","Developing trade facilitation to meet international standards in infrastructure, logistics and transportation systems.",""],[1,"137","12","ONESTOP Export Service Center Improvement","Improving the ONESTOP Export Service Center (OSEC):",""],[1,"137","13","OSEC Service Improvement and National Single Window Connectivity Expansion","Improving the services of OSEC and enhancing the connectivity of the National Single Window (NSW) system for networking and to expand the service to local levels.",""]],"100":[[1,"126","1","ICT and E-Commerce Support for Entrepreneurs","Supporting entrepreneurs to invest in information and communications technology systems, use e-commerce to enhance business productivity in the manufacturing and financial sectors, marketing, management, and logistics along with progress towards the digital economy.",""],[1,"126","1","Secure Electronic Payment System Development","It is necessary that government agencies focus on developing secure electronic payment systems, developing a guarantee system for buyers and sellers that meets recognized standards and credibility, and providing support for skilled labor as well as supporting the free flow of skilled labor.","government agencies"],[1,"137","5","SME E-commerce Market Access Promotion","Promoting small and medium enterprises to be able to access both domestic and global makets via e-commerce.",""]],"101":[[1,"128","9","Smallholder Land Ownership Protection Plan","The plan to protect land ownership among small-holder farmers.",""],[1,"142","3","Public Land Boundary Resolution through One Map Project","Accelerate actions to resolve the overlapping borders of public lands by using the mapping criteria for improving public land boundaries (One Map Project).",""],[1,"143","2","Integrated Land Management System Development","Develop land management systems and resolve public land encroachment.",""],[1,"143","2","Community Common Land Rights and Economic Instruments","Apply economic instruments when providing communities with common land rights for collective use in developing the production system and creating revenue for communities.",""],[1,"143","2","Efficient Land Leasing System Reform","Design efficient land leasing systems to create opportunities in land utilization.",""],[1,"143","2","Progressive Land Tax Collection","Collect land taxes progressively.",""],[1,"143","2","Foreign Land Ownership Restriction Measures","Formulate measures that prevent land ownership by foreigners.",""],[1,"143","2","Soil and Land Conservation Measures","Conserve soil and land to retain its fertility.",""],[1,"150","6","Community Forest Bill Review and Revision","The focus should be put on the Community Forest Bill, with an emphasis on protecting communities' rights, way of life, culture and local wisdom.",""],[1,"151","1","Compensation Measures for Affected Persons","Provide compensation measure for those affected by government policies such as flooded zones and land expropriated for development projects.",""],[1,"151","6","Public Land Demarcation Map Improvement Program","Program on Improvement of Public Land Demarcation Map Scale 1:4000.",""]],"102":[[1,"128","16","Environmental Tax and Fee Enforcement","enforcement of environmental tax and fee collection from products and materials that create pollution, based on the Polluter Pays Principle",""],[1,"128","16","Local Pollution Tax Collection Initiative","encouraging Local Administrative Organizations to collect taxes or fees from polluters in their areas",""],[1,"145","3","Polluter Pays Waste Fee Reform","Review and revise the criteria and rates applied to solid waste management fees.",""],[1,"151","2","Polluter Pays Fiscal Measures Study","Conduct a study to identify proper and fair fiscal measures, following the Polluter Pays Principle (PPP), prior to putting it into effect.",""]],"103":[[1,"129","4","Specialized Financial Institutions Role Definition and Performance Enhancement","Defining precisely the role of Specialized Financial Institutions (SFIs) and their goals; (2) enhancing the competitiveness and efficiency of SFIs to help them fulfill their specific objectives and serve the function as financial institutions for development.",""],[1,"129","8","Financial Literacy and Personal Financial Management Education","Providing better knowledge and understanding on financial issues, investment tools and personal financial management to all groups of people;",""],[1,"129","8","Financial Intermediary Support for Financial Literacy Funds","encouraging financial intermediaries to engage in providing funds for projects or establishing capital funds that help improve financial literacy in order to cultivate corporate social responsibility.",""]],"104":[[1,"131","6","Animal Species and Plant Seed Banks","Preserving animal species and plant seeds so that poor farmers nationwide can obtain the breeds required to improve productivity and hence increase their income.",""],[1,"142","4","Support for Existing Gene Banks","systematically support the existing gene banks of plants, animals and microorganisms;",""]],"105":[[1,"141","3","Solid and Hazardous Waste Management Prioritization","setting the prioritization of solid waste and hazardous waste management, restoring water quality in the major rivers, and finding solutions to the haze pollution problem.",""],[1,"141","3","Major River Water Quality Restoration","setting the prioritization of solid waste and hazardous waste management, restoring water quality in the major rivers, and finding solutions to the haze pollution problem.",""],[1,"141","3","Haze Pollution Reduction Measures","setting the prioritization of solid waste and hazardous waste management, restoring water quality in the major rivers, and finding solutions to the haze pollution problem.",""],[1,"145","2","Air Pollution and Waste Control Acceleration","speed up the control of air pollution, waste water, solid and harzadous waste from production and consumption.",""],[1,"145","4","Watershed Water Quality Management Improvement","Increase the efficiency of water quality management in the main watershed areas, particularly those facing pollution crises, by reducing wastewater from",""],[1,"146","1","Wastewater Treatment and Water Quality Management Measures","Accelerate the treatment of wastewater from households and industries.",""]],"106":[[1,"146","2","Forest Fire and Haze Prevention Measures","Solve the crisis of forest fires in the north and south of Thailand.",""],[1,"146","2","Transboundary Haze Cooperation Mechanism","Collaborate with neighboring countries at the multilateral and bilateral levels, following the ASEAN Agreement on Transboundary Haze Pollution.",""],[1,"146","2","Agricultural Waste Burning Incentives and Farmer Advisory Support","Accordingly, it is important to change farmers' practices in agricultural waste burning by creating incentives, and providing knowledge and information about good agricultural practice.",""],[1,"146","2","Alternative Crop Research and Farmer Retraining Programme","Conduct research to find substitute crops which are more suitable, have higher market demand and lower cost.",""]],"107":[[1,"149","7","Post-Disaster Restoration and Reconstruction Systems","Establish restoration and reconstruction systems after the incidence of disasters.",""],[1,"149","7","Fair Disaster Victim Assistance Measures","Meet the demands of disaster victims widely and fairly.",""],[1,"149","7","Post-Disaster Inspection Standards","Leverage post-disaster inspection standards.",""],[1,"149","7","Building and Infrastructure Safety Standards Improvement","Improve safety standards of buildings and infrastructure.",""],[1,"149","7","Resilient New Infrastructure Standards","Develop safety standards of new infrastructure which should be resilient to possible extreme disasters in the future.",""],[1,"161","4","Disaster and Epidemic Response and Rehabilitation","Prevent and deal with disasters, health epidemics, as well as rehabilitation treatment after a disaster situation returns to normal.",""]],"108":[[1,"150","3","Environmental Impact Assessment Process Reform","Revise mechanisms and processes of Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) to increase efficiency at all stages, ranging from the first step of study to the last step of monitoring and inspection.",""],[1,"150","3","EIA Compliance Monitoring and Enforcement","Urge government agencies with permit-granting authority strictly to monitor and inspect mitigation measures, as indicated in the EIA report.",""],[1,"150","3","EIA Penalties for Non-Compliance","If there is no compliance, punishment measures should be applied earnestly.",""],[1,"150","3","Permit Extension EIA Monitoring Conditions","Moreover, monitoring and inspection conditions should be set as requirements when there is a request for permit extension, and/or for change or additional construction within the project.",""],[1,"150","3","EIA Procedure Streamlining","In general, the steps and duration of the EIA process should be steamlined.",""],[1,"150","3","Public Participation Review in EIA","The level and procedures of public participation in the EIA process by all stakesholders should be reviewed and revised.",""],[1,"150","4","Strategic Environmental Assessment Legal Requirement","Advocate Strategic Environmental Assessments (SEA) to be legally required as a significant tool for government decision making on certain policies.",""],[1,"150","4","Pilot Strategic Environmental Assessment Studies","Encourage pilot studies of SEA at the watershed level to support spatial management in economic development zones and critical ecosystems.",""]],"109":[[1,"150","5","Public Participation and Environmental Governance Enhancement","Create appropriate attitudes and awareness, as well as improve the process of public participation.",""],[1,"150","5","Participatory Natural Resource and Environment Fund","Establish a fund for the participatory management of natural resources and environment: encourage all stakeholders to contribute financially.",""],[1,"150","5","Environmental Justice Governance Support Mechanism","Enhance mechanisms to support good governance in environmental justice and public participation.",""],[1,"150","5","Environmental Awareness Media Campaigns","Employ the mass media to run campaigns for dissiminating ideas and good practices in natural resources and environmental management.",""],[1,"151","2","Private Sector and Community Implementation Partnership Mechanism","Enhance the role of the private sector and communites in creating synergies in implemtation.",""],[1,"151","2","Corporate Governance Partnership Support for Private Businesses","Promote private businesses that adopt corporate governance by providing them with the opportunity to work with the government and communities.",""],[1,"151","2","Restoration, Redress, and Compensation Mechanisms and Funds","Support the establishment of mechanisms and funds to restore, redress and compensate those affected people, both in the short and long terms.",""],[1,"151","2","Environmental Liability Law and Regulation Reform","Amend related laws and regulations such that business operators will be liable for their actions that bring about long-term losses to communities.",""],[1,"151","2","Natural Resources and Environment Justice Process Reform","Advance the justice process in natural resources and environment at all stages, starting from access to information, human rights protection, and proving liability.",""],[1,"151","2","Natural Resources and Environment Law Revision","Revise laws and regulations that have become a hindrance to the sustainable and fair management of natural resources and the environment.",""]],"110":[[1,"156","4","National Security Management Capacity Strengthening","To create readiness and combine the forces of all sectors in strengthening security management capabilities and the country's potential to prevent and remedy situations caused by both traditional military threats and other non-traditional security threats.",""],[1,"158","10","Security Plan Integration","Security plans will be integrated in accordance with the National Security Policy and the Economic, Social, Natural Resources and Environment Policy:",""],[1,"158","11","Urgent National Security Strategy Development","The objectives above have determined the development guidelines for the Twelfth National Economic and Social Development Plan by defining the development of an urgently needed security strategy that expedites the development of economic, social, environmental, and national security, and requires immediate action in order to achieve the target of strengthening internal security, reducing and preventing external threats, and building trust in ASEAN and the international community in the next 5 years, as follows:",""],[1,"162","4","National Security Planning and Policy Support Mechanism","Develop mechanisms for national security and systems to motivate the various work plans to handle security situations at national and local level by building a network to support policy-making, knowledge-generation and the creation of mechanisms to underpin work plans for economic and social development, natural resources and environmental protection, and national security.",""],[1,"163","2","National Strategy for Combating Money Laundering and Terrorism Financing","National Strategy for Combating Money Laundering and the Financing Of Terrorism, 2016-2020;",""],[1,"163","2","National Security Strategy to Prevent and Tackle Global Terrorism","Draft National Security Strategy to Prevent and Tackle Global Terrorism, Year ....;",""],[1,"163","2","National Security Strategy to Prevent and Tackle Transnational Threats","National Security Strategy to Prevent and Tackle Transnational Threats, 2015-2021;",""],[1,"163","2","Strategic Plan to Prevent and Resolve Drug Problems","Strategic Plan to Prevent and Resolve Drug Problems, 2015-2019;",""],[1,"163","2","Drug Prevention and Resolution Publicity Campaign","Action Plan for Publicity Campaign to Prevent and Resolve Drug Problems, 2015-2019.",""]],"111":[[1,"143","3","Integrated Marine and Coastal Resource Management","Protect marine resources and prevent coastal erosion.",""],[1,"143","4","Mineral Resource Management and Mining Regulation Reform","Plan and manage mineral resources to optimize their utilization whilst minimizing the impacts on the environment and human beings.",""],[1,"144","1","Community-Mining Conflict Reduction Mechanisms","mechanisms to reduce conflicts between communities and mining operators, bearing in mind community rights and social justice.",""],[1,"160","6","River Bank Protection Infrastructure Development","Support the development of physical infrastructure to prevent land loss and natural disasters, such as river bank protection works along the borders with neighboring countries.",""],[1,"161","6","Maritime Security Cooperation and Safe Sea Transport Mechanism","Strengthen local and international cooperation in maintaining maritime security to resolve overlapping maritime claims; develop cooperation in seeking and expediting the sustainable use of maritime natural resources; develop systems and mechanisms for effective prevention and mitigation systems at sea; and maintain safe maritime transportation that contributes to mutual benefits.",""],[1,"161","7","National Maritime Security and Resource Protection Mechanism","maintaining the security of national maritime resources and the environmental protection, prevention, and preservation of maritime national interests from maritime offenses and maritime crises; develop practical mechanisms to safeguard national maritime interests; revise related laws and regulations to be up-to-date and cosmopolitan with a unified, effective and efficient management system to maintain the entirety of national maritime security and national maritime interests, together with integrating the use of resources, mobilization and policy into tangible practices.",""],[1,"162","1","Maritime Knowledge and Innovation Development","knowledge about the laws related to maritime activities, as well as promote the development of maritime knowledge and innovation that will benefit future development.",""]],"112":[[1,"163","5","National Maritime Security Plan","National Maritime Security Plan, 2015-2021",""],[1,"163","5","Measures to Promote Investment in the Merchant Navy","Measures to Promote Investment in the Merchant Navy",""],[1,"165","6","Maritime Security and Management System Development","the aim is to enhance maritime security and develop a good maritime management system by troubleshooting controversies over maritime resources; maintaining the security of the national maritime resources; strengthening environmental protection, preservation of national maritime interests and prevention of maritime offenses and maritime crises; developing practical mechanisms to assist maritime accidents, maritime rescue and disaster relief efficiently and effectively; and revising related laws and regulations to be up-to-date and cosmopolitan.",""]],"113":[[1,"164","5","Counter-Terrorism and Transnational Threat Cooperation Mechanism","create cooperation within and between countries at all levels.",""],[1,"164","5","Legislative and Law Enforcement Strengthening for Security Threats","Improve legislation and law enforcement to address the issues by developing the intelligence system and the mechanisms for emergency response, promoting human resource development and the modernization and development of equipment, together with the exchange of information with allied countries to support the efficient and effective combatting of terrorism and transnational threats such as drugs and human trafficking.",""]],"114":[[1,"168","12","Integrated Public Policy Management Reform","Improving public policy management to be more integrated, and to be able to support efficiently the production process of goods and services in accordance with the long-term Strategic Plan.",""],[1,"172","1","Public Governance Remodelling under Pra-Cha-Rath","Remodelling public governance in order to leverage the participation of the public sector, private sector, citizens, and civil society, according to the principle of \"Pra- Cha-Rath\".",""],[1,"180","1","Public Service Provision Support for Private and Other Sectors","Providing full support for the private sector and other sectors to improve overall public service provision, both in terms of quantity and quality, leading to high-quality public service provision which is accessible to the people and well-organized.",""]],"115":[[1,"170","2","State Enterprise Long-Term Development Strategy Review","Initiating strategies for the long-term development of state enterprises that are clear and applicable, together with reviewing their missions' compliance with the prevailing situation and needs of each state enterprise, according to its functional objectives.",""],[1,"170","3","State-Owned Enterprise Merger and Restructuring","Merging acquiring, transferring or restructuring SOEs to reduce redundancy in cases where the private sector or other government agencies already provide the same service more efficiently.",""],[1,"170","4","State Enterprise Restructuring and Strategic Management Reform","Restructuring state enterprises in order that they perform their missions efficiently.",""],[1,"170","5","SOE Regulatory and Supervisory Framework Reform","Enhancing the regulatory and supervisory framework for SOEs to bring them into line with the industry situations in which they are placed, and clearly separating the roles of policy-makers, regulators and operators in order to underpin transparency and fairness.",""]],"116":[[1,"172","8","Local Administration Organization Management Efficiency Improvement","Improve the management efficiency of Local Administration Organizations (LAOs), so people are able to receive efficient services that are accessible to all, and stakeholders have a chance to participate in developments.",""],[1,"172","8","Local Administration Organization Fiscal Autonomy and Service Standardization","Additionally, LAOs are to become more flexible, more financially independent in the long-run, depend less on public subsidy budgets, as well as be able to provide standardized basic public services efficiently by:",""],[1,"172","9","Decentralization and Mission Transfer Procedures to Provincial Administrations","Identifying clear procedures for decentralization and mission transfer to provincial administrations, especially in the fields of education and public health.",""],[1,"173","1","Independent Local Potential Assessment Offices","the accurate and clear evaluation of local potential by independent assessors' offices should be encouraged.",""],[1,"173","1","Decentralization Control Mechanisms","mechanisms and controlling measures for decentralization should be clearly established.",""],[1,"173","2","Local Public Service Development Support","Supporting LAOs to develop various public services which directly respond to the public's requirements, using participatory approaches among LAOs, the private sector and civil society.",""],[1,"173","4","Local Administrative Organization Decentralization and Governance Reform","Promoting decentralization by allowing LAOs the flexibility to formulate policies, manage human resources, undertake financial, fiscal and budgeting management, and encouraging LAOs to partner with other stakeholders in accordance with good governance frameworks.",""]],"117":[[1,"173","3","Local Revenue Mobilization Support","Furthermore, the capability to mobilize additional sources of income besides tax systems should also be supported.",""],[1,"173","5","Local Government Revenue and Tax Decentralization Reform","Restructuring the revenues of central and local governments, as well as the tax structures of LAOs, by providing subsidies in accordance with their roles and missions, together with considering, as appropriate, the decentralization of tax collection to LAOs",""],[1,"173","6","Local Administrative Organization Non-Tax Revenue Reform","Revising laws and measures to increase LAOs' non-tax revenues, which includes fees or revenue from businesses, social enterprises, and area-based development, or other non-tax revenues which can be obtained in the future.",""],[1,"173","7","Provincial Financial and Fiscal Management Strengthening","Strengthening provincial financial and fiscal management and providing control and monitoring measures for revenue collection by LAOs, both tax and non-tax.",""],[1,"173","7","LAO Investment Project and Loan Appraisal Guidelines","Additionally, project assessment guidelines, decision-making criteria for investment project proposals and loan applications, and feasibility analysis of LAO indebtedness capacity should all be clearly established.",""],[1,"173","7","LAO Expenditure and Debt Data System Development","Data systems concerning LAOs' expenditures and debts should also be developed to be accurate and up-to-date.",""]],"118":[[1,"174","5","Political Party System Renewal and Participatory Monitoring","Attracting young-blood politicians with high moral standards to assume positions in the political sector through the political party system, and to foster active participatory monitoring systems from all sectors.",""],[1,"174","7","Media Codes of Conduct Promotion and Self-Supervision","Promoting codes of conduct in media groups through professional associations and self-supervision.",""],[1,"174","7","Public Participatory Media Monitoring Approach","Also, a public participatory approach should be promoted to monitor the media.",""]],"119":[[1,"182","11","Honesty School Campaign","Promoting morality, ethics and good governance in education institutions, as one of the activities in the \"Honesty School\" concept campaign in order to build the knowledge and the skillsets required for learning processes that are adaptable to changing contexts and environments.",""],[1,"182","11","Values and Integrity Development in Education Institutions","Furthermore, cultivating desirable attributes, analytical skills, discipline, integrity, and the application of the Sufficiency Economy into the way of living and the public mindset should be encouraged.",""]],"120":[[1,"184","4","Energy Security and Clean Energy Expansion","To ensure energy security, improve energy efficiency, increase the use of alternative and clean energy, and expand Thailand's energy-related business opportunities in ASEAN.",""],[1,"194","2","Power Generation Fuel Diversification","Diversifying the types of fuels for power generation, as planned in Thailand's Power Development Plan, and according to each area's potential.",""],[1,"194","2","Area-Based Electricity Transmission and Distribution Planning","Related agencies should plan the development of transmission and distribution systems according to each area's demand for electricity, potential for power generation, and existing power supply.",""],[1,"194","2","Area-Based Electricity Tariff Structure Study","Regulating offices should conduct studies to find an appropriate structure for electricity tariff rates that vary by area, and examine its effects compared to the existing uniform tariff structure in terms of its ability to reflect the costs of producing and transmitting electricity.",""],[1,"194","3","Natural Gas Pipeline and LNG Terminal Development","Thailand should develop its natural gas pipeline networks and LNG terminals to accommodate increasing demand and improve competitiveness among natural gas businesses, while continuing to develop a third-party access regime with a fair price structure.",""],[1,"194","3","Third-Party Access Regime for Natural Gas Infrastructure","Thailand should develop its natural gas pipeline networks and LNG terminals to accommodate increasing demand and improve competitiveness among natural gas businesses, while continuing to develop a third-party access regime with a fair price structure.",""],[1,"194","3","Oil Pipeline Investment for Transport Efficiency","Thailand should continue to invest in oil pipelines to increase efficiency in oil transportation.",""],[1,"195","3","Energy Business Regulatory Process Reform","Improve regulatory processes for energy businesses, incorporating transparency and good governance practices, as well as increasing the adaptability of regulations and regulatory processes to changes in the energy markets in order to prepare Thailand for energy market liberalization in the future.",""],[1,"195","3","Cost-Reflective Energy Pricing Framework","Regulatory offices should also determine a cost-reflective pricing structure to give both producers and consumers the greatest net benefit.",""],[1,"195","4","ASEAN Energy Trading Hub Promotion","Promote Thailand to become ASEAN's energy trading hub and increase opportunities for Thailand to expand its energy businesses in ASEAN by:",""],[1,"195","5","Domestic Energy Infrastructure Upgrading","Upgrading domestic energy-related infrastructure in terms of quality, reliability, and efficiency to be ready to connect to an ASEAN energy grid.",""],[1,"195","5","Energy Laws and Regulations Revision","Laws and regulations should also be revised to prepare Thailand to become ASEAN's energy hub and to accommodate the expansion of Thai energy businesses to the region.",""],[1,"195","6","Regional Energy Collaboration and Joint Electricity Network Development","Pushing for regional energy collaboration in developing a joint electricity network and to achieve shared refined oil standards to increase opportunities for investment and energy development.",""],[1,"195","6","Support for Neighboring Countries' Energy Infrastructure Development","Thailand should assist neighboring countries in developing energy infrastructure and their other endeavors regarding energy development to help strengthen the economy and cultivate good relationships among the ASEAN community.",""],[1,"195","7","Cross-Border Expansion of Energy State-Owned Enterprises","Encouraging Thailand's energy-related state-owned enterprises to take their expertise outside Thailand and expand their businesses to neighboring countries.",""],[1,"202","5","Floating Storage and Regasification Unit Development","The development of a floating storage and regasification unit (FSRU), carried out by the Ministry of Energy, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Energy"]],"121":[[1,"197","7","Sectoral Water Consumption Management Plans","Developing water consumption management plans by sector, as well as implementing 3R measures (Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle) and wastewater fees in order to promote water-saving behavior and awareness in the residential, business, and industrial sectors.",""],[1,"197","8","Water Production Technology Research and Application Programme","Promoting research by both the public and private sectors on water production technology, in particular low-cost water desalination technology, water transmission efficiency, water saving innovations or tools for the residential, business and industrial sectors, as well as encouraging the application of this research in water supply operations for commercial and social benefits.",""],[1,"197","9","Non-Revenue Water Reduction and Water Supply Maintenance","Proactively reduce non-revenue water as well as undertake maintenance to prevent wastage and leakages from the water supply system nationwide by:",""],[1,"197","10","Non-Revenue Water Reduction Plans in Provincial Areas","Developing non-revenue water reduction plans in provincial areas with high non-revenue water rates, with definite operational areas, scope of tasks, non-",""],[1,"198","2","Private Sector Participation in Water Loss Reduction","Increasing the private sector's participation in water loss reduction, encouraging technical knowledge transfer between public and private personnel, and raising collaboration levels with provincial authorities, providing them with technical and operational assistance in non-revenue water reduction.",""],[1,"198","3","Non-Revenue Water Management Technology Upgrade","Upgrading the information technology used in non-revenue water management to be in accordance with international standards, and increasing the adoption of this technology for better control of water pressures and management of water losses.",""]],"122":[[1,"198","4","Water Works Governance Restructuring and Regulatory Authority Law","Restructure water works management by differentiating between policy making authorities, regulatory authorities, and operational authorities.",""]],"123":[[1,"188","5","Road Capacity Expansion and Expressway Upgrade Programme","The country should increase road capacity in bottle-neck areas.",""],[1,"188","5","Border Gateway Expressway and Motorway Upgrade Programme","The expressway and motorway network around border crossing areas and important gateways should be upgraded and expanded to serve the increasing passenger and freight traffic resulting from",""],[1,"189","1","Border Crossing Expansion and Transport Connectivity Enhancement","The priority areas include the Padang Besar Border Crossing and the Ban Phunamron Border Crossing.",""],[1,"200","2","Intercity Motorway and Road Widening Projects","Key road network development projects include intercity motorway projects connecting border areas, special economic zones, and major trade gateways such as the Songkhla-border (Malaysia) section and the Kanchanaburi-Ban Phu Nam Ron border section, as well as road widening projects from 2 to 4 lanes to meet increasing passenger and freight transportation demand along Highway 33 (the Prachin Buri-Kabin Buri section) and Highway 408 (the Songkhla-Thungwang section).","Department of Highways | Department of Rural Roads"],[1,"201","1","Road Safety Rest Area Construction","Other related projects are the construction of rest areas to increase road safety.",""]],"124":[[1,"185","6","Airport Capacity Expansion","to expand the capacity of the Bangkok airports and of regional airports to meet increasing demand from passengers",""],[1,"189","3","Airport Expansion and Regional Airport Utilization Planning","Completing the extensions of Suvarnabhumi Airport and Don Mueang Airport by 2021 according to the Airport Master Plan, as well as conducting feasibility studies for future airport expansion to accommodate air transportation demand after Suvarnabhumi Airport and Don Mueang Airport have reached their maximum capacities.",""],[1,"189","3","Regional Airport Utilization and Maintenance Plan","Utilization and maintenance plans for existing regional airports should also be developed.",""],[1,"189","3","Feasibility Studies for Potential Airport Utilization","Feasibility studies on increasing the utilization of other potential airports should also be conducted, for instance U-Tapao Airport to be used to support Thailand's aviation industry.",""],[1,"189","4","Airport Management Performance Improvement","Improving airport management performance to ensure that the quality of services in passenger and goods transportation, the qualifications of staff, the readiness of equipment, and the processes of emergency respons are all in accordance with international standards, including those established by the International Civil Aviation Organization (ICAO), the European Aviation Organization (EASA), the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), and the Japan Civil Aviation Bureau (JCAB).",""],[1,"189","5","Airspace Management Organizational Structure Development","Developing the organizational structure of airspace management in order to improve airspace utilization to cope with future air traffic demand, reduce flight delays, better facilitate air traffic control, and increase the competitiveness of Thailand's aviation sector.",""],[1,"200","3","Suvarnabhumi Airport Development","The Suvarnabhumi Airport Development, carried out by the Airport of Thailand Public Company Limited, with a timeline of 7 years and 5 years (2011-2017 and 2017-2021),",""],[1,"200","4","Don Mueang Airport Development","The Don Mueang Airport Development, carried out by the Airport of Thailand Public Company Limited, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).",""],[1,"200","5","Mae Sot Airport Development","The Maesot Airport Development, carried out by the Department of Airports, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Department of Airports"],[1,"200","7","U-Tapao Airport Development","The U-Tapao Airport Development, carried out by the Royal Thai Navy and the Airport of Thailand Public Company Limited, with a timeline of 5 years (2017- 2021).",""]],"125":[[1,"187","5","Logistics Facilities and Service Centers Development","Developing logistics facilities and service centers (e.g. distribution centers, cargo terminals, and container lifting equipment) to serve multimodal transportation along the strategic routes connecting industrial and agricultural manufacturing bases to major trade gateways, especially international ports and important border areas.",""],[1,"189","6","Existing Ports Utilization and Port Network Development","To ensure optimal use of existing infrastructure, the Marine Department and Local Administrative Organizations should operate in collaboration with related agencies to study appropriate management and marketing schemes, find ways to increase demand for the existing coastal and river ports, and create a network connecting river and coastal ports to the major deep sea ports in Thailand.","Marine Department | Local Administrative Organizations"],[1,"190","1","Laem Chabang Deep Sea Port PPP Regulation and Monitoring","Regulating and monitoring public-private partnership contractors at the Laem Chabang deep sea port, increasing the level of services at the port to be on par with the world's leading deep sea ports, and preparing Laem Chabang deep sea port's third expansion phase with active public participation.",""],[1,"200","10","Laem Chabang Deep-Sea Port Development Plan Phase 3","The Laem Chabang Deep-Sea Port Development Plan (Phase 3), carried out by the Port Authority of Thailand, with a timeline of 5 years (2016-2020).","Port Authority of Thailand"],[1,"201","1","Intermodal Freight Transport Facilities Development","Plans and projects to develop facilities supporting intermodal freight transportation include the construction of intermodal facilities, cargo terminals, and container yards near key trade gateways and potential areas in order to shift from road transportation to rail and waterway transportation.",""]],"126":[[1,"189","2","Intelligent Transport Systems for Bangkok Traffic Management","Using Intelligent Transport Systems (ITS) technology to integrate all transportation data in the Bangkok Metropolitan Area in order to monitor and control traffic in real time and be able to provide travelers with information to plan their commute.",""],[1,"190","2","Transportation Technology and Workforce Development Programme","Supporting the research and development of transportation- related technology and innovation along with human resources to raise the capacity of the country to provide world-class transportation services, and for its transportation workforce to be equipped with up-to-date skills and be adaptable to changing technology and standards.",""],[1,"190","5","Department of Rail Transportation Formation","Accelerating the formation of the Department of Rail Transportation, which would act as a regulatory unit for rail operators, set standards for safety and maintenance, establish a price structure and required quality of services, put in place measures to help increase the role of the private sector in rail businesses, and ensure consumer protection.",""],[1,"190","5","State Railway of Thailand Restructuring","The country should also expedite the restructuring of the State Railway of Thailand to increase the efficiency of its services in passenger and freight transportation.",""],[1,"191","1","Air and Waterway Transport Regulatory Capacity Upgrade","Advancing the capabilities of air and waterway transportation regulatory agencies by improving their human resources and equipment, as well as updating their regulatory frameworks to be in accordance with changes in technology and forms of services.",""]],"127":[[1,"191","4","Logistics Management Upgrading and Supply Chain Value-Addition Support","Advance the country's logistics management to meet international standards, and support value-added processes across the supply chain by:",""],[1,"191","5","Industrial Logistics Management Upgrading","Upgrading logistics management in the industrial sector by encouraging businesses to increase their adoption of information technology in managing their logistics, and promoting the transition to digital logistics and supply chain management.",""],[1,"191","5","Modern and Green Enterprise Capability Improvement","Business management capabilities should be improved according to international standards for modern and green enterprises.",""],[1,"191","5","Spatial Logistics Network Development","Spatial logistics management should be developed by creating networks that connect the sources of raw materials to production bases and to markets in order to support related local industries, including manufacturing and tourism.",""],[1,"191","5","Enterprise Emergency Planning and Risk Management","The government should also encourage enterprises to plan for emergency situations and implement risk management.",""],[1,"191","6","Agricultural Logistics and Supply Chain Efficiency Improvement","Improving logistics management in the agricultural sector by working to increase the overall efficiency of logistics and the supply chain in the sector,",""],[1,"192","1","Farm-to-Fork Value Chain Development","developing a Farm-to-Fork value chain for farmers, agricultural institutions, and businesses, and upgrading agricultural logistics infrastructure (e.g. facilities to sort, process, package, and distribute) for shared use in local communities.",""],[1,"192","2","Thai Logistics Service Provider Competitiveness Upgrade","Increasing the competitiveness of Thai logistics service providers (LSPs) by raising the capabilities and standards of Thai LSPs in providing shipping and insurance services that are comparable with international standards.",""],[1,"192","2","Digital Efficiency Upgrades for Logistics Management","LSPs should also use information technology to help increase efficiency in transportation management, backhaul management, and product tracking.",""],[1,"192","2","Thai Business and Logistics Partnership Promotion","Building business partnerships between Thai business owners and Thai LSPs should be encouraged to raise the market share of Thai companies in the logistics service industry.",""],[1,"192","2","Logistics Investment Tax Incentives and Financial Support","Tax incentives or other financial measures should be given to logistics service providers to boost investment and help logistics businesses expand in the region.",""],[1,"192","2","Overseas Logistics Business Consulting Units","Business consulting units should be established abroad to provide local information and guidance for Thai businesses to help them invest in and build logistics businesses in potential markets.",""],[1,"192","3","Private Sector Logistics Investment Incentives","Encouraging private sector investments in logistics-related industries, as well as the research and development of logistics technology and innovations (e.g., shipment tracking systems, lifting equipment, and maintenance tools used in logistics activities), by using financial measures or investment incentives.",""],[1,"201","2","Industrial and Agricultural Logistics and Supply Chain Management Plan","Plans to enhance industrial and agricultural logistics and supply chain management, carried out by the Ministry of Industry and the Ministry of Agriculture and Cooperatives, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Industry | Ministry of Agriculture and Cooperatives"],[1,"201","3","Competitiveness Enhancement for Logistics Service Providers","Competitiveness enhancement for logistics service providers, carried out by the Ministry of Commerce, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Ministry of Commerce"]],"128":[[1,"185","10","National Single Window System Expansion","to develop further the National Single Window (NSW) system to be fully integrated and able to handle electronically all information exchanged in the import/export process",""],[1,"185","10","Border Freight Transportation Efficiency Improvement","to increase the efficiency of freight transportation at border crossings that connect to the main transportation network",""],[1,"192","4","National Single Window Trade Facilitation Agency","3.3.2 Enhance trade facilitation mechanisms to meet global standards by accelerating the establishment of an agency to invest in, further develop and manage the National Single Window (NSW) system.",""],[1,"192","4","Revision of Import and Export Regulatory Procedures","The regulatory procedures for imports and exports, such as licensing and certification approval procedures, should be revised, especially for five pilot goods including sugar, rice, rubber, frozen goods, and hazardous substances.",""],[1,"192","4","Electronic Single-Entry Trade Data Integration","NSW system development should be accelerated to achieve a complete network integration for import/export and logistics data, linking both government agencies and the private sector (G2B), and to be able to operate electronically as a single entry service.",""],[1,"192","4","Trade Facilitation and Logistics Legal Reform","Legal and regulatory mechanisms concerning trade facilitation and logistics activities should be improved, especially for key gateways along major ports, airports, and borders, as well as speeding up the enactment of new regulations related to international electronic transactions.",""]],"129":[[1,"185","10","Logistics Workforce Productivity Improvement","to raise the productivity of the logistics workforce",""],[1,"192","5","Logistics Human Resource and Planning Enhancement","The emphasis should be on escalating workforce productivity through promoting collaboration among the business sector and educational institutes (vocational colleges, universities and training institutes) in revising both vocational and university-level educational programs and organizing training in both operational and technical skills.",""],[1,"192","6","Logistics Development Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","Develop a mechanism to monitor closely and evaluate Thailand's logistics development, focusing on the performance of government agencies according to",""],[1,"193","1","Logistics Development Monitoring Mechanism","The mechanism will also monitor any changes to international agreements and collaborations, both bilateral and multilateral, that affect logistics development, including the WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement and the Trans-Pacific Partnership (TPP).",""],[1,"193","1","Logistics Database Development","Other developments of logistics databases, such as logistics databases for the agricultural, industrial, and commercial sectors as well as key performance indicators, are encouraged.",""],[1,"201","6","Logistics and Supply Chain Database and Monitoring Mechanism","The development of a logistics and supply chain database and indicators along with a monitoring mechanism for changes in international agreements, carried out by the Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board, with a timeline of 5 years (2017-2021).","Office of the National Economic and Social Development Board"]],"130":[[1,"207","2","Public-Private Partnership Investment for Technology Development","Thailand should attach great importance to public private partnership (PPP) investment",""],[1,"207","2","Strategic Industry Competitiveness and Technopreneur Development Funds","by establishing funds such as strategic industry competitiveness funds and technopreneur development funds.",""],[1,"207","2","High-Risk Disruptive Technology Investment","the government should invest in higher- risk disruptive technology, including the concept of reverse engineering, and concentrate on mega project investment in order to promote the development of science, technology, research, and innovation.",""],[1,"208","2","Private Sector R&D Support and Public-Private Technology Partnership Measures","Thailand should revise regulations and issue measures to support private sector investment in R&D, and provide opportunities for the private sector in conducting research for the government.",""],[1,"208","3","Innovation Support Measures for Agriculture, Industry, and Services","Promote innovative creation, especially in design and technology- related business management by issuing measures to support the agricultural, industrial, and service sectors to create innovations, and enhance capability and competitiveness such as through funds, tax incentives, and low interest rate loans, etc.",""],[1,"208","4","Startup and SME Capital, Research Collaboration, and Technology Services Support","Support start-ups and SMEs to access capital and funds, to work with researchers and specialists in education institutes and research institutes, and to access technology-related services provided by government.",""],[1,"210","3","New Financial Tools for Innovation Financing","Support new financial tools as funding mechanisms: such as joint ventures, funds, and money markets in order to enhance innovation creation, research translation, and commercialization.",""],[1,"210","5","R&D Translation and Commercialization Promotion Act","Encourage and accelerate legislation for research translation and commercialization: e.g. a (proposed) R&D Translation and Commercialization Promotion Act, B.E. .... , which will offer opportunities for the private sector to own technology and innovation funded by the government, and to be flexible to pass on technology and innovation to the agricultural, industrial, and service sectors.",""],[1,"211","11","Thai Entrepreneur Innovation and Joint Venture Support","Promote Thai entrepreneurs to play a leadership role, and use innovation to create value in their goods and services, consisting of sub-projects such as joint venture projects, in order to provide the technology needed for a leap in business growth.",""],[1,"242","1","Entrepreneurship Development and Innovation Support","Enhancing new generations of entrepreneurs equipped with technology and innovation, and guiding research and development, technology and innovation, management, and branding to add value to businesses, products, and services.",""]],"131":[[1,"207","3","Inclusive Technology Research and Development Investment","Invest in R&D and technology for society to promote inclusive growth and quality of life, such as educational technology, information and communication technology (ICT), technology for the disabled and the elderly, as well as medical technology (medicines, vaccines, and medical equipment).",""],[1,"207","3","Multi-Stakeholder Technology Development Network","These groups of technological advancement should be developed through networks of education institutes, research institutes, the public sector, the private sector, and civil society.",""],[1,"207","4","R&D and Technology Transfer Support to Farmers, Community Enterprises, and SMEs","Accelerate R&D and technology transfer to farmers, community enterprises, and SMEs by hiring technology transfer specialists through networks involving education institutes, research institutes, the public sector, and the private sector.",""],[1,"208","5","Community Learning Centers and Innovation Promotion Initiative","Provide a proper environment for districts and communities to learn and develop creative thinking by developing learning centers, providing innovative/creative idea-sharing spaces, searching for role models, and promoting innovative products and successful innovation models to be well-known and widely used.",""],[1,"208","6","Science and Technology Public Engagement Campaign","Promote a campaign to increase people's engagement in R&D, increase people's respect for IP, and increase logical thinkers by using media, activities, and mechanisms which will pass on science and technology knowledge and services to every district and community.",""],[1,"210","4","R&D Facilities Sharing Initiative","Promote the sharing of R&D facilities, such as tools, equipment, and laboratories among research institutes, education institutes, the public sector, and the private sector.",""],[1,"211","3","Provincial Research and Studies Support Programme","Promote research and studies consistent with area and provincial development to support provincial/provincial cluster development plans.",""],[1,"211","4","Science, Technology, and Innovation Knowledge Exchange and Advisory Capacity Strengthening","Encourage knowledge exchange and in-depth development in science, technology, research, and innovation via existing mechanisms, such as promoting the capability of the science, technology, and innovation councils in order to recruit specialists in science, engineering, and related fields to advise the government and the public on science, technology, research, and innovation development.",""],[1,"211","4","Science Diplomacy for Policy Planning and Implementation","Moreover, it is important to promote science diplomacy in order to exchange knowledge in policy planning and implementation with other countries.",""],[1,"211","10","Support for Organizational Research and Innovation Action Plans","Supporting involved organizations to create action plans on research and innovation in different fields such as agriculture, industry, tourism, sports, and so on.",""],[1,"249","11","Agriculture and Agro-based Technology Exchange Programme","Agriculture and Agro-based Technology Exchange through research and development of public agencies, the private sector, and the academia (2017-2021).",""]],"132":[[1,"208","8","STEM Personnel and Education System Strengthening","Increase, both qualitatively and quantitatively, the science and technology personnel who are needed in labor market, especially in the STEM (Science: S, Technology: T, Engineer: E, Mathematics: M) subjects by drawing people's attention to these fields, motivating people, supporting funds, and so on in order to increase the number of graduates, lecturers, and personnel in STEM, and enhance the STEM-related educational system.",""],[1,"209","1","Researcher Development and Management Initiative","Accelerate the development of researchers especially in such occupations as production engineers, physicians, data scientists, designers and others, consistent with the development of strategic industries and national growth.",""],[1,"209","2","Researcher Capability Enhancement and Feasibility Study Use","Enhance researcher capability in order to understand technology, markets, business management, IP management, and end-users by prioritizing market needs.",""],[1,"209","3","Tax Incentives for Strategic Industry Talent Attraction","Use tax incentive channels to attract specialists, researchers, and scientists in strategic industries from abroad to work in public and private institutes to strengthen the country's R&D, and use tax incentives to support technology development in the agricultural, industrial, and service sectors.",""],[1,"228","11","Vocational Education Standards Improvement","Improve educational standards in vocational education, especially in the fields of engineering and technology.",""],[1,"229","7","Labor Skills Development and Industrial Upgrading Initiative","Develop labor skills while employing advanced technology and conducting research and development to upgrade manufacturing and service standards.",""],[1,"249","4","Labor Skills and Standards Improvement for Skilled Labor Mobility","to improve labor skills and uplift labor standards with neighboring countries to support skilled labor movement, and increase labor competitiveness to accommodate an expanded labor market under the IMT-GT.",""],[1,"249","5","Joint Labor Skill Certification","Joint Labor Skill Certification (2017-2021).",""],[1,"249","6","Labor Skill Standard and Certification","Labor Skill Standard and Certification, in accordance with the ASEAN Qualification Reference Framework (AQRF) (2017-2021).",""],[1,"250","10","Human Capital Strengthening and Labor Market Access Initiative","to strengthen human capital, apply innovation to enhance learning ability, and increase employment opportunity and access to the labor market, particularly regional labor mobility and employment.",""],[1,"251","1","Labor Skills and Competency Improvement Initiative","labor skill and competency improvement,",""]],"133":[[1,"209","4","Research System Development for Priority Technologies","Improve and develop an effective research system to support new significant technology: such as ICT, graphene, educational technology, technology to support demographic changes and to enhance the quality of life (technology for elderly and disabled), technology which will add agricultural product value, transportation and logistics technology, green technology, and future technology.",""],[1,"209","4","Space Industry R&D Promotion","Furthermore, Thailand should promote R&D and technology in the space industry, and develop user-friendly indexes and databases for science, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"209","4","Science, Technology, and Innovation Index and Database Development","Furthermore, Thailand should promote R&D and technology in the space industry, and develop user-friendly indexes and databases for science, technology, and innovation.",""],[1,"209","5","Science and Technology Infrastructure Enhancement","Enhance science and technology infrastructure to support fast-changing technology: by promoting research center investment, focusing on competent areas of development, and providing proper measures.",""],[1,"209","5","Domestic and International R&D Partnership Promotion","Moreover, Thailand should promote domestic and international R&D partnerships, particularly in strategic industrial research centers, and also encourage industrial estate modification into science business parks.",""],[1,"209","5","Science Park and Research Institute Network Development","Other important activities cover promoting the private sector to invest in science business parks, developing and promoting all science parks and research institutes in Thailand to work with networks (academic sector, private sector, and civil society) in order to solve critical problems in the agricultural, industrial, and service sectors.",""],[1,"210","8","Research Institute Capability Evaluation","Evaluate research institutes' capabilities in terms of science, technology, research, and innovation capability, management systems, monitoring and",""],[1,"211","2","Technology Roadmap and R&D Strategic Plan","Launch a Technology Roadmap and R&D strategic plan in important sectors in order to prioritize programs/activities in the strategic industries, including the agricultural sector, industrial sector, tourism sector, and sports sector, in accordance with the science, technology, research, and innovation strategic plans.",""]],"134":[[1,"207","5","Thai Invention and Innovation Database Registration System Improvement","Develop the Thai technology and innovation market by improving the registration system for the Thai Invention Database and Thai Innovation Database Programs, the government procurement programs.",""],[1,"208","1","Intellectual Property System Modernization","Promote an effective world class IP system to create value-added products and a user-friendly IP database.",""],[1,"210","1","Quality Systems and National Metrology Development","Promote quality systems, standards systems, and national metrology systems: including measurement, calibration, and accreditation to be in line with international standards.",""],[1,"210","1","Private Sector Metrology Center Support","Thailand should enhance and develop the private sector's world class metrology centers in the country through providing proper funds and incentives.",""],[1,"212","6","Thai Goods and Services Standards and Innovation Database Listing Support","Support Thai goods and services to meet appropriate standards and be listed on the Thai Invention Database and the Thai Innovation Database Programs for procurement.",""],[1,"248","16","Halal Standards Harmonization and Standardization Program","Harmonization and Standardization of Halal Standards through the Halal Verification System, Halal Education and Research, Halal Logistics and Supply Chain, and Laboratory Program (2017-2021).",""],[1,"249","1","Halal Verification System for Entrepreneurs","Halal Verification System for Entrepreneurs (2017-2021).",""]],"135":[[1,"210","6","Public Science, Technology, Research, and Innovation Organization Restructuring","Restructure public organizations and their role in integrating the country's operation of science, technology, research, and innovation development, including organizations that are responsible for policy formulation, research funding, undertaking research, knowledge management, and so on.",""],[1,"210","7","Program-Based Budgeting Reform","Improve government budgeting systems, from functional- based budgeting into program-based budgeting in order to integrate programs, activities and budgets between public organizations, and decide on strategic plans or exit plans.",""]],"136":[[1,"217","7","Agro-processing and Food Industry Development in Nakhon Ratchasima","Developing Nakhon Ratchasima to become the center of agro-processing and food industries by: (1.1) supporting research and development activities to enhance regional food-industry competitiveness, and (1.2) encouraging networking of the private sector, local scholars, and government agencies to share their knowledge, information, technology, and innovations for the agro-processing and food industries in order to produce high value-added products to meet the market demand.",""],[1,"218","1","Thai Silk and OTOP Product Upgrading Initiative","(2) Upgrading the standards of Thai silk commodities, cotton and indigo-dyed cotton fabrics, including fostering the high-potential provinces such as Khon Kaen, Nakhon Ratchasima, Surin, and Sakon Nakhon to become international fashion centers by: (2.1) supporting the development of product quality, design, and branding, (2.2) developing technology and innovation to create value, (2.3) encouraging entrepreneurs to upgrade OTOP goods while fostering networks of community enterprises, SMEs, and the industrial sector, and (2.4) promoting business matching between community enterprises, SMEs and the business sector to create business opportunities.",""],[1,"218","2","Support for Local Small-Scale Consumer Goods Producers to Export via the East-West Economic Corridor","Supporting local small-scale producers of consumer goods along the East-West Economic Corridor (EWEC), namely Chaiyaphum, Khon Kaen, Kalasin, Roi-Et, and Mukdahan Provinces to export to neighboring countries by: (3.1) supporting green industries, and (3.2) utilizing local raw materials.",""],[1,"219","5","Green Industrial Base Upgrading for the Central Region","To strengthen the competitiveness of the existing industrial bases and promoting future industrial development as a new income source by upgrading the industrial economic base of Central Region to become the leading green industrial center of Southeast Asia:",""],[1,"219","6","Industrial Cluster Upgrading and Investment Promotion in Eastern Provinces","Developing and upgrading the industrial clusters in Pathumthani, Ayutthaya, Chachoengsao, Prachinburi, Chonburi, and Rayong to become the production base for high-tech and future industries, such as automotive and auto- parts, electronic, electrical, and telecommunication appliances, and environmentally-friendly chemical and petrochemical industrial clusters, by improving endorsement measures regarding investment privileges, human and technological development, infrastructure development, rules and regulations amendment, and provision of financial support in order to attract investments in the target areas.",""],[1,"219","7","Industrial Processing Center Development for Livestock, Agro-Products, and Textiles","Developing Kanchanaburi, Ratchaburi and Upper Phetchaburi to be industrial processing centers of livestock and agro-products, as well as centers for the textile and garment industries linking with production sources in Myanmar by improving logistics systems to reduce transportation costs while upgrading the",""],[1,"220","3","Food Production Efficiency and Value-Adding Upgrade","Improving the efficiency of food production in Chainat, Singburi, Angthong, Ayuthaya, Suphanburi, Chachoengsao, Ratchaburi and Prachuapkhirikhan, which are production bases of rice, vegetable, coconut, and freshwater fisheries, to become the major food exporting base and meet the needs of customers in niche and high-end markets by: (1.1) focusing on value-adding processes, and (1.2) restoring coconut plantation areas.",""],[1,"220","4","Fruit Export Production and Trading Base Development","Developing the fruit-trading business in eastern Rayong, Chanthaburi, Nakhonnayok, Prachinburi, and Chachoengsao to be the production and trading bases for fruit exports by improving productivity and quality control in the processes of production, packaging, processing, and trading.",""],[1,"232","6","Upgrading Production Processes and Agro-Processing to Meet Standards and Safety Project","Upgrading Production Processes and Agro-Processing to Meet Standards and Safety Project:",""]],"137":[[1,"216","3","Watershed Forest Rehabilitation and Conservation Programme","Rehabilitating and conserving watershed forests in 8 provinces of the Upper Northern Region by: restoring the degraded watershed forests to improve water storage capability in each watershed area, alongside with preventing forest encroachment and promoting reforestation in watershed forests.",""],[1,"219","4","Upstream Forest Rehabilitation and Biodiversity Conservation","To rehabilitate forestry resources and conserve biodiversity in upstream areas of Loei, Udon Thani, Sakon Nakhon, Chaiyaphum and Nakhon Ratchasima by: (1) identifying distinctive demarcation of the natural conservation forest areas, (2) encouraging local communities to take part in forest rehabilitation, reforestation, and forest encroachment prevention in order to protect upstream areas and avoid soil erosion, and (3) promoting wetland conservation and supporting the sustainable utilization of community forests.",""],[1,"231","11","Community Reforestation and Participatory Resource Management","promoting reforestation and encouraging participatory resources management in local communities.",""],[1,"246","2","Core Environment Program and Biodiversity Conservation Corridors Initiative Phase III","The Core Environment Program and Biodiversity Conservation Corridors Initiative Phase III (2017-2021).",""]],"138":[[1,"216","5","Upper Northern Smog Mitigation Measures","Solving smog problems in the Upper Northern Region and Tak Province by: (3.1) shifting from monoculture to agroforestry systems, (3.2) organizing the burning cycle in agricultural areas by identifying suitable burning periods (before the critical smog problem period), (3.3) utilizing agricultural residues to make organic fertilizer or fuel briquettes, and (3.4) enhancing stakeholder participation among the public sector, private sectors, local people, and local governments in preventing and mitigating smog problems.",""],[1,"231","4","Managing Agricultural By-Products for Smog Reduction Project","Managing Agricultural By-Products for Protecting the Smog Problem in the Northern Region Project:",""],[1,"231","5","Agricultural By-Products Management System","developing a system for managing agricultural by- products efficiently to protect the smog problem in the Northern Region, and which farmers can adapt to their existing practices for income-generation.",""]],"139":[[1,"224","5","Environmental Law Enforcement and Coastal Zone Planning","Enforcing environmental laws and urban planning, especially in the control of activities in coastal areas to minimize impacts on coastal erosion in the long run.",""],[1,"224","13","Comprehensive Waste Management Improvement Guidelines","Employing comprehensive waste management guidelines to improve waste collection, waste separation, recycling processes, and establish joint communal waste management facilities.",""],[1,"227","8","Environmental Law Monitoring and Enforcement for Factories","Meticulously and continuously monitor the implementation and enforcement of environmental laws, rules, and regulation concerning factories.",""],[1,"227","9","Participatory Environmental Monitoring","Empower local governments, educational institutions, and people to take part in the environmental monitoring process.",""],[1,"227","10","Interconnected Environmental Data and Monitoring System","Develop an interconnected environmental data and monitoring system to be efficient and transparent in order to create trust and diminish conflict between the industrial sector and local communities.",""],[1,"228","2","Industrial Estate Expansion for Environmental Impact Control","Promote industrial area expansion as industrial estate development to control environmental impacts.",""],[1,"229","12","Participatory Natural Resource and Environmental Management in Special Economic Zones","To include participatory processes in the management of natural resources and the environment in the special economic zones:",""],[1,"229","13","Natural Resource Conservation and Environmental Rehabilitation","Conserve and rehabilitate natural resources and the environment through efficient resource utilization.",""],[1,"230","1","Solid Waste Management through 3Rs and Communal Waste Centers","Solve solid waste problems by applying the 3Rs concept (Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle) and establishing communal waste management centers.",""],[1,"230","2","Special Economic Zone Impact Control Measures","Create measures to control negative impacts from activities operating within the special economic zones.",""],[1,"230","7","Rayong Pollution Reduction and Elimination Action Plan","Pollution Reduction and Elimination Action Plan in Rayong's Pollution Control Area, 2017-2021",""],[1,"230","8","Border Special Economic Zone Natural Resources and Environment Management Plan","Natural Resources and Environment Management Plan",""],[1,"235","8","Volatile Organic Compounds Monitoring and Mitigation Project","The Volatile Organic Compounds (VOCs) Monitoring and Mitigation Project in Map Ta Phut and Surrounding Areas in Rayong Province:",""]],"140":[[1,"223","9","Stakeholder Participation in Security and Safety Planning","Promoting the participation process to include all stakeholders in the conduct of security and safety plans to create confidence among international and domestic investors.",""],[1,"230","3","Border Area Public Health Service System Integration","Improve the public health service system in the border areas to be efficient and integrated with the border crossing system, health insurance system, and alien labor system.",""],[1,"230","4","Labor One-Stop Service Center","Organize a complete One-Stop-Service-Center for labor with the ability to provide services regarding border crossing documents, electronic identification, and a fingerprints system which link to the central database.",""],[1,"230","5","Area Security Measures and Communication Systems","Create security measures and communication systems in the area.",""]],"141":[[1,"257","5","Private Sector Development Partnership Integration","Encourage the private sector to integrate important development issues when they formulate their business investment plans.",""],[1,"258","5","Plan Implementation Coordination and Partner Linkage Mechanism","The NESDB is responsible for creating understanding and connecting development partners with the plan implementation committees at all levels so that they are able concretely to translate the Plan into action as follows:",""],[1,"259","1","National Committee Coordination for Twelfth Plan Implementation","Link national committees in order to use the strategies under the Twelfth Plan as guidelines for implementation.",""],[1,"259","4","Civil State Coordination Approach","Encourage a \"Civil State\" approach as one of the ways of vigorously driving the Twelfth Plan into action.",""],[1,"260","4","Citizen-Local Authority-Academic Cooperation Mechanism","Cooperation among citizens, LAOs, and local academic institutions should be encouraged.",""],[1,"261","2","Private Sector Social Development Partnerships","The private sector should form alliances with communities, non-governmental organizations (NGOs) and academic institutions to bring about collaboration in social activities.",""],[1,"261","5","Regional Public Agency Coordination Reform","Amending the roles of government personnel and their work methods to accommodate the overall development efforts and encourage regional public agencies to be coordinators for connecting other sectors at the local level.",""],[1,"261","5","Provincial Development Partnership Coordination","Provincial organizations should join development partners in efforts to work towards the common goals, fulfill national strategies, solve problems and increase performance at the local and community levels.",""],[1,"261","6","International Knowledge-Sharing Forums","International forums to share knowledge should be organized, especially for countries involved in regional and sub-regional cooperation.",""]],"142":[[1,"257","3","Cabinet and Parliament Approval of Development Implementation and Monitoring Guidelines","the guidelines used to realize programs and projects and to monitor and evaluate national development at all levels should be approved by the Cabinet and Parliament.",""],[1,"258","2","Regulatory Amendment Package for Plan Implementation","Amend regulations to enable efficient execution of the Plan at every level.",""],[1,"259","2","Public Administration Mechanism Review and Streamlining","The mechanisms needed to review and evaluate development performance, including committees, agencies, and public organizations, will be revised and evaluated to increase their flexibility and reduce redundancy.",""]],"143":[[1,"260","4","Community Empowerment and Local Adaptation Support","Communities should be strengthened through information.",""],[1,"260","4","Local Research Networks and Knowledge Sharing Initiative","Their ability to manage affairs, and to benefit from knowledge from outside sources through local research networks should be supported.",""],[1,"260","5","Local Administrative Organization Capacity Strengthening","In order to perform their duties efficiently, the capabilities of LAOs should be enhanced and their administration simplified and made more flexible.",""],[1,"260","6","Community Development Participation by Regional Universities and Vocational Institutions","Encouraging regional universities and vocational institutions to participate in community development.",""],[1,"261","1","Technological Skills Training for Local Development","Vocational institutions should provide technological skills training to assist local development.",""],[1,"261","3","Constructive Media Messaging Promotion","The media should present information that promotes benefits for society, be impartial, deliver accurate information and reflect the needs of the people.",""]],"144":[[1,"257","7","Research and Development for National and Area-Based Development","Policy-level government agencies will work cooperatively and utilize research and development (R&D) to accommodate national and area-based developments.",""],[1,"261","6","Technical and Innovation Cooperation Promotion","Cooperation in the technical and innovative sectors should be encouraged to support both domestic and international growth.",""]]}});